PVD("vietnam_ndp_2006-2010",{"docs":["","VN NDP 2006 2010"],"s":{"1":[[1,"140","7","Central-Local Decentralization Reform","Readjust regulations on central-local decentralization and decentralization among different levels of local authorities in order to improve their powers and responsibilities.",""],[1,"140","7","Inspection of Administrative Managers and Agency Heads","Also intensify inspection of the performance of managers and heads of administrative agencies at all levels.",""],[1,"140","8","Local Government Structure Readjustment","Readjust the local government structure in accordance with the changes in the central government in the direction of reducing focal points and strengthening the role of guiding, checking and supervision of professional agencies under People's Committees.",""],[1,"140","8","Reduction of People's Councils Scope and Functions","Study and reduce the scope, function and tasks of People's Councils at district and ward levels in urban areas, and those at district level in rural areas.",""],[1,"143","7","State Economic Management Decentralization Reform","Push up decentralization of the State's economic management: eliminate tasks that the central State does not necessarily have to implement or manage directly.",""]],"2":[[1,"7","7","Flexible Monetary Policy and Exchange Rate Reform","Develop and operate flexible monetary policies to ensure the macro economic stabilization, control inflation, to ensure the safety of the banking system and strengthen credit quality.",""],[1,"7","7","Investment Capital Mobilization for Economic Reform","Mobilizing resources in cooperation with reform to increase economy's ability of capital supply for investment.",""],[1,"7","7","Non-Cash Payment Reform and Currency Convertibility Improvement","reform payment methods with using more non-cash methods, improving the convertibility of Vietnamese currency.",""],[1,"26","1","Interest Rate Liberalization","Interest rates continued to be liberalized, creating favorable conditions for banks to actively adjust mobilized capital and loan interest rate to suit international interest rate fluctuation as well as domestic financial changes.",""],[1,"82","4","Financial Sector Legal and Regulatory Framework Reform","In the two years of 2006-2007, build and complete the legal framework in line with the roadmap of integration and market opening commitments, ensure a fair, unified and stable mechanism and financial policy system applicable to all economic sectors.",""],[1,"82","4","Commercial Banking Liberalization and State Bank Deregulation","Gradually abolish all preferences enjoyed by State-owned commercial banks, while stop the interference of the State Bank into the business of commercial banks.",""],[1,"82","4","Banking Services Expansion and Modernization Programme","Boost the development of banking services, including extended deposit and loan services, modernizing the electronic transaction system, investing more into the inter-bank and credit card transaction system, and introducing some new services.",""],[1,"82","4","Financial Services Diversification and Market Participation Expansion","Increase the quantity and quality, diversify financial services, and increase their percentage in the service structure.",""],[1,"82","4","Financial and Banking Service Market Opening","Attract the participation of all economic sectors into the financial and banking service market.",""],[1,"82","4","Financial Sector Service Culture Modernization","Reform the communicative manner in the financial and banking system so that they can be truly civilized, modern and polite.",""],[1,"134","5","Monetary Policy Stabilization and Currency Convertibility Reform","The objectives of monetary policies over the next five years are to control inflation and to ensure the safety of the banking system and the credit organizations with a view to stabilizing the macroeconomy and contributing to the economic growth.",""],[1,"134","7","Vietnamese Currency Convertibility Improvement","improve the convertibility of Vietnamese currency within the country and prepare conditions for its gradually improved convertibility in the world market.",""],[1,"134","8","Market-Based Monetary Policy Development","Develop and realize monetary policies in accordance with market principles and fully realize international norms and practices in banking activities.",""],[1,"134","8","Negotiable Interest Rate Policy Implementation","Continue the implementation of negotiable interest rate policies according to market principles.",""],[1,"134","9","Reduce State Bank Intervention in Commercial Banking Operations","Reduce the direct intervention of State banks in the operation of commercial banks.",""],[1,"134","9","Interest Rate-Based Monetary Policy Framework","Manage monetary policies based on the regulation of supplied money amount, while creating necessary conditions to move to the implementation of governing monetary policies on the basis of regulating interest rates; prime interest rates, capital replenishment interest rates and re-amortization interest rates of the State Bank are used to direct and regulate market interest rates.",""],[1,"134","10","Flexible Exchange Rate Policy and De-dollarization Measures","Continue carrying out flexible exchange rate policies with an enlarged range in conformity with the openness of the financial market and controllability by the State Bank.","State Bank"],[1,"134","10","Restriction on Foreign Currency Use for Payments","Narrow the scope of using foreign currencies as payment modes in Vietnam with a view to gradually lessening the 'dollarization'.",""],[1,"135","6","Economic Forecasting and Price Stabilization Measures","Improve quality and effectiveness of economic forecasts and analysis; strengthen measures to manage and control market fluctuation and prices and effectively handle the issue of price-salary-money.",""],[1,"135","6","Measures to Address World Market and Input Price Shocks","It is important to take initiatives in dealing with negative impacts of price fluctuation in the world market and input prices to meet the demand of integration, inflation control, stabilizing business environment and development of domestic production.",""],[1,"135","7","Inflation Control and Exchange Rate Management Measures","To control inflation, banking instruments are essential together with flexible exchange rate policy; interest rates should be managed as to encourage export and reduce trade deficit, improving investment effectiveness in economic activities.",""],[1,"135","7","Market Information and Domestic Distribution System Strengthening","the trade sector needs to establish a good market information system and ensure close relationship between the state, associations and businesses to help deal with complicated changes of the market; consolidate good distribution system in the domestic market; enhance control of export and import to regulate supply and demand of commodities, stabilize prices of essential goods for production and the people's life.",""],[1,"135","7","Price Violation Enforcement Measures","The government should introduce strict measures to punish violations of prices to prevent any monopoly linkage and unhealthy competition behaviors in regard to prices.",""]],"3":[[1,"132","7","Financial Market and Stock Market Regulatory Improvement","Continue to perfect policies and State management mechanism over the financial market in order that the financial market as well as the stock market can develop in a rapid and safe manner",""],[1,"134","6","Banking System Non-Performing Debt Reduction","Rapidly reduce the proportion of overdue debts of the banking systems to an average level of the countries in the region by 2010.",""],[1,"135","1","State Bank Monetary Policy and Supervision Reform","Improve responsibilities and powers of the State Bank in planning and realizing monetary policies.","State Bank"],[1,"135","2","Credit Organization Development and Banking Sector Reform","Develop credit organizations, reform and develop Vietnam commercial bank system with diverse forms of ownership and organization; introduce the international practices and standards on banking administration.",""],[1,"135","2","Strengthening State Commercial Banks","Bring into play the core role of State commercial banks while ensuring self-control, self-responsibility and healthy competition in the whole system under the Law.",""],[1,"135","2","People's Credit Fund Development and Quality Improvement","Develop and improve the quality of people's credit funds in order for them to become credit organizations working on principles of voluntary, self-control, and self-responsibility for their operational results.",""],[1,"135","2","Development of Non-Banking Financial Institutions","Encourage the development of non- banking financial institutions such as securities firms, finance companies, insurance companies, financial leasing companies, etc., to better serve the economy.",""],[1,"135","3","Financial Inclusion and Non-Cash Payment Expansion","Facilitate people and enterprises in their access to banking services; then rapidly spread out forms of non-cash payment and payment through banks.",""],[1,"135","4","Liberalization of Banking Services Market","Ensure the rights to business of foreign banks and financial institutions pursuant to international commitments.",""],[1,"135","5","Commercial Bank Restructuring and Capital Strengthening","Strengthen the financial capacity of commercial banks, strive for the fundamental accomplishment of the plan of restructuring commercial banks approved by the Government.",""],[1,"135","5","Banking Legal and Regulatory Framework Reform","By the year 2010, establish a comprehensive legal framework; fully apply international standards and norms on safety to financial and banking businesses.",""]],"4":[[1,"6","14","Infrastructure Development Breakthrough","make a breakthrough in building infrastructure",""],[1,"74","2","Industrial Production and Economic Infrastructure Development","Push up development of energy production industries, and important material production industries; attention should be paid to labor-used industries; and push up development of economic infrastructure for industrialization and modernization.",""]],"5":[[1,"37","2","ODA Harmonization and Aid Effectiveness Coordination","Vietnam and the donors have put forward initiatives to harmonize procedures and processes; aligning the donors' strategies to Vietnam's national development priorities to gradually reduce transaction costs in supply and implementation of ODA funds and improvement of its effectiveness.",""],[1,"40","3","ODA-Financed Socio-Economic Infrastructure Development","ODA funds are preferentially spent on assisting the development of socio-economic infrastructures, contributing to economic growth and hunger eradication and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"40","3","ODA-Supported Legal and Administrative Reform Programme","ODA funds have contributed to enhancing capacity and institution through programs and projects that assist the legal and administrative reforms, work out economic management policies in line with the roadmap of integration into the world economy, and enhance the human resource's quality.",""],[1,"40","3","ODA Technical Assistance and Capacity-Building Programme","Through many ODA projects and technical assistance, many Vietnamese cadres have been trained and retrained to improve their professional skills; many advanced production technologies and modern management skills have been transferred.",""]],"6":[[1,"147","13","Natural Disaster Prevention and Mitigation Strategy","Build a strategy for prevention and mitigation of natural disasters.",""]],"7":[[1,"72","2","Afforestation and Forest Protection in Watershed and Coastal Areas","Focus on afforestation and protection of forests in the watershed area of major hydropower plant reservoirs and costal prevention forests.",""],[1,"72","2","Special-Use Forest Protection","Protect forests for special use purpose.",""],[1,"72","2","Production Forest Plantation and Value Chain Development","Plant forests for production linked with processing and sale of products to meet the demand of providing materials for the economy and generate income for the forest farmer",""],[1,"72","3","Forest Master Plan Review","Review the master plans of three kinds of forests.",""],[1,"73","8","Multi-purpose Afforestation Project Enhancement","Review, amend, supplement policies and solutions in order to improve the effectiveness of the Project of planting 5 million hectares of forests in the orientation of multi-purpose afforestation, both for wood and for protection of the ecological environment.",""],[1,"73","8","Land and Forest Allocation Completion","Complete land allocation and forest allocation mainly for people and other economic sectors.",""],[1,"111","1","Natural and Protection Forest Conservation","Properly protect natural forests and protection forests.",""],[1,"111","1","Planted Forest Expansion for Raw Materials","Expand planted forests, especially forests supplying raw materials for paper industry as planned.",""],[1,"112","6","Tree Planting and Forest Protection Programme","intensify tree planting on bare lands and hills, maintain protection forests, and watershed protection forests to protect water sources for the downstream regions",""],[1,"112","6","Environmental Protection in Mineral Mining Areas","Pay attention to environmental protection in mineral mining areas",""],[1,"127","4","Protection and Production Forest Development and Erosion Control","Give emphasis on development of protection and production forests, deal with the situation of erosion and water draining.",""],[1,"146","7","Tree Planting and Urban Greening Programme","Plant trees and vegetation on bare land, hills and mountains, increasing forest coverage up to over 42-43% in 2010, and increasing green spaces in urban areas;",""]],"8":[[1,"8","6","Environmental Protection and Pollution Control Strengthening","Harmoniously combine socio- economic development with effective and appropriate use of natural resources, protecting environment; significantly tackle the environmental degradation in industrial zones, densely-populated areas in major cities; raise the State's management efficiency in environment protection.",""],[1,"67","18","Clean Technology and Pollution Minimization Compliance Programme","Strive for 100% of Level-1, 2 and 3 cities, 50% of Level-4 cities and all newly built production establishments to apply clean technology or equipped with pollution minimization facilities, ensure waste treatment and 50% of production and business establishment satisfy environmental standards.",""],[1,"77","3","Plastic Industry Development and Eco-Friendly Product Promotion","Plastic industry: Satisfy demands for plastic packages and accessories for industry and daily life.",""],[1,"104","7","Strengthening Environmental Administration Capacity","Complete and strengthen operation capacity of the state administration agency involved in baseline study and environmental protection from central to local levels.",""],[1,"104","7","Decentralization of Natural Resources and Minerals Administration","Identify clearly decentralized functions of state administration of natural resources and minerals among sectors and levels of authority.",""],[1,"105","5","Environmental Pollution Reduction and Remediation Programme","Minimize the pollution level, overcome the degradation and improve the environmental quality; significantly tackle the environmental degradation in industrial zones, densely- populated areas in major cities, craft villages, and some rural areas; improve environment and treat environmental pollution in rivers, lakes, ponds, canals and ditches.",""],[1,"105","6","Natural Disaster Prevention and Environmental Incident Response","Improve the prevention capacity and mitigate averse effects of natural disasters and negative climate changes on the environment; provide effective support and resolution of environmental incidence caused by natural disasters.",""],[1,"105","6","Sustainable Natural Resource Management and Biodiversity Conservation","Manage exploitation and utilization of natural resources, especially soil, water, forests and scarce minerals; ensure a high level of eco-balance; preserve the nature and biodiversity.",""],[1,"105","7","Industrial and Urban Pollution Control and Environmental Sanitation Programme","Tackle the environmental pollution in industrial zones and villages and cities as well as ensure rural environmental sanitation in highly populated areas.",""],[1,"105","9","Remediation of Dioxide-Contaminated Areas","Fundamentally tackle the issues in dioxide-contaminated spots.",""],[1,"105","9","Catchment Water Quality Improvement for Agriculture and Aquaculture","Make sure that water in the catchments areas meet the standards to serve agricultural production and aquaculture.",""],[1,"105","10","Forest Coverage Expansion and Restoration Programme","Increase the forest coverage to 42-43% of the total natural land area, restore 50% of degraded upstream forests and improve the forest quality, promoting tree planting among the people.",""],[1,"105","10","Natural Preservation Parks Expansion and Protection Initiative","Increase the total area of natural preservation parks to 11.2% of the total natural land area, especially marine and wetland protection.",""],[1,"105","11","Environmental Research and Forecasting Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen scientific study on environment, study and forecast environmental trends in the international economic integration, study national and international environmental changes.",""],[1,"106","2","Mainstream Environmental Protection into Development Planning","Mainstream environmental protection into socio-economic development plans to achieve the sustainable development goals of the country.",""],[1,"106","2","Environmental Protection Planning Renewal","Renew the planning work in regard to environmental protection.",""],[1,"106","3","Environmental Protection Awareness and Training Programme","Improve awareness of environmental protection: enhance education and communication for the whole society to be aware of and responsible for environmental protection, seeing this as the whole society's responsibility.",""],[1,"106","4","Environmental Protection Investment Diversification","Diversify investment in environmental protection.",""],[1,"106","4","Environmental Protection Socialization Initiative","Promote socialization in environmental protection.",""],[1,"106","4","Economic Instruments for Environmental Protection","Attention is to be paid to develop and apply economic instruments to increase the fund.",""],[1,"106","4","Environmental Pollution Treatment Facilities Support","Assist organizations to establish environmental pollution treatment facilities, treatment of waste substances and water ...",""],[1,"106","5","Environmental Protection Policy and Legal Framework Reform","Complete the policy and legal system for environmental protection; review and revise legal documents on environmental management.",""],[1,"106","5","Environmental Standards and Sustainable Development Indicators Promulgation","Continue to promulgate legal documents on environmental standards and sustainable development indicators.",""],[1,"106","6","Pollution Treatment Technology Transfer and Environmental Industry Development","Study, apply and transfer technological solutions of pollution treatment.",""],[1,"106","6","Clean Technology Adoption for Businesses","Encourage businesses to apply advanced and clean technology to reduce emission into the environment.",""],[1,"106","7","Human Resources Training for Environmental Protection Work","Strengthen training of human resources in universities, colleges and institutes to meed the human resources demand for baseline study and environmental protection work.",""],[1,"106","8","Physical and Technical Infrastructure Development","Develop physical and technical infrastructure.",""],[1,"106","8","Environmental Protection Socialization and Resource Mobilization","Promote the \"socialization\" policy to invest in environmental protection, mobilizing resources from businesses, organizations, NGOs and the whole society to fulfill the tasks of management and treatment of pollution and environmental sanitation.",""],[1,"106","9","Environmental Administration Capacity Building","Enhance the capacity for state environmental administration agencies at all levels, provide professional training for staff involved in environmental protection at all levels; establish environmental management organizations in ministries and sectors.",""],[1,"106","9","Environmental Policy Study, Inspection, and Monitoring Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of policy study, control, inspection and monitoring as well as physical infrastructure for effective environmental management.",""],[1,"106","10","International Environmental Cooperation and Pollution Control","Strengthen international cooperation, actively participate in international and regional environmental activities, fulfill international commitments, especially those with regional countries on management, control and treatment of environmental pollution.",""],[1,"146","8","Clean Technology Adoption and Pollution Control in Production Establishments","Gradually apply clean technologies to social and economic sectors; by 2010 strive to reach 100% of new business and production establishments to apply clean technologies or be equipped with pollution minimization facilities, ensuring waste treatment to reach environmental standards; 50% of production establishments satisfy environmental standards;",""]],"9":[[1,"8","3","Education and Vocational Training Reform and Investment Programme","Continue the systematic and comprehensive reform.",""],[1,"18","9","Human Resource Development through Education, Training, Science and Technology","create a substantial change in human resource development with emphasis placed on education and training, science and technology;",""],[1,"41","8","Education and Training Quality Improvement Investments","focal investments have been made in the implementation of the Central Resolution No.2 to create changes in education, enhancing the quality of human resource training, skilled worker training; in leading universities, regional universities, and vocational training colleges.",""],[1,"45","2","Expansion of Higher and Vocational Education Capacity","The size and training courses of university, college, technical and vocational schools have been extending.",""],[1,"45","2","Accelerated Recruitment into Technical and Vocational Training","Recruitment structures of every level are adapted to quickly recruit more students into technical and vocational training institutions.",""],[1,"45","3","University Network Expansion in Underserved Regions","University network planning has been proactively implemented57.",""],[1,"45","3","Teacher Training University System Consolidation","The teacher training university system from central to local level is continuously consolidated, enhanced in order to meet the needs of lower secondary education universalization and the implementation of new curricula for upper secondary education in the upcoming years.",""],[1,"45","8","National and Regional University Reorganization and Upgrading","Two national universities are reorganized; 3 regional universities (Thai Nguyen, Thua Thien-Hue, Da Nang) continue to be upgraded and developed; key universities of teacher training, technology, agriculture, and economics are enhanced.",""],[1,"66","3","Science, Technology, Education, and Training Development Initiative","Fourth, strongly develop science and technology, education and training, improve the quality of the human resources for the sake of the national industrialization and modernization, and enhance the development of knowledge economy.",""]],"10":[[1,"86","8","University and Technical Education Expansion","Enhance forms of university and technical education: enrollment into universities and colleges is targeted to increase by 10.3% annually with 200 students/10,000 people by 2010, enrollment into professional high schools to increase by 14.7%; train about 7.5 million workers, 25% of whom enjoy long-term training; ensure an annual 17% increase of new long-term training enrollment.",""],[1,"87","2","Training System Completion and Education Diversification Reform","Complete the training systems that allow interchanges and transfers, offering more studying opportunities to the youth.",""],[1,"87","2","Modernized and Flexible Education System Development","Promote the strengths of the current training programs, adopt relevant international programs to build a diversified, flexible, advanced and modern education system with good linkages between training levels.",""],[1,"87","10","Vocational Training Unit Development and Reform","Give priority to investment in the development of vocational training units with 3 levels (vocational primary, vocational secondary and vocational college); renovate the methods of teaching and learning in order to improve vocational training quality.",""],[1,"87","10","Preferential Support for Vocational Training Investment","Create a level playing field among vocational training units of all economic sectors; work out preferential policies on land, infrastructure support, capital borrowing, etc., with an aim to mobilizing all economic sectors to invest in vocational training, human resource development for the sake of national industrialization, modernization and international economic integration.",""],[1,"87","11","Private and Foreign-Invested Education and Training Institution Development","Encourage the establishment of private education, training and vocational training institutions; encourage training cooperation with high-quality foreign training institutions; foster the opening of high quality, accredited and 100% foreign-invested training institutions",""],[1,"88","1","Foreign Expert and Diaspora Teaching Initiative","Encourage foreign scientific and educational experts and overseas Vietnamese expatriates to teach in Vietnam.",""],[1,"88","2","Distance and Continuing Education Quality Upgrade","Strengthen, develop and upgrade the quality of distant education, continued education centers and community learning centers to meet the requirements for regular study of people of all levels and ages everywhere.",""],[1,"88","3","School Facility Standardization Program","Continue the implementation of the Program of \"concretizing schools and classrooms\" in association with the standardization of facilities;",""],[1,"88","3","University and Vocational Facilities Modernization Investment","Diversify investment sources to modernize facilities and dormitories at universities, colleges, technical and vocational schools.",""],[1,"88","3","Key University Construction Investment Program","Concentrate investment in the construction of 14 key universities; basically complete the first stage of investment in the construction of two national universities and 2 key teacher training universities by 2010.",""],[1,"88","3","International-Standard University Development Study","Study the way to develop Vietnam's universities of international standards.",""],[1,"88","7","Teacher Training and Staffing Improvement Program","Develop, improve the quality of the teaching staffs and educational management officials under the Directive 40-CT/TW of the Party's Secretariats.",""],[1,"88","7","Pedagogical School Teacher Training Reform","Renovate teacher training work at pedagogical schools.",""],[1,"88","7","Teacher Shortage Reduction Program","Implement the teacher training program to solve teacher shortage, improve teaching quality and eliminate structural imbalance.",""],[1,"120","6","School Upgrading and New Higher Education Institutions","Upgrade schools and establish new universities and colleges.",""],[1,"120","7","Vocational Training Expansion for Rural Laborers","Strongly develop vocational training, particulary to rural laborers, in association with crop and livestock substitution in order to create local jobs and contribute to agricultural and rural labor structural transformation;",""],[1,"120","7","Vocational Training Institution Development Investment","invest in the development of vocational training institutions;",""],[1,"120","7","Standardized Vocational Secondary Schools and Colleges Establishment","establish 9 standardized vocational secondary schools and colleges;",""],[1,"120","7","Vinh Long Technical Teachers Training College Upgrade","upgrade Vinh Long Technical Teachers Training College into University of Technical Pedagogy;",""],[1,"120","7","Technical Teacher Training Assignment for Vocational Colleges","assign the province's two vocational colleges with the task of training technical teachers.",""],[1,"126","4","National and Regional University Construction Investment","Focus on investments in the construction of national universities, focal universities and regional universities.",""],[1,"126","4","Vocational Institutions Investment Mobilization","Attract domestic investment capital, including investments from foreign-owned corporations and companies, and external investments to improve the system of vocational institutions.",""],[1,"126","5","Higher Education and Vocational Facilities Upgrade Investment","Focus on in-depth investments to upgrade and provide facilities for universities, colleges and vocational secondary institutions.",""],[1,"126","5","University and Technical Laboratory Modernization","Invest in the modernization of laboratory facilities in important universities and technical training institutions.",""],[1,"126","5","New Learning and Educational Facilities Provision","Invest in the provision of new learning and educational facilities to improve quality.",""],[1,"126","5","Student Dormitory Construction Programme","Build new dormitories for students.",""],[1,"126","5","Support for Non-Public School Investment","Support investments in non-public schools.",""],[1,"126","6","University Construction in Underserved Regions","Build new universities in Northern mountainous area, the Central Highland and the Mekong Delta such as the Northwest University, the West Cultural University, accelerate the construction of Can Tho Medical and Pharmaceutical University.",""],[1,"126","7","Education Bond Financing for School Infrastructure","Continue to issue education bonds to invest in building decent secondary schools; expand classroom areas in primary schools so that pupils can have full-day schooling.",""]],"11":[[1,"8","6","Science and Technology Capacity and Management Reform","Improve science and technology capacity, renovate the management mechanism and organization of science and technology activities.",""],[1,"8","6","Advanced and Traditional Technology Modernization Programme","Develop advanced technologies and modernize traditional technologies to accelerate technological innovation in all economic sectors.",""],[1,"8","6","Information Technology and Biotechnology Development Initiative","Gradually develop information technology and bio-technology to become key sectors with a fast growth rate and which increasingly satisfy domestic demands and contribute to an increase in export revenue.",""],[1,"46","5","Applied Science and Technology for Socio-Economic Development","Science and technology concentrate more on applied research to better serve the requirements of socio-economic development.",""],[1,"46","5","Technology Application for Domestic Production and Exports","A large number of research results in biotechnology, mechanical engineering, automation technology, and information technology are applied to production in order to increase quality and types of domestic consumer goods, increase export and substitute imported ones.",""],[1,"47","1","Equipment Improvement and Upgrade Programme","equipment improvement and upgrade; some key laboratories and two high-tech zones are being built59.",""],[1,"47","2","Enterprise Technology Transfer Strengthening","Technological transfer in enterprises, especially FDI enterprises and State-owned industrial enterprises, is strengthened to improve the effectiveness and competitiveness of many products and services.",""],[1,"47","3","Science and Technology Policy and Governance Reform","Reforms in policies and governance as well as improvement of legislation on science and technology undergo several changes in such a way that the effectiveness of State management of science and technology is enhanced, and encouragement is provided to scientific, technological activities and innovation.",""],[1,"60","4","Science and Technology Market Development","Science and technology market is established and gradually developed through the organization of equipments and technology fairs nationwide, together with services, software production and supply, technology transfer to enterprises, and legal and managerial consultancy activities.",""],[1,"60","4","Linkage Between Research Institutions and Producers","Scientific and technological research institutions and scientists install closer linkages with producers and manufacturers, and receive research orders to create initial supply-demand relations in a number of scientific and technological activities.",""],[1,"78","5","Automation and Novel Materials Master Plan Development","develop the master plan on automation and novel material technology of the 2006 - 2010 period to authorities for appraisal and approval.",""],[1,"88","9","National Science and Technology Capacity Strengthening","Improve internal science and technology capacity and the reception, mastery and application of the advances in science and technology taking place in the world.",""],[1,"88","10","Science and Technology Management Reform","Renovate the management mechanism and organization of science and technology activities;",""],[1,"88","10","Research Application and Commercialization Promotion","create new developments with higher effectiveness in research and application of research results to production and business",""],[1,"89","3","Science and Technology Management Mechanism Reform","Fundamentally renovate the management mechanism in science and technology, especially the financial mechanism to increase autonomy, self-responsibility in line with their creativeness as well as risks in scientific and technological activities.",""],[1,"89","3","Competitive Selection and Direct Assignment Mechanism for Science and Technology Tasks","Rationally combine selection mechanism through bidding for the implementation of scientific and technological tasks with the mechanism of direct task assignment on the basis of competitiveness, effectiveness and quality assurance principles.",""],[1,"89","3","Autonomy and Self-Responsibility Regime for Public Science and Technology Institutions","Implement the mechanism of autonomy and self-responsibility in all public science and technology institutions.",""],[1,"89","3","Transformation of Applied Research and Technological Development Institutions into Enterprises","Transform institutions of applied research and technological development into an appropriate form of enterprises.",""],[1,"89","3","Development of Science and Technology Enterprises","Strongly develop science and technology enterprises.",""],[1,"89","3","Science and Technology Development Fund System","Establish and put into effective operation the system of foundations for science and technology development at all levels.",""],[1,"89","3","High-Tech Research and Development Risk Investment Fund","Establish a 'Risk investment fund' for high-tech research and development.",""],[1,"89","4","Science and Technology Market Development Support Scheme","Accelerate the development of science and technology markets through initial support schemes by organizing technology and equipment fairs, different forms of consultancy, brokerage, and technology transfer services.",""],[1,"89","4","Science and Technology Transaction Centers Network","Establish and develop science and technology transaction centers in all key economic areas of the country.",""],[1,"89","4","Intellectual Property and Technology Transfer Law Enforcement","Effectively enforce the Law on Intellectual Property Right and the Law on Technology Transfer.",""],[1,"89","8","Science and Technology Human Resource Development Strategy","Develop strategies, policies for training and developing human resources in science and technology, utilizing and respecting talents in order to facilitate creativity, quickly increase the quantity and quality of inventions, technical innovations to better serve the requirements of the country's socio-economic development.",""],[1,"90","2","International Science and Technology Integration Strategy","Develop strategies for international scientific and technological integration, reducing the gap in science and technology between our country and the world to better serve the industrialization, modernization and international economic integration process.",""],[1,"90","2","Foreign Investment Promotion in Science and Technology","Encourage foreign organizations and individuals to invest in science and technology development in Vietnam.",""],[1,"90","2","Expatriate Expert Attraction Mechanism for Science and Technology","Install mechanism and policies to attract foreign expatriates, particularly talented experts among overseas Vietnamese into the country's science and technology development activities.",""],[1,"122","7","Human Resources Development Investment","Make investments in the development of human resources; build and maintain education facilities and improve secondary education system; gradually modernize tertiary education.",""],[1,"122","7","Education Facilities and Secondary Education Improvement","build and maintain education facilities and improve secondary education system; gradually modernize tertiary education.",""],[1,"122","7","Science and Technology Research Center Modernization","Make intensive and extensive investments in the modernization of research centers for science and technology.",""],[1,"125","7","Researcher and Scientist Support Investments","Make intensive investments to provide favorable conditions for researchers and scientists.",""],[1,"125","7","Information Collection and Analysis Equipment Investment","Invest in devices and equipment for collecting, analyzing, exploiting and disseminating information.",""],[1,"125","7","Breakthrough Policy Planning Investment","Make focal investment to create breakthrough development in each stage and period for policy-making and socio-economic development planning.",""],[1,"125","8","Targeted Investment in Research Institutions and High-Tech Facilities","Pool resources primarily for leading research institutions, 2 science centers, focal laboratories, high-tech areas, and software industry; Increase investments in centers for technology application and transfer towards the development of advantaged high-tech.",""],[1,"125","8","Renovation of Existing Research Facilities","Make some in-depth investment to renovate research facilities at existing research centers.",""],[1,"125","8","In-Depth Investment in Selected Institutes and Universities","Select 5-10 institutes, focal universities for in-depth investment to achieve regional standards, making significant changes in our research and technology.",""],[1,"125","9","Research Center Funding and High-Tech Industry Development","Provide adequate funding to research centers for major production sectors and services, increase the effectiveness and competitiveness of the economy; develop high-tech industry",""],[1,"126","3","High-Tech Zones, Internet Gateways, and National Laboratories Investment","Invest in high-tech zones in Hoa Lac and Ho Chi Minh City; open some Internet Gateways/Portals in big cities; build and put into operation 17 focal national laboratories.",""]],"12":[[1,"81","7","Science and Technology Services Development","Boost the development of science and technology services to effectively support the reform process, improve the technological level of economic sectors; rationalize production, foster the application of quality assurance and environment management in enterprises consistent to Vietnam's conditions, protect the intellectual right of any organizations, enterprises and individuals.",""],[1,"81","8","Market-Oriented Science and Technology Service Provision Reform","Strongly transform some non-productive scientific and technological activities into service provision mechanism in line with the market economy, including the evaluation, assessment, appraisal, information, consultancy and brokerage of technology transfer; study, design and implementation; legal counseling on intellectual property right; and services on standards, measurements and quality.",""],[1,"81","9","Private and Foreign Sector Participation in Science and Technology","Enlarge the participation of all economic sectors and foreign enterprises in scientific and technological activities.",""],[1,"82","1","Science and Technology Services Legal and Policy Framework","Complete the legal basis, mechanisms and policies to promote activities of science and technology services.",""],[1,"139","8","Science and Technology Market Development Measures","For the science and technology market: carry out preferential policies, recognize and grant patents to scientific inventions and creative activities; develop and apply new technologies.",""],[1,"139","8","Scientific and Technological Enterprise and Applied R&D Development","Establish scientific and technological enterprises, organizations specialized in applied research and development that operate according to enterprise principles.",""],[1,"139","8","Commercialization and Technology Transfer Promotion","Promote the commercialization of scientific-technological products.",""],[1,"139","8","Technology Trading and Research Linkage Mechanism","Create a convenient trading environment for technological products, link research activities with technological application, develop contractual relations between production enterprises and scientific- technological research establishments.",""],[1,"139","8","Venture Capital Investment in Research","Ensure venture capital investment in research,",""],[1,"140","1","Technology Transfer and Trading Support Services","Intensify assistance services for intellectual property ownership, consultancy, technology trading, appraisal, evaluation and transfer of technology.",""],[1,"140","1","Technology Markets and Intermediary Organizations","Establish intermediary organizations for technology trading, technology markets and technological nurseries.",""],[1,"140","2","Commercialization and Competitive Procurement Reform for R&D","Abolish monopoly in scientific and technological activities; substantially improve the bidding and ordering contract mechanism to select projects, research themes and research institutions; commercialize R&D activities.",""],[1,"140","2","Financial Self-Sufficiency Reform for Research Organizations","Change organizations for technological research and application into financially self- standing ones, like enterprises or companies.",""]],"13":[[1,"8","5","Mass Sports Participation and Sports Development Promotion","Encourage, mobilize and facilitate the involvement of all people in sports activities and sports development.",""],[1,"8","5","School, Military, and Security Unit Physical Training Promotion","Ensure favorable conditions to promote physical training at schools, army and security units; pay more attentions to popular sports, non-professional sports centered upon children and adolescents.",""],[1,"8","5","Professionalization of High-Performance Sports","Continue to implement and expand the professionalization of high-record sports.",""],[1,"97","7","School and Military Physical Fitness Training","Ensure all conditions to speed up physical health training in schools and military units; develop different types of public physical exercises and sports.",""],[1,"97","7","Youth Athlete Training and Sports Talent Development","Continue to renovate and intensify the training of young athletes who are capable enough to replace vacancies when necessary and to take part in SEA GAMES; and in international Olympic Games.",""],[1,"97","8","Nationwide Sports and Physical Training Promotion","Strive for healthy sport and physical training movement nationwide; expand international culture and sport exchanges.",""],[1,"97","8","Sports Development Expansion","Develop sport activities both in terms of quality and scale in order to improve physical and intellectual health and promoting national spirit of Vietnamese people.",""],[1,"97","10","Sports and Physical Training Facility Planning and Participation Incentive Policy","Develop planning for sports and physical training facility systems, implement incentive policies to encourage and create favorable conditions for all people to participate in the activities and development of sports and physical training.",""],[1,"98","2","High-Performance Athlete Training and Development Programme","Continue the completion of training and fostering a pool of high-record athletes.",""],[1,"98","2","Strategic Sports Investment Planning and Resource Allocation","Choose, and group advantageous sports in order to make good plans for investments and efficiently use resources in athlete training.",""],[1,"98","2","Sports Science and Technology Advancement Initiative","Give priority to research and application of scientific and technological advances so as to make breakthroughs in improving the country's sport achievements.",""],[1,"98","2","Professionalization of Football and Other Potential Sports","Renovate the organizational and operational practices by applying professional mechanisms to soccer and any other potential sports.",""],[1,"98","2","Elite Athlete Preparation for Major International Competitions","Well prepare athletes for participating in and recording high scores in 2008 Olympic, ASIAD 2010 and subsequent SEA GAMES.",""],[1,"98","3","National Health and Physical Development Measures","Promote scientific research and implement comprehensive measures to gradually ameliorate the health and height of Vietnamese people.",""]],"14":[[1,"9","3","Free Health Care for Young Children and Vulnerable Groups","Implement the free-of-charge health care policies for under 6 children, elderly people and other social targeted people.",""],[1,"9","3","Medical Fee Reduction and Exemption for Poor Children","Through medical insurance, reduce or exempt medical fees for under 6 children of poor households.",""],[1,"9","3","Health Insurance Expansion and Voluntary Insurance Development","Develop and enhance the quality medical insurance, implement voluntary medical insurance, gradually and firmly step to extend medical insurance for all people.",""],[1,"94","1","Free Health Examination and Treatment for Children Under Six","Effectively implement policies of free health examination and treatment for under-6 children, health insurance for the poor, elderly and social-support people through health insurance schemes, and hospital fee exemption for poor under-6 children.",""],[1,"94","1","Health Insurance Expansion for Poor, Elderly, and Social-Support Groups","Effectively implement policies of free health examination and treatment for under-6 children, health insurance for the poor, elderly and social-support people through health insurance schemes, and hospital fee exemption for poor under-6 children.",""],[1,"94","1","Universal Health Insurance Implementation","Develop and enhance quality of health insurance with better implementation of ordinary health insurance schemes and volunteering health insurance, creating firmed steps to implement health insurance for all people.",""],[1,"94","6","Medical Financial Policy Reform and Universal Health Insurance Expansion","Renovate and improve medical financial policies so as to increase public financial sources.",""],[1,"94","7","Results-Based Health Service Financing Reform","Change the methods of funding from budget allocation according to the number of sick beds to allocation on the basis of treatment results (the government buys medical services",""],[1,"95","2","Hospital Fee Collection Reform","Basically change the methods of hospital fee collection at public healthcare centers according to the principle of collecting exactly and enough for necessary expenses.",""],[1,"95","2","Medical Insurance Coverage for Vulnerable Groups","The Government ensures that poor people and children under six and targeted groups receive basic services through medical insurance; partially support hospital fees for near-poor people in disadvantaged localities.",""]],"15":[[1,"94","2","Grassroots Public Health Care Strengthening Programme","Invest, strengthen and improve public health care at grassroots level both in terms of infrastructure, and staff.",""],[1,"94","2","Primary and Preventive Health Care Prioritization","Give priorities to grassroots health care and preventive healthcare.",""],[1,"94","2","Provincial and District Hospital Upgrade Programme","Build and upgrade hospitals, especially General hospitals in provinces and districts to basically meet local people' demands of medical check and treatment.",""],[1,"94","2","Sanatorium and Rehabilitation Facility Development","Gradually build wards and hospitals for sanatorium and rehabilitation.",""],[1,"94","2","Health Check and Treatment Center Network Expansion","Plan and invest more in health check and treatment centers network proportionate to residences rather than administrative borders, continuing investment in specialized medical centers.",""],[1,"95","5","Completion and Upgrading of Commune Medical Stations","Invest in the completion of commune, ward, and town medical stations so that they reach national standards and are capable of doing preventive medical tasks, treating and offering primary healthcare, especially those in the remote, hinterlands, disadvantaged areas and areas with a lot of ethnic minority inhabitants.",""],[1,"95","5","Preferential Remuneration Policy for Rural Health Workers","Continue to complete the concrete preferential remuneration policy to encourage doctors and nurses to work in these areas.",""],[1,"95","6","Medical Staff Development and Reform Policy","Develop the medical staff based on the requirements of improved professional skills, responsibilities and ethics.",""],[1,"120","8","Hospital Modernization Investment","give priority to investment in existing hospital modernization, especially provincial-level general clinics;",""],[1,"120","8","Specialized Health Center Construction","accelerate the construction of such specialized health centers as those for tumors, heart diseases and specialized antenatal and obstetric clinics in Can Tho City.",""],[1,"122","4","Marine Health System Strengthening","Intensify and develop marine medical systems in order to control diseases, protect, care for and improve the health of local people, of the armed forces and seaborne laborers.",""],[1,"126","8","Primary Health Facility Upgrading and Expansion","In the next five years, make intensive investments in upgrading and completing the network of local clinics; make full investments of national standards for communal, ward and town clinics.",""],[1,"126","8","Provincial and District General Clinic Strengthening","Pool resources to improve, expand, upgrade and supplement medical facilities to provincial and district general clinics to tackle with local demands for check-up and treatment.",""],[1,"126","8","Functional Rehabilitation Ward and Clinic Network Development","Gradually develop the network of functional rehabilitation wards and clinics.",""],[1,"126","8","Residential Area Health Service Network Development","Invest in the development of the network of health services for particular residential areas.",""],[1,"126","8","Traditional Hospital and Oriental Treatment Ward Upgrading","Upgrade traditional hospitals and oriental treatment wards in general hospitals.",""],[1,"126","9","Investment Support for Specialized Health Facilities","Support investments in tuberculosis hospitals, malaria research and prevention institutes, mental disease hospitals; vaccine-producing centers.",""],[1,"126","9","Completion of Specialized Health Center Investments","Complete investments in specialized health centers in Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh City and Central Region (Hue-Da Nang) and Can Tho.",""],[1,"126","10","Central Hospital Modernization and Synchronization","Modernize and synchronize central hospitals to apply technology achievements in examination and treatment.",""],[1,"126","10","Medicine and Vaccine Testing Capacity Building","Implement capacity building for medicine and vaccine testing.",""]],"16":[[1,"9","1","Compulsory and Voluntary Social Insurance Expansion","Strictly implement the compulsory social insurance regime, prepare and implement the voluntary social insurance system and loosing job insurance for labors.",""],[1,"9","4","Social Security Network Development","Develop the social security network.",""],[1,"9","4","Social Protection for Meritorious Persons and Vulnerable Groups","Well implement policies towards people with meritorious contribution to the nation, and families of martyrs and disabled soldiers, disable people and other social targeted groups.",""],[1,"55","1","Social Insurance Program Expansion","The social security system has been expanded.",""],[1,"55","2","Social Services and Health Care for Merited Persons","Social services and health care for merited persons have been maintained and extended.",""],[1,"55","2","Housing Support and Rehabilitation for Pre-August 1945 Revolutionaries","Policies to support and rehabilitate houses for pre-August- 1945 revolutionaries have gained achievements.",""],[1,"66","5","Social Security System Development and Social Problem Prevention","Sixth, realize social progress, equity and gender equality, create jobs, encourage people to get rich in legitimate ways, alleviate hunger and reduce poverty, develop social security system and prevent social problems.",""],[1,"69","8","Social Policy Implementation","implementing social policies as planned targets and for five years 2006-2010.",""],[1,"79","7","Expansion of Basic Social Welfare and Services","The state should increase budget for the development of material and technological bases to improve social welfare and ensure the provision of basic social services for poor people, poor regions and people with meritorious services to the country, primarily health care and educational services; at the same time favorable conditions should be created for development of private service facilities and foreign invested ones.",""],[1,"91","2","Compulsory Social Insurance Collection","Compulsory social insurance premium should be collected accurately.",""],[1,"91","2","Voluntary Social Insurance and Unemployment Insurance Implementation","Have good preparation and effective implementation of volunteering social insurance as well as unemployment insurance for workers.",""],[1,"91","4","Social Wage and Insurance Reform","Continue renovation of social salary scheme and insurance; have mechanism and policies on housing and social welfare for workers working in industrial parks, especially for those who are immigrants due to job location;",""],[1,"137","1","Pension Benefit Reform and Social Insurance Expansion","The objective the social security policy is to deal with shortcomings in pension benefits in the context of salary reform; gradually introduce the principle of payment based on contribution, improving the effectiveness of the social insurance investment fund to sustain and grow the fund; diversify social insurance forms, introduce voluntary and unemployment insurance to expand the coverage of the social security network to all employees who are not required to make compulsory contribution.",""],[1,"137","2","Social Insurance Policy Reform","Conduct reform of social insurance policy in line with the salary reform roadmap, such as deal with inappropriate practices in pension benefit in the context of salary reform; adjust pension benefits when the system of salary scale and scheme is changed with the principle that average pension benefits of those retiring before new salary scheme is introduced will correspond proportionately to the average pension benefits of those retiring after the new scheme has been introduced.",""],[1,"137","3","Social Insurance Salary Ceiling Control","Control the ,ceiling' salary level for social insurance purpose to ensure reasonable pension benefit relations among pension earners.",""],[1,"137","4","Voluntary Social Insurance Regime","Issue the voluntary social insurance regime for the worker not under the category of compulsory social insurance, including farmers, handicraft workers, self-employed people ...",""],[1,"137","5","Unemployment Benefit Regime for Workers with Long-Term Labor Contracts","Issue the unemployment benefit regime for the worker engaged in labour contracts from 12 months onwards.",""],[1,"137","6","Social Insurance Law Implementation","Organize implementation of the Social Insurance Law after the National Assembly's approval.",""],[1,"147","10","Social Insurance Policy and Mechanism Reform","Renovate the policy and mechanism of social insurance; encourage the community's participation in voluntary insurance schemes;",""],[1,"147","15","Pro-Poor Policy and Institutional Strengthening","Continue accomplishing policies and institutions affecting the poor, set more feasible targets and allocate better resources for programs which benefit the poor.",""],[1,"147","16","Public Sector, Jurisdiction, and Financial Management Reform","Perfect reform strategies related to public sector, jurisdiction, and financial management to better support the poor.",""]],"17":[[1,"90","3","Child Access to Basic Services Initiative","Ensure all children's access to basic healthcare and quality educational services, to clean water and sanitation facilities at school, public places and at home.",""],[1,"90","3","Child Protection Against Discrimination and Harassment","Maximize the number of children protected against discrimination and harassment.",""],[1,"90","4","Social Services Network for Family and Children Care and Protection","Establish social services network in communication, education, and counseling on family and children care and protection.",""],[1,"90","5","Elderly Care and Disability Rehabilitation Services","expand services to care for the elderly, PLWD (people living with disability), and rehabilitation facilities for children and PLWD.",""],[1,"90","5","Multi-level Coordination and Social Organization Engagement Mechanism","Raise responsibility and intensify coordination among different levels, sectors and people, involve all economic sectors and social organizations in population, family and children activities.",""],[1,"90","6","Family Access to Social Services and Welfare Initiative","Facilitate families' access to legislation, culture, healthcare, education, science, technology and social welfare.",""],[1,"90","6","Healthy Community and Sustainable Family Development Initiative","Construct a healthy social environment in communities, and build up sustainable families with good cultural norms.",""],[1,"90","6","Population, Family and Children Coordination Mechanism","Complete the mechanism for integration and inter-sectoral coordination in population, family and children activities.",""],[1,"101","7","Child Protection Strategy and Social Worker Network","Make sure that children are protected from abuse, discrimination and maltreatment in the family through child protection strategy and establishment of a network of professional social workers.",""],[1,"101","7","Child-Friendly Commune Standards Programme","By 2010, 70% of communes, wards and towns are to meet the children-friendly standards, 85% of schools are provided with safe drinking water and hygienic latrines for girls and boys separately, 90% of children with extremely difficult situation are protected and taken care of.",""],[1,"102","1","National Action Plan for Children","The National Action Plan for Children shall be implemented to 2010 to exercise the basic rights of children.",""],[1,"102","2","Mainstream Child Protection, Education, and Care into Development Plans","Mainstream the tasks of protection, education and taking care of children into socio- economic development plans of all sectors and at all levels with concrete indicators and linked with resources to ensure the best benefits for children.",""],[1,"102","3","Children's Rights Coordination and Monitoring Mechanism","Strengthen the role, capacity and coordination mechanism between functional authorities working for children's rights.",""],[1,"102","4","Child Rights Awareness and Family Support Measures","Propagandize, improve awareness, create favorable conditions for families in children rearing and education, improve the role, capacity and coordination mechanism among authorities concerned in the protection of children's rights.",""],[1,"102","4","Targeted Child Access to Basic Services and Protection","Take strong measures to ensure poor children, ethnic minority children, children in difficult areas, remote areas, street children, and handicapped children to have access to basic services, learning, care, participation in social activities in order to grow up both spiritually and physically.",""],[1,"102","4","Child Protection Against Abuse and Exploitation","Protect children from abuse, harassment, exploitation and hard work.",""],[1,"102","5","Support Policies for Talented and Gifted Children","Adopt policies to support talented and gifted children.",""],[1,"102","5","International Cooperation for Child Protection and Education","Enhance international cooperation to take advantage of technical assistance and resources for protection, education and taking care of children.",""],[1,"147","12","Adolescent Protection and Child Labor Elimination","Intensify the protection of adolescents; completely eliminate child labor;",""]],"18":[[1,"109","5","Socio-Economic Development Action Plans for Disadvantaged Areas","For disadvantaged areas: execute Resolutions of the Politburo85 on socio-economic development, national defense and security, and action plans of the Government on implementing socio-economic development in these areas.",""],[1,"110","1","Infrastructure Construction and Basic Services Expansion","construction of infrastructure, primarily transport and irrigational systems, clean water and electricity supplies, education and training development, improvement of people's education levels and the quality of human resources.",""],[1,"110","1","Provincial Central Town Development","Establish central towns of provincial level.",""],[1,"110","1","Targeted Provincial Investment Support","Mobilize investments for provinces that face difficulties with high rate of poor households to make breakthroughs so that they can rapidly catch up with the common development level of the whole country.",""],[1,"110","1","Social Safety Net Expansion for Low-Income Households","Develop the social safety nets for low-income and poor people.",""],[1,"110","1","Vocational Training and Job Creation for Women","Strengthen vocational training and job creation, reduce the work burden and increase incomes for women.",""],[1,"110","1","Hunger Eradication and Poverty Reduction in Disadvantaged Areas","Speed up hunger eradication and poverty reduction in disadvantaged areas.",""],[1,"110","3","Northern and Midland Mountainous Area Development Programme","Speed up socio-economic development of the Northern and Midland mountainous areas for hunger eradication and poverty reduction, narrow the disparities in terms of living conditions, and social progress among different regions nationwide; take advantage of each region's strengths in terms of soils, climate, mineral resources, hydroelectricity, and proximity to border gates for economic development.",""],[1,"110","3","Regional Socio-Economic Infrastructure Improvement","Significantly improve socio- economic infrastructure to meet the demands of development in the region; complete the task of encouraging people to move back to border areas; preserve and develop the cultural identities of ethnic minority people; improve people's material and spiritual life; combine socio-economic development with environment protection and national security and defense assurance.",""]],"19":[[1,"9","2","National Targeted Program for Hunger Eradication and Poverty Reduction","Diversify methods and resources to better implement the national targeted program on hunger eradication and poverty reduction",""],[1,"9","2","Poverty Reduction Support Policies for Remote and Ethnic Minority Areas","Promote special policies to support investment and production, particularly policies on production land; support living land, houses, clean water, vocational training and job creation for poor ethnic minority people, and people that live in isolated, remote and disadvantaged areas",""],[1,"55","5","Essential Infrastructure Investment for Remote and Ethnic Minority Areas","Following the policy on supporting socio-economic development for remote and mountainous areas and areas with ethnic minority people, so far, the State has paid attention to investment in such essential infrastructure as transport, irrigation, power, water, medical station, school, etc., in order to serve production and life of ethnic minority people.",""],[1,"55","6","Ethnic Minority Land Support and Livelihood Stabilization Policy","Moreover, in addition to continuing the policy of land allocation, forest allocation, bare land and hill greening coverage, and clear definition of land-use rights for ethnic minority households, the Government has decided to support production land for ethnic minority households in order to stabilize and improve their living standards.",""],[1,"55","6","Ethnic Minority Agricultural Settlement and Residence Stabilization","The work of agricultural settlement, fixed residence, life stabilization of ethnic minority people has been done well.",""],[1,"55","6","Ethnic Minority Housing Support Policy","Housing problems of ethnic minority people have been paid much attention.",""],[1,"55","6","Ethnic Minority Social Service Assistance Policy","The policies on social, educational, medical and cultural assistance have been carried out.",""],[1,"71","2","Rural Hunger and Poverty Reduction","Completely eliminate hungry households and substantially reduce poor households by 2010.",""],[1,"72","7","Hunger Eradication and Poverty Reduction Investment","invest in hunger eradication and poverty reduction, primarily in mountainous, remote areas and areas with large ethnic minority population.",""],[1,"73","4","Measures to Mitigate Impacts of Integration on Agriculture and Rural Areas","Work out proper measures to release impacts of integration on agricultural and rural fields.",""],[1,"73","5","Farmer Compensation, Training, and Job Support for Land Reclamation","Take care of the lives and jobs for farmers whose agricultural land has been reclaimed for the sake of industrialization, renovate compensation mechanism for agricultural land reclamation, using part of the compensation to provide training and support to knowledge improvement for female farmers as well as new job training to young laborers.",""],[1,"91","7","Hunger Eradication and Poverty Reduction Effort","Hunger eradication, poverty reduction and encouragement to get rich in legitimate manner",""],[1,"91","8","National Targeted Poverty Reduction and Job Creation Program","Diversify resources and methods to implement the National Targeted Program on Poverty Reduction, The Program on Job Creation.",""],[1,"92","1","Basic Social Services Access Improvement for the Poor","Improve access to basic social services of the poor through policies on medical care, education, clean water, housing, residential land, infrastructure for people's lives;",""],[1,"92","1","Public Participation in Program and Policy Decision-Making","improve people's participation in the decision-making process of programs and projects, mechanisms and policies on hunger elimination, poverty reduction and reduction of repeated poverty rate.",""],[1,"92","2","Targeted Poverty Reduction Investment Prioritization","Diversify the mobilization of resources for poverty reduction; give priority of investment to communes and districts with high poverty rate in order to make significant changes.",""],[1,"92","3","Hunger Elimination and Poverty Reduction Capacity-Building and Mobilization Program","Enhance the awareness and capacity of all authority levels, branches, organizations and people in terms of hunger elimination and poverty reduction; strengthen and improve the capacity of cadres involved in the work of hunger elimination and poverty reduction in communes and districts, particularly difficulty-stricken communes, remote and mountainous areas; mobilize organizations and unions to participate in the national target program on hunger elimination and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"92","4","Hunger Eradication and Poverty Reduction Program Monitoring and Evaluation System","Develop the system for information, monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of hunger eradication and poverty reduction programs according to set objectives from the Central to local levels.",""],[1,"92","5","International and Community Cooperation for National Target Program Implementation","Intensify international and community cooperation, continue the decentralization of management and governance of the implementation of national target programs, and better conduct the socialization of hunger eradication and poverty reduction work.",""],[1,"92","5","Decentralized Management and Governance of National Target Programs","continue the decentralization of management and governance of the implementation of national target programs",""],[1,"92","5","Socialization of Hunger Eradication and Poverty Reduction","better conduct the socialization of hunger eradication and poverty reduction work.",""],[1,"93","4","Poverty Training and Knowledge Transfer Support","Help the poor through training, knowledge transfer and experience sharing.",""],[1,"120","8","Khmer Poverty Reduction Support Measures","Create favorable conditions for Khmer people to eliminate poverty and improve their life;",""],[1,"122","8","Target Program on Hunger Eradication and Poverty Reduction","More investments will be made to effectively implement the target program on hunger eradication and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"125","6","Gratitude and Charity Housing Support","Promote movements to develop \"Fund of Gratitude\" [to revolutionaries, invalid soldiers, etc.], encourage the construction of houses of \"gratitude\" and houses of \"love/charity\" to provide accommodation to poor households.",""],[1,"125","6","Accommodation Support for Ethnic Minorities","Continue accommodation support for ethnic minorities with housing difficulties.",""],[1,"127","6","Housing Development Fund Investment","Invest in housing development funds in different forms and from different investment resources, especially in the Mekong Delta, the Northern mountainous areas, the Central Highland, disadvantaged ethnic areas, remote areas, big cities and industrial regions.",""],[1,"127","6","Social Welfare and Resettlement Housing Provision","Develop accommodation for beneficiaries of social welfare and residents of resettlement programs.",""],[1,"127","6","Student and Low-Income Housing Expansion","Build more accommodation for students and low-income people.",""],[1,"127","6","Rental and Hire-Purchase Housing Development","Develop more accommodation for lease or for hire-purchase (paying through installments).",""]],"20":[[1,"9","7","National Defense and Security Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen national defense capacity and security, maintain proactiveness against any situation, firmly defend national independence, sovereignty, unity, territorial integrity, and national security, keeping politic stability, national security and social orders.",""],[1,"9","8","Development of Army Industries","Develop army's industries to meet requirements of defending national security and of people needs.",""],[1,"66","7","National Defense and Security Strengthening","Eighth, strengthen national defense and security, firmly maintain peaceful environment, stabilize socio-political situation and expand foreign relationship to create advantageous conditions for national construction and protection.",""],[1,"108","1","Development of Military Production Industries","Push up development of production industries of military forces to link the needs of defense with the needs of social life.",""],[1,"108","3","National Defense and People's Security Strengthening","Reinforce national defense potentials, maintain national security.",""],[1,"108","3","National Unity and Solidarity Bloc Strengthening","Strengthen and promote the strength of the whole people's great unity and solidarity bloc.",""],[1,"108","3","All-People National Defense and Security Front","Build up a firm national defense of all people and combine it with people's security front.",""],[1,"108","4","Legal System Completion and State Security Management Strengthening","Complete the law system, improve the efficiency of State management over order and security in all fields; prevent our revolutionary achievements from taking advantage of democracy and human rights for unsound purposes.",""],[1,"108","4","Integrated Coordination of Economic Development, National Defense, Security, and Foreign Affairs","Strictly combine the tasks of economic development, national defense, security and foreign affairs.",""],[1,"108","5","Military and Police Readiness and Logistics Upgrade","Improve the army's readiness for action and the people's police's activeness in dealing with any unexpected situations.",""],[1,"108","6","Army Industry Development Master Plan Implementation","Implement the master plans of army's industry development until 2010 and its strategy until 2020 as decided by the Prime Minister.",""],[1,"108","6","Investment and Development of Army Industries","Strengthening investment and development of army's industries (including civil industrial production units that serve defense objectives), key laboratories for scientific researches and technologies.",""],[1,"108","7","Strengthening Training Facilities for National Security and Defense Units","Consolidate and strengthen material and technical facilities for training units of national security and defense at the Central and localities in order to improve the readiness for fighting against and coping with unexpected situations which can influence national security and social order.",""],[1,"109","2","Upgrade Material and Technical Facilities for Public Forces","Improve material and technical facilities for all forces to implement the national strategies for drug and social problems prevention, national defense, road safety, fire fighting and prevention; gradually invest in facilities for jails and retention camps.",""]],"21":[[1,"6","17","Energy Industries and Industrial Materials Development","Push up the development of energy industries, critical industries that manufacture production materials,",""],[1,"74","11","Stable Power Supply and Grid Investment Programme","Ensure stable power supply to production and daily life in the next five years.",""],[1,"75","1","Competitive Electricity Market Development","Continue to establish a competitive electricity market.",""],[1,"75","1","Regional Power Exchange Cooperation","Be proactive in regional and international cooperation for power exchange with other countries through grid connections with China, Laos, Cambodia and Thailand; cooperate with Laos and other countries in investment into power sources.",""],[1,"75","1","Integrated Power Generation and Grid Investment","Synchronous investment in power sources and grids, with appropriate structure of coal thermal, gas thermal and hydropower generation is important.",""],[1,"75","1","Priority Power Source Project Acceleration","Particular attention should be paid to projects concerning power sources to ensure schedule and avoid power shortage due to slow investment.",""],[1,"75","1","Son La Hydropower and Thermal Power Priority Investment","Priority should be given to Son La Hydropower project, coal and gas thermal power projects.",""],[1,"75","1","Electricity Capacity Expansion Plan","Try to increase power generation capacity by 16,800 Mw79 in the next five years so that the total power capacity can reach 28,200 Mw by 2010.",""],[1,"123","3","Power Plant Capacity Expansion","More investments will be made to increase capacity of power plants.",""],[1,"123","3","Comprehensive Electricity Transmission and Distribution Network Development","Develop a comprehensive electricity transmission and distribution network; focus on the improvement of quality and expansion of electricity system in rural, remote and mountainous areas, and areas of ethnic minorities.",""]],"22":[[1,"84","8","Import Prioritization and Trade Deficit Reduction Policy","Give priority to the import of materials, advanced equipment and technologies; be pro-active in importation, focus on importing modern equipment from countries with source technologies; rapidly reduce and limit the import of backward or intermediary technologies as well as goods, materials, equipment and consumer goods available domestically.",""],[1,"85","3","Priority Import of Advanced Machinery and Production Equipment","Give priority to imports from developed countries with advanced machinery industry.",""],[1,"85","3","Technology Line Quality and Cost Compliance","Pay attention to technological lines which meet the quality, cost requirements and conditions of Vietnam.",""]],"23":[[1,"52","5","Cultural and Information Activities Development","Cultural-information activities continue to develop with diversity, enhancing efficiency of political, idealism and legal training, making contribution to raising public spiritual life and for an advanced and traditional culture of Vietnam.",""],[1,"53","3","Grassroots Cultural and Information Services Expansion","investment is made in building people's spiritual and cultural life; the quality of cultural life at grassroots level is enhanced, ensuring that all grassroots units provide cultural services to the local people, such as books, newspapers, radio broadcasts, television broadcasts, movie shows, concerts and theatrical performances, etc., particularly in remote, mountainous and border areas, while \"information-blank\" areas are gradually eliminated.",""],[1,"53","3","Family Values and Good Family Movement","Attention is also paid to the movement to build up good families and preserve family rules, which helps diversify the cultural life at grassroots levels.",""],[1,"53","3","Cultural Institutions and Regulations Development","The development of cultural institutions and regulations in a market economy has been fostered.",""],[1,"53","3","Increased Investment in Cultural and Information Activities","Investments in cultural and information activities in the whole country have increased.",""],[1,"53","5","Community Cultural Facilities Maintenance and Expansion","Reading rooms and bookcases of communes, hamlets and communal cultural posts have been stabilized; increased social awareness of preservation and upholding of tangible and intangible cultural heritages has been an incentive for ceaselessly developed restoration works.",""],[1,"53","5","Cultural House Maintenance and Talent Promotion Activities","cultural houses from the central, provinces, districts to communes have been maintained and extended with various activities of culture, art, and promotion of talents for all social classes.",""],[1,"53","5","Mobile Cultural Outreach for Rural Communities","Performing artists, drama troupes, mobile movie-showing teams, cinematographical companies, etc., are encouraged to travel and serve people all over the country.",""],[1,"53","9","Cultural Heritage Restoration and Traditional Practice Promotion","\"Restoration and recovery of cultural, historical monuments, such as pagodas, temples\"; \"Maintenance of good cultural practices and customs, traditional songs, national artistic traditions, such as singing, music, dancing, fine arts, handicrafts, architecture, etc.\"",""],[1,"55","2","Patriotic Gratitude and Commemoration Movement Promotion","Movements, such as \"thanks-giving\", \"as you drink water, remember its source\", have been progressively promoted.",""],[1,"55","2","Martyrs' Cemetery Construction and Upgrading","Martyrs' cemeteries, particularly international ones, are being constructed and upgraded.",""],[1,"78","10","Social Participation in Culture and Social Activities","This is considered a breakthrough to mobilize more social participation in culture, and social activities.",""],[1,"96","4","Public Cultural Infrastructure Development","Develop public culture centers like commune and village's sports and culture centers, central culture houses, libraries, theaters, cinemas, art monuments, parks, and entertainment centers, etc.",""],[1,"96","7","National Cultural Heritage Preservation and Development Programme","Preserve and develop the nation cultural heritage values, and good traditional customs and practices, traditional artistic forms and folk arts.",""],[1,"96","7","Traditional Arts Preservation Initiative","Give priority to the preservation and development of traditional arts (tuong, cheo, cai luong, quan ho, water puppetry, etc).",""],[1,"96","7","Cultural Monument and Relic Preservation Programme","Attach importance to the preservation of revolutionary, historical, and special cultural monuments and relics.",""],[1,"96","7","Sino-Nom Document Surveying and Archiving Programme","Basically complete surveying, collecting, archiving, preserving and translating documents in Sino - Nom scripts.",""],[1,"96","7","Intangible Cultural Heritage Research and Collection Programme","Continue to study and collect typical intangible cultural values of different ethnicities.",""],[1,"96","7","Pilot Preservation of Typical and Ancient Villages","Pilot the preservation of typical villages and ancient villages, and cultural values of all ethnic groups.",""],[1,"96","8","National School and Library Network Development","Develop the library system at schools and library network nationwide.",""],[1,"97","2","Private Heritage Preservation Support","Encourage private collectors, museums to contribute to the preservation of monuments, tangible and intangible cultural heritages.",""],[1,"97","4","Cultural Heritage Protection and Management Decentralization","Assign and decentralize exact tasks and authority to proper agencies and individuals in order to manage and protect monuments, tangible and intangible cultural heritages.",""],[1,"97","4","Commune Post Office Conversion to Cultural and Sports Centers","Closely coordinate with commune post offices to turn them into communal culture and sport centers.",""],[1,"126","11","Community Cultural Center Construction","Build cultural centers for communities.",""],[1,"126","11","Cultural Heritage Preservation and Development Investment","Invest in the preservation and development of cultural heritages, with focus on historical, revolutionary sites and special national cultural sites.",""],[1,"126","11","Sino-Nom Document Preservation and Translation Initiative","Complete baseline research, collection, storage, preservation and translation of Sino-Nom documents.",""],[1,"126","11","Pilot Heritage Preservation Programmes in Ethnic Minority Villages","Pilot heritage preservation programs in typical ancient villages or hamlets of ethnic minorities.",""],[1,"126","12","Cultural Heritage Preservation and Commune Sports and Culture Center Construction","Mobilize resources for cultural projects.",""],[1,"126","12","Management and Preservation of Historical and Cultural Relics","Manage and preserve tangible and intangible historical and cultural relics;",""],[1,"126","12","Commune Sports and Culture Center Construction","accelerate the construction of commune sports and culture centers.",""],[1,"127","1","Vietnam Cultural and Tourism Villages Development","projects for Vietnam cultural and tourism villages representing various ethnic groups in the country",""],[1,"127","1","Cultural and Historical Site Preservation and Maintenance","preservation and maintenance of cultural and historical sites",""],[1,"127","1","Museum and Library System Investment","make in-depth investments in museums, library system",""],[1,"127","2","Sports Training Center Construction and Community Sports Facilities Support","Focus on the construction of Sports Training Center No I, II, III.",""]],"24":[[1,"81","2","Telecommunication and Postal Service Improvement and Expansion","Continue to improve the quality, reduce the cost, keep reasonable charges to increase the competitiveness in line with integration requirements.",""],[1,"81","2","Telecommunication and Postal Network Development","Boost the development of telecommunication and postal network and new services such as high-speed Internet, domestic and international mobile phone, broadband services, etc; continue developing communal culture-post agents, universalizing basic telecommunication and postal services; boost services with export potentials for foreign currency revenue.",""],[1,"96","2","Expansion of Cultural and Broadcasting Services","Plan and develop the efficiency of cultural, radio and television broadcasting, and press services in performing their roles of providing information and entertainment.",""],[1,"96","2","Universal Radio and Television Access Expansion","Popularize radio and television to all the people, including those in remote and hinterlands areas.",""],[1,"96","2","Information Technology Development Initiative","Develop information technology (telecommunications, informatics, electronic newspapers).",""],[1,"96","2","Publication Distribution Expansion","Strive for the popularizing of publications to all districts and most communes by 2010.",""],[1,"97","6","Digital Radio and Television Transition","Gradually move to digital radio and television technology in order to improve program quality and expand services.",""],[1,"97","6","District Radio Broadcast System Expansion","Attach importance to district radio broadcast system, especially that of mountainous, island and ethnic minority areas.",""],[1,"97","6","Universal Access to Radio and Television Receivers","Popularize radio and television receivers to all people.",""],[1,"97","6","Media Management and Regulation Improvement","Development should go along with proper and effective management in press and other mass media.",""],[1,"124","9","Telecommunication Infrastructure Development","Formulate and develop telecommunication infrastructure with advanced technology at the same level with other advanced countries in the region; with wide coverage, strong bandwidth and high speed and quality to meet the socio-economic development demand.",""],[1,"124","9","Network Security and Service Quality Assurance","To ensure the network infrastructure, quality of service and security of information for various services: public service, public administration, e-commerce, finance, banking and customs ...",""],[1,"126","13","Digital Broadcasting Technology Investment","Invest in the application of digital technology to radio and television broadcasting, improve the quality of programs and offer more services.",""],[1,"127","1","Radio and Television Station Capacity Improvement","improve capacity for radio and television stations",""]],"25":[[1,"7","3","Enterprise Development and Competitiveness Improvement Measures","Create favorable environments for the development of enterprises; improve the quality and efficiency of production and business activities of enterprises.",""],[1,"7","3","State Enterprise Reorganization and Equitization Reform","Complete the reorganization, innovation and equitization of State enterprises as regulated by the Law on Enterprises.",""],[1,"7","3","Non-State Enterprise Expansion Programme","Vigorously develop the number and size of non-state enterprises, raise the number of enterprises to 500,000 by the year 2010.",""],[1,"20","1","Private Sector Investment and Production Promotion","which will create new driving forces to encourage all economic sectors to invest into and promote production and trade.",""],[1,"31","2","State Economic Sector Renovation and Restructuring","The State economic sector, of which SOEs, is continuing its renovation and restructuring in accordance with the Resolution of the Third Central Party's Plenum (9th tenure)",""],[1,"31","3","State Enterprise Restructuring and Equitization Program","the government has made great efforts to direct ministries, branches, cities' and provinces' People's Committees in the renovation and development of State enterprises in accordance with the government's Action Program to implement the Central Resolution No.3, in order to restructure, equitize, sell and lease State enterprises",""],[1,"31","3","Pilot Transformation of State-Owned Enterprises","it has had several pilot transformations from State-owned enterprises to one-member limited companies, and some pilot restructuring in the model of parent companies and subsidiaries (holding companies)",""],[1,"31","7","Enterprise Law Amendment and Enterprise Incentive Reform","The Enterprise Law has been amended to be more suitable and to bring into full play each enterprise's activeness.",""],[1,"72","9","Restructuring of State-Owned Agricultural and Forestry Enterprises","Complete the re-arrangement and renovation of production organization of the system of State-owned agricultural and forestry enterprises.",""],[1,"72","9","Equitization of Agricultural State-Owned Enterprises","Fundamentally complete the equitization of SOEs in agriculture.",""],[1,"129","5","State Enterprise Restructuring and Equitization","Complete the basic reorganization, innovation and equitization of State enterprises as it is regulated in the Law on Enterprises; at the same time vigorously develop the number and size of non-state enterprises.",""],[1,"130","2","Enterprise Equitization and Project Bond Financing","Press forward the equitization and issue project bonds in order to attract investment capital for enterprise development.",""],[1,"130","2","Development of Strong Economic Groups in Strategic Sectors","Establish strong economic groups in such fields as petroleum, aviation, telecommunications, electricity, etc., with financial and technological potentials to participate in regional and world markets.",""],[1,"130","3","State Enterprise Reorganization and Renovation Programme","Continue strengthening the reorganization and renovation and improve the efficiency and competitiveness of State enterprises.",""],[1,"130","4","State Enterprise Reorganization and Ownership Diversification Reform","Steadily speed up the reorganization and renovation of State enterprises by diversifying the ownership to improve efficiency and competitiveness;",""],[1,"130","4","Removal of Ministry and Local Authority Representatives from State Enterprise Governance","Gradually narrow and eliminate the function of representatives of ministries, provincial and city peoples' committees in the governance and management board of State enterprises.",""],[1,"130","5","State Enterprise Equitization and Public Listing Reform","Expand the scope of equitization of State enterprises.",""],[1,"130","6","Corporation Equitization and Holding Company Reform","For large-scale corporations which cannot be equitized as a whole, equitize their member businesses and transform the remaining ones into single-member (i.e. the State) or limited companies of several State members; at the same time, transform those corporations into the form of group companies held by a holding company.",""],[1,"130","6","Corporate Ownership Representation Board Reorganization","The management board is reorganized to represent the ownership in the corporation.",""],[1,"130","7","Pilot State-Controlled Economic Groups and Corporations","Establish some powerful economic groups and corporations with diversified ownership in which the State holds a controlling stake.",""],[1,"130","8","State Enterprise Restructuring and Divestment","Transform enterprises with 100% State capital into joint stock, multi-member or single- member limited companies whose owner is the State.",""],[1,"130","9","State Enterprise Monopoly Oversight and Regulation Reform","Minimize the scope of state monopoly and eliminate business privilege; install an oversight mechanism and regulation policy with regards to State enterprises holding a business monopoly position.",""],[1,"130","10","State Enterprise Manager Accountability and Contracting Reform","Build the mechanism that links the responsibility, power and interest of the enterprise manager with operational results of the enterprise.",""],[1,"130","10","Recruitment and Employment Contract Mechanism for State Enterprise Managers","Implement the mechanism of recruitment and working contract with managers of State enterprises, firstly those with management boards.",""],[1,"130","11","State Enterprise Capital Investment Mechanism","Carry out the mechanism of the State's capital investment in enterprises through the State financial investment company; State enterprises should try to mobilize market capital for their business development.",""],[1,"131","1","State Enterprise Establishment and Joint-Stock Conversion Policy","Set up new State enterprises only when they have all favorable conditions and only if they operate in the fields of production, supply of products and services vitally necessary for socio- economic development, and they should be mainly in the form of joint-stock companies.",""],[1,"131","2","Clarification of State Enterprise Governance Roles","Clearly define the function, power and responsibility of State administrative management agencies and the owner representative in State enterprises.",""],[1,"131","10","State Enterprise Equitization and Joint-Stock Enterprise Development","Encourage development of multi-owner economic forms, mainly joint-stock companies by equitizing State enterprises and developing new joint-stock enterprises, which will become an important component of the economy.",""],[1,"131","12","State Enterprise Share Sale and Equity Participation Scheme","Attract individuals to buy shares of State enterprises and invest in important fields of production and business of the economy.",""],[1,"131","12","Employee Share Ownership Conversion for Large Private Enterprises","Encourage large private enterprises to become joint-stock companies and sell their shares to employees.",""]],"26":[[1,"6","18","Services Sector Development and Competitiveness Enhancement","Facilitate the outstanding development of services.",""],[1,"78","10","Service Sector Development and Public Service Management Reform","Facilitate the outstanding development of services, in favor of highly potential and competitive ones, pay attention to the development and improvement of the quality of traditional services, develop new services, especially those with high intellectual proportion and those for business support.",""],[1,"79","2","Fair Competition and Trade Administration Reform","Perform fair competition, increase the role and efficiency of State administration in trade and services to meet various demands of production, business and social life, contribute effectively to the economic growth, market expansion and international economic integration.",""],[1,"79","4","Domestic Trade Modernization and Market Expansion","Upgrade the quality of domestic trade activities in the orientation of modernization, civilization and availability in every region of the country, meet all demands for production and social consumption at reasonable and stable prices, support domestic production, ensure the mobilization of huge sources of export goods, and ensure compatibility with the international integration and competition process.",""],[1,"79","4","Domestic and International Goods Circulation Improvement","Ensure the circulation of goods domestically and internationally.",""],[1,"79","4","Comprehensive Market Expansion in Urban, Rural, and Mountainous Areas","Comprehensively expand all kinds of markets in urban, rural and mountainous areas.",""],[1,"139","2","Services Market Development Initiative","Focus on vigorous development of the services market, particularly those that are of high quality and have a high value added.",""]],"27":[[1,"89","1","Advanced Technology Development and Industrial Modernization","Develop advanced technologies and modernize traditional technologies to accelerate technological innovation in all economic sectors, in order to improve the competitiveness of goods and services in domestic and international markets.",""],[1,"89","1","Information Technology and Biotechnology Sector Development","Gradually develop information technology and bio-technology to become key sectors with a fast growth rate and which increasingly satisfy domestic demands and contribute to an increase in export revenue.",""],[1,"89","2","Enterprise Technological Innovation and Research Institutions","Intensify technological innovation in enterprises, create the demands for the transfer and application of scientific and technological advances to production and life.",""],[1,"89","2","Enterprise Technological Research and Innovation Institutions","Establish institutions for technological research, innovation, invention in enterprises.",""],[1,"89","2","Research-Training Linkage for High-Value Technology Development","Closely link research with training with a view to create more high-valued technological products and young and scientifically and technologically qualified human resources.",""],[1,"89","2","University Pure Research Intensification","Concentrate and intensify pure research tasks at universities.",""],[1,"89","5","High-Tech Research and Application Promotion","Give priority to high-tech research development and application, primarily information technology, bio-technology, automation, production of materials.",""],[1,"89","5","Scientific and Technological Services Development","Develop scientific and technological services in quality standards, intellectual property, technology consultancy and transfer.",""]],"28":[[1,"127","9","Business Spirit Promotion and Self-Employment Support Programme","Launch programs and movements for all the public to encourage, train and praise business spirit and ideas; compliment brilliant individuals for excellent business ideas; encourage, support and provide training to self-employed households so that they can become private companies regulated by the Law on Enterprises.",""],[1,"129","5","Enterprise Development Enabling Environment","Create legal and socio-economic environments for the development of enterprises; improve with strong attention the quality and efficiency of production and business activities of enterprises.",""],[1,"129","5","Export Promotion and Technology Attraction Support","Create favorable conditions for enterprises to rapidly increase exports and attract capital and technologies, especially high technologies in order to lower production costs and improve the competitiveness of enterprises.",""],[1,"129","6","Enterprise Expansion and SOE Equitization Programme","Raise the number of efficiently operated enterprises to 500,000 by the year 2010, including about 320,000 new establishments.",""],[1,"129","7","Development of Large Economic Groups and Holding Companies","Develop large State or private corporations into large economic groups diversely owned by both the State and the private sector; develop private enterprises on a large scale in the form of holding companies with diversified ownership.",""],[1,"129","7","Enterprise Specialization and Efficiency Promotion","Develop enterprises with high specialization, efficiency, stability and sustainability.",""],[1,"129","9","Joint Venture Promotion and SME Development Support","Promote joint ventures between enterprises of various economic sectors to strengthen mutual development.",""],[1,"129","9","Inclusive Investment Support for Women and Small Businesses","Encourage all economic sectors to invest in production on various scales and levels, assisting women in business development.",""],[1,"129","9","Small and Medium-Sized Enterprise Development Support","Pay special attention to small and medium - sized businesses in connection with national development goals and directions, taking advantages of each region and locality.",""],[1,"131","11","Private Sector Development and Investment Facilitation","Create favorable conditions for the development and investment of the private sector without limiting their scales, trades, fields and regions.",""],[1,"131","11","Anti-Discrimination Measures for Private Producers and Entrepreneurs","Strictly eliminate all forms of discrimination and praise good producers and entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"131","11","Support for Large Private Enterprises and Women-Owned Enterprises","Encourage the development of large private enterprises, private economic groups and women-owned enterprises.",""],[1,"131","11","Small and Medium Enterprise Development Support","Support and encourage the development of SMEs in order to mobilize all possible resources and make use of the comparative advantages of each region and each locality, together with the development of rural industries, trade villages and farms, focusing more on SME development in remote, mountainous or difficult areas.",""],[1,"132","6","Enterprise Support Program for SMEs","Implement the enterprise-support program, particularly to newly-established SMEs (in human resource training and development, provision of market information, credit guarantee funds for SMEs, etc.)",""],[1,"132","6","SME Financial Policy Support Measures","Continue to address obstacles in financial policies so that the private sector can strongly and effectively develop, pay more attention to support to SMEs, enabling them to expand and improve their business efficiency.",""]],"29":[[1,"141","6","Enterprise Participation and Competition Support Mechanism","Accomplish the mechanism to support the participation, operation, development and competition of enterprises",""],[1,"142","1","Investment and Enterprise Law Enforcement Guidance","Execute the Law on Investment, and the Law on Enterprises and provide guidance on their enforcement.",""],[1,"142","2","Competition and Monopoly Control Legal Framework Reform","Accomplish and concretize an institutional and legal framework for competition and monopoly control.",""],[1,"142","2","Delegation of State Functions to Enterprise Support Associations","Transfer some functions of State bodies to associations and organizations which promote enterprise development.",""]],"30":[[1,"6","16","Agricultural Modernization and Rural Economic Development","Promote in-dept investment to make substantial changes in agriculture and to develop comprehensively rural economy.",""],[1,"6","16","Agricultural Structural Transformation and Modernization","Shift the structure of agriculture and rural economy toward modernization and industrialization; improve scientific researches and technology application in production, preservation and processing.",""],[1,"6","16","High-Tech Agricultural Production Zones","Establish hi-tech agricultural production zones and replicate this model in wider regions.",""],[1,"71","2","Agricultural Modernization and Rural Economic Development","Facilitate in-depth investment, create quality change in agricultural production and comprehensively develop rural economy, satisfy domestic demands and increase export turnover.",""],[1,"71","2","Diversified Clean Commodity Agriculture Development","Build up diverse and clean commodity agriculture, with fast and sustainable development, high quality, productivity and competitiveness.",""],[1,"71","2","Agricultural Research and Technology Application Program","enhance the research capacity levels, improved efficiency and technology through the application of scientific and technological advances to production, preservation and processing.",""],[1,"71","2","Industry-Agriculture Linkage Strengthening","Intensify the linkages between industry and agriculture so as to improve production efficiency.",""],[1,"71","2","High-Tech Agro-Production Zone Development","Establish hi- tech agro-production areas and let them develop widely.",""],[1,"71","2","Agricultural Value-Added Growth Target","The value added of agriculture, forestry and fishery is to increase by about 3.0 - 3.2% per annum (production value 4.5%).",""],[1,"72","3","Agricultural, Forestry, and Aquacultural Production Planning Reform","Review agricultural, forestry, aquacultural production planning to make it adaptive to domestic and international market requirements; make use of the natural and economic advantages of each ecological region, improve the competitiveness of each type of agricultural product and economy of which we are strong.",""],[1,"72","3","Centralized Production and Intensive Farming Area Development","Establish centralized production, intensive farming areas in association with processing industry.",""],[1,"72","3","Integrated Agro-Processing and Raw Material Supply Planning","Terminate the situation of building processing factories where raw materials are unavailable, or establishing raw material supply areas without the parallel construction of processing factories.",""],[1,"72","4","High-Productivity Plant and Livestock Variety Development","Develop high-productivity, high quality plant and livestock varieties, contributing to the reduction of production costs and improvement of agricultural product competitiveness.",""],[1,"72","4","Grassroots Agricultural Extension Network Strengthening","Improve the agricultural extension network at grassroots level, guide farmers to develop their production in accordance with master plans, apply scientific and technological advances to cultivation and livestock raising.",""],[1,"72","8","Agricultural and Rural Development Investment Intensification","Intensify investment in agricultural and rural development, including ODA, FDI, individuals' and enterprises' capital;",""],[1,"72","8","Public Budget Prioritization for Critical Rural Infrastructure","the State budget will be focused only on critical sectors such as irrigation, transport and clean water supply, on essential infrastructure to support the adoption of improved varieties, and on important basic research.",""],[1,"72","9","Multi-sectoral Rural Economic Development Policy","Continue the implementation of the policy for multi-sectoral economic development, mobilize all possible resources for production development in association with the re- organization of agricultural production and rural economy.",""],[1,"72","9","Farm Economy and Cooperative Development","Emphasize the development of farming economy; intensify the development of cooperatives; continue the implementation of field defragmentation.",""],[1,"72","9","Agriculture, Forestry and Fishery Investment Socialization","Accelerate socialization of investment into agriculture, forestry and fishery to reduce pressure on the State investment.",""],[1,"73","1","Agricultural and Rural Market Development","Develop markets for the sales of agricultural, forestry and fishery products as the bases for more effective structural transformation of agricultural production and rural economy.",""]],"31":[[1,"80","13","Marine Transportation Services Expansion","In marine transportation: expand shipping services abroad, encourage all economic sectors to invest into marine transportation, initially focus on services with a wide range of activities and high percentage of profits such as shipping agents, logistic services and multi-means transportation.",""],[1,"80","13","Port Administrative Reform","Boost the administrative reform at ports.",""],[1,"80","13","International Entrepôt Construction and Seaport Management Policy","Consider the construction of international entrepôts and issue seaport management policies.",""],[1,"81","1","Maritime Transport and Seaport Modernization Support","Continue applying and studying preferential policies of investment to modernize fleets and seaports; build suitable mechanisms to facilitate the transportation of imports and exports for Vietnamese transportation enterprises.",""],[1,"81","1","International Entrepôt Development at Seaports","Boost the exploitation of advantages, especially in seaports with overseas-link potentials to open international entrepôts.",""],[1,"121","4","Shipping Fleet Capacity Expansion","By 2010, the fleet of ships will increase by 192 ships of all kinds with total shipping capacity of 1.94 million DWT, including 18 container ships with shipping capacity of 301,736 DWT; 21 tankers with shipping capacity of 587,447 DWT, etc.",""],[1,"121","5","International Sailor Training Cooperation","Promote international cooperation in sailor training.",""],[1,"121","5","Marine Services Modernization and Safety Investment","Develop marine and support services with focus on facilities, modernization investment in marine safety management and marine services.",""],[1,"121","5","Rescue Services Improvement","Improve rescue services.",""],[1,"121","5","Overseas Marine Labor Market Expansion","Develop and expand oversea markets for marine labors.",""],[1,"121","12","Seaport Upgrading Investment Programme","Continue to invest in upgrading seaports to ensure the quality of the export products via these ports in the period of 2006-2010.",""],[1,"124","5","Seaport Modernization and Deep-Water Port Construction","Gradually complete and modernize a comprehensive system of sea ports, re- structure the fleet of ships and rejuvenate the fleet to increase their international competitiveness.",""],[1,"124","8","Sea and River Shipping and Waterway Development","Focus on maintenance and development of sea and river shipping, waterways to islands.",""]],"32":[[1,"80","10","Transport Network Expansion and Modal Shift Programme","Establish multi-means transportation network, shift the transportation structure in the orientation of increasing the volume of freight and passenger traffic by sea and by train, and reduce the rate of traffic on roads.",""],[1,"80","10","Transport Quality Improvement and Road Safety Measures","Improve the quality of means of transport; find solutions to minimize traffic accidents.",""],[1,"123","11","National Transportation Network Completion","Basically complete the transportation network to meet the demands of goods and passenger circulation within the country and with other countries, contributing to ensured defense and security.",""],[1,"124","1","National Transport Network Completion and Modernization","Basically complete and put into operation the network of essential national highways, railway routes and waterway routes.",""],[1,"124","1","Transport Infrastructure Development in Focal Economic Zones","Continue comprehensive construction of transportation system in focal economic zones.",""],[1,"124","1","Local Road Access Improvement to Commune Centers","Focus on the development of local traffic systems; ensure traffic flow on roads to the commune centers with 90% of the roads usable in all seasons.",""],[1,"124","2","National Roads and Highway Development Programme","Complete communication axes on the North-South lines, on major communication lines in important economic areas, focus on the development of roads in mountainous regions, the Central Highland and the Mekong Delta.",""],[1,"124","2","Highway Expansion in Economic Zones","Develop the highway system, with emphasis on developed economic zones with heavy traffic to avoid traffic jams.",""],[1,"124","2","Border Gate Infrastructure Upgrading","Invest more in infrastructure at international border gates, especially inland borders , facilitating faster throughput and increasing goods circulation.",""],[1,"124","2","Border Roads and Patrol Roads Completion","Basically complete border roads, especially the patrol roads and roads to border patrol stations in combination with people's welfare improvement.",""],[1,"124","2","Combined Economic and Defense Road Routes","Build up some routes for combined economic and defense purposes.",""],[1,"124","2","District Road Upgrading Programme","Upgrade district-level roads to ensure normal traffic flow in all seasons.",""],[1,"124","3","Rural Commune Road Construction","Complete the construction of roads to communes or communal centers.",""],[1,"124","3","River Bridge Construction for Relocation and Traffic Decongestion","Build bridges over rivers for population relocation and reduction of the density of traffic in cities.",""],[1,"124","3","Road Upgrading and Construction in Developing Districts","Upgrade or build roads in developing districts.",""]],"33":[[1,"120","9","Coastal Ports, Airports, and Sea Rescue Facilities Upgrade","Build up some coastal ports, airports, a fleet of ships and sea rescue facilities.",""],[1,"124","1","International Terminal Expansion and Modernization","Expand and modernize international terminals - airports and sea ports.",""],[1,"124","6","International Airport Expansion and Modernization","Gradually expand and upgrade international airports, modernize airplane facilities.",""],[1,"124","6","National Airport Capacity Expansion","Build up a system of airports with capacity of 20 million passengers annually.",""],[1,"124","6","Air Safety and Air Traffic Control Modernization","Improve ground services, air safety and modernize air traffic control systems.",""],[1,"124","6","Local Airport Investment","Invest in local airports if possible.",""]],"34":[[1,"7","2","Economic Integration Implementation and WTO Accession Preparedness","Effectively implement agreements with countries and international organizations in trade, investment, services and other fields.",""],[1,"7","2","Post-WTO Commitment Readiness Measures","Prepare good conditions to realize commitments after the country fully joins the World Trade Organization (WTO).",""],[1,"7","2","Resource, Technology, and Management Experience Mobilization for Integration","Take advantage of favorable conditions, make use of advantages, and minimize negative impacts of integration in order to mobilize more resources, technologies and to learn advanced management experiences.",""],[1,"34","9","Implementation of Trade Agreements and Commitments","Commitments under ASEAN Free Trade Area (AFTA), Vietnam-US Bilateral Trade Agreement and negotiations for WTO accession have been implemented effectively.",""],[1,"34","9","Signing and Implementation of Multilateral and Bilateral Agreements","The signing and implementation of multilateral and bilateral agreements and commitments with other countries, regional and international organizations has made significant contribution in the country's economic development.",""],[1,"35","1","Policy Harmonization and Subsidy Phase-Out Reform","policies for different economic sectors, domestic and foreign investors have been gradually unified; subsidy and financial support policies for inappropriate enterprises have been phased out; import tax reduction roadmap has been implemented in line with international commitments.",""],[1,"64","4","Strengthening Global Economic Integration","Globalization and international economic integration in connection with trade liberalization will be strengthened; investment, movement of goods and services, labor and capital will be increasingly expanded.",""],[1,"66","2","International Economic Integration Acceleration","Third, actively accelerate international economic integration, dramatically expand and improve the efficiency of foreign trade together with the establishment of an autonomous and self-reliant economy.",""],[1,"79","5","WTO and ASEAN Trade Services Compliance and Liberalization Measures","Complete mechanisms and policies aligned with the standards of WTO and general Trade and Services Agreement to facilitate negotiations and dispute settlement.",""],[1,"86","2","International Economic Integration Legal and Institutional Framework","Effectively implement bilateral and multilateral agreements on trade, investment, services and other fields.",""],[1,"86","3","Intergovernmental Coordination for Commitment Implementation","Establish close coordination between ministries and central sectors, central government and localities, the State and companies in the implementation of commitments.",""],[1,"86","3","Overseas Capital Policy and Legal Reform","Complete policies and laws concerning overseas capital, define a reasonable roadmap for the liberalization of capital flow in the international economic integration process.",""],[1,"86","4","Vietnamese-Foreign Enterprise Cooperation and Market Promotion Support","Facilitate cooperative activities between Vietnamese and foreign enterprises.",""]],"35":[[1,"50","4","Housing Ownership Certification and Real Estate Market Regulation Reform","Registration and issuance of housing ownership certificates have been pushed up, primarily in urban areas; regulations on housing ownership transfer have been rectified, promoting sale of State accommodation, diversifying types of housing business in urban areas.",""],[1,"73","6","Agricultural Land Limitation Policy Abolition and Land Use Tax Regulation","Abolish agricultural land limitation policies, applying taxes as instruments for regulating all activities related to land use.",""]],"36":[[1,"108","9","Maritime Economy Strategy Implementation","Implement the strategy of maritime economy to 2020.",""],[1,"108","9","Maritime Sovereignty Defense and Coastal Protection Investment","Continue to invest in the defense and protection of national sovereignty and interests on the sea, islands and coastal areas in combination with their socio-economic development.",""],[1,"110","2","Maritime Economy Development Program","Quickly, comprehensively and focally develop maritime economy with more comparative advantage sectors to make our country soon become a nation of powerful maritime economic development; attach maritime development to the assurance of national security and defense, and international cooperation.",""],[1,"110","2","Coastal Transport and Strategic Coastal Defense Infrastructure","Build a coastal transport system and economic units in combination with building strategic posts to protect the coast and strengthen the protection of Vietnamese territorial waters.",""],[1,"110","2","Maritime Science, Technology, and Human Resource Development","Strongly develop science, technology and human resources to serve the purposes of maritime development.",""],[1,"110","2","Marine Industry and Services Development","Develop industries and services supporting maritime economy.",""],[1,"110","2","Seaport and Island Service Center Development","Build some general service centers at some seaports and islands.",""],[1,"110","2","Marine Security and Sovereignty Protection Force Strengthening","Strengthen conditions and forces for ensuring marine security, firmly protecting sea and island sovereignty.",""],[1,"110","2","Marine Research and Forecast Center Development","Concentrate on the development of marine research and forecast centers.",""],[1,"115","1","Coastal Afforestation and Forest Cover Expansion","afforestation in coastal areas to prevent the intrusion of sand and salinity; increase forest coverage to 44 - 45%.",""],[1,"115","2","Aquaculture Development and Infrastructure Investment","Develop aquaculture, invest in infrastructure for aquaculture, ensure sustainable development, protect the ecological environment.",""],[1,"115","2","Offshore Fishing and Fishery Logistics Infrastructure","Develop offshore fishing combined with maritime security protection, build seaports infrastructure, and services sectors as logistics for fishery; build areas for storm sheltering in river mouths and islands with heavy water traffic.",""],[1,"115","3","Coastal, Island, and Cultural Tourism Development","Pay special attention to the attraction of investment in coastal and island tourism development; develop attractive tourist places and areas as Phong Nha-Ke Bang, Ancient Capital of Hue, Canh Duong-Lang Co-Non Nuoc complex, Hoi An, My Son, Van Phong, Dai Lanh, Cam Ranh, Mui Ne.",""],[1,"115","3","Integrated Urban, Industrial, and Tourism Development","Combine the development of cities, industrial groups with tourist development, especially sea and island tourism.",""],[1,"115","3","Regional Tourism Cooperation and Route Expansion","Bring into play the tourist role in economic cooperation of East-West corridor; pay attention to expanding trade, tourist and service relations with neighboring countries as Laos, Cambodia, Thailand; participate in tourism of the Me Kong sub-region, and expand trans-Asian routes.",""],[1,"115","4","Regional Transportation and Service Sector Development","Develop transportation services: air transportation, sea transportation, international telecommunications, banking, finance, insurance, and information technology application services in industrial, economic zones, in border economic zones and cities in the region.",""],[1,"115","4","Trade Center and Trade Zone Development","Build trade centers in Vinh, Hue, Da Nang, Quy Nhon, Nha Trang, Phan Thiet and trade zones in some inland border gates.",""],[1,"115","4","Fishing Industry and Island Tourism Services Development","Develop services for fishing industry and tourism in some island districts in the region.",""],[1,"115","4","Rural Market Development Acceleration","Speed up the development of rural markets.",""],[1,"115","5","Van Phong and Tien Sa Port Development and Regional Transport Infrastructure Upgrade","Comprehensively develop infrastructures: Build Van Phong international transit seaport (Khanh Hoa), Tien Sa seaport (Da Nang) of the second stage as gateway ports for the development of the Central key economic region; upgrade seaports, airports in the region for the purpose of socio-economic development.",""],[1,"115","6","Road Infrastructure Connectivity Investment","Invest in road building to ensure smooth traffic between Eastern and Western parts during rainy and flooding seasons; build road links among seaports, airports and coastal towns to Western districts of the region, links the Central Highland to the neighboring countries of Laos, Cambodia and Northeast Thailand.",""],[1,"115","8","Coastal Economic Zone Development","Gradually invest in establishing some costal economic zones attached to some transport routes, urban centers and border economic zones in the West of the region.",""],[1,"115","8","Vinh City Economic and Cultural Center Development","Build Vinh city to make it the economic and cultural center of the Northern Central area.",""]],"37":[[1,"131","4","Collective Economy Development Plan Implementation","Implement the 5-year Plan for Collective Economy Development 2006 - 2010 approved by the Prime Minister in the Decision 272/2005/QD-TTg dated 31 October, 2005.",""],[1,"131","5","Cooperative Sector Growth Promotion","Increase the growth rate of cooperatives, enabling it to contribute more to the whole economy and to the cause of hunger alleviation and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"131","6","Cooperative Economy Development Support","Create favorable conditions for developing various forms of cooperative economy in line with the development level of industries and trades in regions.",""],[1,"131","7","Cooperative Model Research and Development Programme","Continue researching and building new cooperative models on the basis of reviewing success stories and best practices with a view to creating development motivation, increasing the attractiveness of the collective sector.",""],[1,"131","7","Collective Economy Ownership Diversification Reform","Diversify the ownership forms in the collective economy (ownership of legal person, legal entity and cooperative included).",""],[1,"131","7","Cooperative and Cooperative Union Enterprise Development","Develop different types of enterprises in the forms of cooperatives and cooperative union.",""],[1,"131","8","Cooperative Modernization and Efficiency Improvement","Renovate and improve the efficiency of cooperatives' operation; increase their role in the provision of services and inputs to farmers; apply advanced technology, improve efficiency and competitiveness of cooperatives, unions as well as their members.",""],[1,"131","9","Cooperative Capital Mobilization and Development Support","Encourage and mobilize shares and capital of cooperative members to continuously increase investment capital for cooperative development; increase assets and undivided funds.",""],[1,"131","9","Cooperative Restructuring and Legal Compliance Reform","Dissolve or transform cooperatives non-eligible to the Law on Cooperatives into a suitable form of production and business institution in accordance with legal regulations.",""]],"38":[[1,"2","17","Economic Legislative System Development","Develop the economic legislative system",""],[1,"2","19","Market Development Initiative","Systematically establish different types of markets",""],[1,"4","14","Market Economy Institutional Reform","Continue reform and complete the market economy institutions with socialist orientation",""],[1,"7","4","Institutional Renovation and Market Planning Reform","Continue renovation and completion of organizational and operational institutions, respecting rules of market economy.",""],[1,"17","4","Economic Innovation and Policy Reform Package","we have consistently implemented economic innovation guidelines for the development of a multi-sectoral economy operating under socialist-oriented market mechanism; socio-economic management policies and mechanisms start to be more complete and harmonious; a number of policies for the mobilization of internal resources and foreign capital, policies for the development of agriculture and rural areas, for domestic and export market expansion, for social development, job creation, poverty eradication, etc., have been successfully implemented",""],[1,"18","9","Policy and Mechanism Renovation for a Socialist-Oriented Market Economy","Establish a harmonious institution for a socialist-oriented market economy with focus on policy and mechanism renovation;",""],[1,"62","6","Establishment of Socialist-Oriented Market Economic Institutions","At this stage, it requires a rapid establishment of socialist-oriented market economic institutions with full market principles.",""],[1,"66","1","Market Economy Transition and Market Institution Development","Second, move more strongly into the market economy, execute market principles, systematically formulate all types of markets and socialist-oriented market economic institutions which are suitable to our country's conditions.",""]],"39":[[1,"7","5","National Development Finance Mobilization and Efficient Use","Strengthen the national financial potentials, mobilize and use effectively all financial sources, including of State, non-state sectors, domestic and external resources, for development investment.",""],[1,"7","6","State Financial and Budgetary Management Reform","Reform the mechanism of the State financial and budgetary management to ensure the predominance of Central Budget, promote decentralization of authorities and responsibilities in budget management at all levels and units using the State budget.",""],[1,"7","6","Budget Transparency and State Audit Strengthening","Strengthen the publicity and transparency in the use and management of the State budget, creating significant changes in budget control, enhancing the State's auditing that can help to stop misspending, losses and corruption of State assets.",""],[1,"25","3","Tax Policy and Revenue Mobilization Reform","many mechanisms and policies relating to finance and budget have been continuously improved",""],[1,"61","1","Budgetary Decentralization and Local Authority Reform","Budgetary decentralization, delegation of investment approval authority, land allocation and allotment, etc., continues to facilitate the autonomy of all levels and sectors in their specification of the Party and Government's guidelines and policies.",""],[1,"69","8","On-Time Public Debt Payment","ensuring on-time debt payment,",""],[1,"133","2","State Financial and Budgetary Management Reform","Reform the mechanism of the State financial and budgetary management to ensure consistency in the State budget, the predominance of Central Budget, promote decentralization of authorities and raising responsibilities in budget management at all levels and units using the State budget.",""],[1,"133","2","Budget Transparency and Allocation Reform","Strengthen the publicity and transparency in the use and management of the State budget and funds; renovate the policies for distribution and allocation of finances and budget; eliminate unreasonable subsidy; clearly define the scope and content of the budget to be executed.",""],[1,"133","2","State Audit and Budget Control Strengthening","Create significant changes in budget control, strengthen State auditing in order to prevent losses, misspending and corruption.",""],[1,"133","2","Social Mobilization for Infrastructure and Socio-Cultural Development","Strengthen social mobilization and mobilization of all possible resources of the whole society for the development of infrastructure and socio-cultural life in all possible areas/localities; renovate financial management mechanism of non-productive units; delegate power and responsibility to them in all 3 aspects: implementation of task assignments, organizational structure and financial budget.",""],[1,"133","3","Rational Allocation and Oversight of National Financial Sources","Rationally allocate national financial sources, focusing on key fields; keep the national and government debts at a justifiable level under the State's tight control; use financial sources economically; bring into play the role of the National Assembly and Peoples' Councils at various levels during the allocation and supervision of the State budget expenditure.",""],[1,"133","4","Medium-Term State Budget Planning Reform","Renovate the content, mode and process of doing the estimations of the State budget in the direction of building the medium-term budgetary-financial plan in close links with the implementation of the budgetary financial strategy.",""],[1,"133","4","Output-Based State Budget Management and Evaluation System","Step by step establish the structure of distribution, management and evaluation of the State budget based on output results; widely apply the mechanism of financial self-control for non-productive institutions.",""],[1,"133","4","Budget Deficit Management Reform","Carry out the management of budget deficits corresponding to international practices and gradually reduce the budget deficits rate.",""],[1,"133","8","State Budget Expenditure Reallocation for Development Investment","Continue adjusting the structure of the State budget expenditure to promote the mobilization of funds for development investment in building infrastructure for the industrialization and modernization process.",""],[1,"134","1","Block Grant Budget Allocation Policy","Speed up the policy of block grants in budget allocation for administrative expenditures and staffing; extensively apply the policy to all administrative institutions.",""],[1,"134","1","Phase-Out of Subsidy-Type State Enterprise Expenditures","Gradually reduce and ultimately abolish all expenditures of subsidy nature in the State budget for State enterprises such as tax exemption, debt suspension, debt clearance, or preferential loans.",""],[1,"134","2","State Budget Transparency and Openness Reform","Improve the openness and transparency of State budget in all processes from policy- making, estimation, appraisal to approval, implementation and clearance at all levels.",""],[1,"134","4","Financial Administrative Reform and Budget Management Modernization","Continue completing legislations and regulations on the administrative reform in the field of finance; modernize financial and budget management.",""],[1,"134","4","Financial and Budget Human Resource Development","Build up strong human resources of financial and budget with high qualifications, professional ethics and political correctness.",""],[1,"136","8","Public Finance Reform and Budget Expenditure Review","Study and implement comprehensive solutions of public finance reforms, review budget expenditures.",""],[1,"138","6","Public Finance Law Completion","Complete the Public Finance Law.",""]],"40":[[1,"46","4","Social Sciences and Humanities Research and Survey Programme","Social sciences and humanities have more focus in their research and surveys in order to provide statistics and scientific foundations for policy- making, and guideline formulation for socio-economic development as well as for the preservation and development of our traditions and cultures.",""],[1,"46","4","Natural Sciences Research for Resource Assessment and Biodiversity Protection","Natural sciences have focused their research and surveys on assessing potential natural resources, protecting biodiversity and preventing natural calamities, which creates prerequisites for applied research to serve production and human resource development.",""],[1,"47","9","Baseline Survey and Environmental Data Monitoring","Baseline survey activities have been regularly maintained so as to collect and process data on the natural conditions and resources for better understanding of the current situation and changes of natural resources, which provide scientific bases for developing and adjusting master plans for the years until 2010.",""],[1,"47","9","Periodic Socio-economic Survey Programme","Such surveys are conducted periodically to study the socio-economic features of each region, locality and the whole country, which provides justifications for policy-making and social needs identification.",""],[1,"47","9","Environmental Pollution Reporting and Analysis","These surveys have generated a good number of reports in which environmental data are collected, analyzed and stored; environmental pollution by industrial waste and domestic waste is investigated, and fundamental elements directly or indirectly related to the quality of the soil, water, air environment, or river and marine ecological systems, etc., are studied.",""],[1,"103","5","Natural and Social Resources Information Management System","Develop modern fundamental study in order to ensure that information of natural and social resources and environment is collected, processed and managed in an adequate, accurate and consistent manner.",""],[1,"103","9","National Topographical and Cadastral Mapping Programme","Complete the measuring, drawing and refining topographical maps with basic scale for the whole country and supplement maps with large scale for key economic areas.",""],[1,"104","1","Land Use Planning and Cadastral Modernization","Complete maps for current status of land use, assess quality of soil, complete and modernize cadastral records; develop and implement land use plans for 2006-2010 and orientation towards 2020.",""],[1,"104","2","Water Resources Baseline Survey and Monitoring Programme","Continue to supplement baseline survey data on water resources by taking stock of the current status of water resources, develop watershed maps, conduct comprehensive and monitoring of surface and underground waters.",""],[1,"104","2","Water Resource Assessment and Pollution Projection Strengthening","Strengthen examination, assessment and projection of exploitation and utilization of water resources, water source pollution and factors influencing water resources.",""],[1,"104","3","Geological and Mineral Resource Survey Programme","Conduct baseline survey of geological resources and minerals, conduct a comprehensive assessment of mineral resources including development of geological maps, site geology and hydrological geology of key areas; conduct assessment of minerals at 500m depth, assess the reserves of the identified mines and conduct survey for marine minerals.",""],[1,"104","4","Natural Resource and Renewable Energy Survey Programme","Continue to survey the forests of Central Highlands, marine resources, wind power, geothermal and biological power.",""],[1,"104","5","Environmental Data Collection and Pollution Monitoring System","Collect, process and store environmental data: industrial wastes, scraps, waste water, dust, radioactive substances, chemicals, noise ... , domestic wastes such as water, excreation, garbage ... and basic factors directly or indirectly related to soil, water, air, river or sea environment ... in order to assess the current status and changing patterns of environment in each sector, region and nation-wide.",""],[1,"104","5","Urban and Industrial Pollution Survey Programme","Conduct environmental pollution survey in big cities, highly-populated areas, industrial zones with signs of severe pollution.",""],[1,"104","5","Natural Resource Misuse Assessment Initiative","Assess the inappropriate use of natural resources causing wastage, economic inefficiency and hazards to the environment.",""],[1,"104","6","Natural Resource and Environmental Database Standardization and Updating","Natural resource and environmental database needs to be standardized and updated regularly to become an information network to provide date for socio-economic, national defense and security activities.",""],[1,"104","6","Digital Cadastral Mapping and Water Resource Monitoring","By 2010, the works of measuring for development of cadastral maps, monitoring of exploitation and utilization of water resources and emission into water sources and marine measuring will be conducted with digital technology.",""],[1,"104","8","Fundamental Research Planning and Infrastructure Development","Conduct planning work in management of fundamental study.",""],[1,"104","8","Physical Infrastructure Completion for Fundamental Study Units","Complete the development of physical infrastructure for units conducting fundamental study (stations and centers of hydro-meteorological forecasting, Archives of baseline study data at local levels).",""],[1,"104","9","Baseline Data Development for Planning","Continue development of adequate, accurate, consistent and synchronous baseline data on natural conditions, resources and socio-economic characteristics to serve development and implementation of strategies, master plans and sustainable development plans at local, sectoral and national levels.",""],[1,"104","10","Capital Construction for Survey Station and Geological Team Network","Invest in capital construction in a regular manner to consolidate the network of fundamental survey stations and geological teams of ministries and provinces.",""],[1,"104","11","Water Resources Survey and Planning Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen capacity and physical infrastructure, renew technology to modernize the network of baseline survey implementers, such as: paying attention to survey, assessment and forecasts of water resources, planning of watershed areas, planning and exploitation of water resources.",""],[1,"104","11","Scientific Research and Advanced Technology Application in Water Management","Conduct scientific study and application of advanced technology in water",""],[1,"105","2","Geological and Hydro-Meteorological Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Upgrade","Focus on rehabilitation and upgrade of physical infrastructure of geological teams, hydro- meteorological stations and units.",""],[1,"105","4","Multi-sector Economic Policy for Survey Work Participation","Exercise the multi-sector economic policy to promote socialization and creation of a equal environment for all organizations and individuals to participate in this fundamental survey work.",""]],"41":[[1,"8","6","Agenda 21 Implementation at All Levels","Organize implementation of the Vietnam Strategic Sustainable Development Orientation (Agenda 21) at all levels and in all sectors.",""],[1,"73","8","Integration of National Targeted Programs","Promote integration of national targeted programs and other agricultural and rural development programs, considerably contributing to the promotion of agricultural and rural development.",""],[1,"106","11","Implementation of Vietnam Strategic Sustainable Development Orientation (Agenda 21)","Organize implementation of the Vietnam Strategic Sustainable Development Orientation (Agenda 21) for rapid, stable and sustainable economic growth; adopt a reasonable economic structure to meet the increasing material and spiritual living demand of the people.",""],[1,"107","2","Policy Mechanisms for Integrated Industrialization and Modernization","develop policy mechanisms to ensure close and harmonious linkage between economic, social and environmental aspects in the course of industrialization and modernization of the country.",""],[1,"107","3","Community Sustainable Development Awareness Campaign","Improve awareness of sustainable development among the community for better understanding and implementation.",""],[1,"107","4","Sustainable Development Institutional System Completion","Continue to complete the institutional system on sustainable development; develop investment policy mechanism and mobilise investment resources for sustainable development; raising awareness of all sectors and levels of authority as well as among the community of sustainable development.",""],[1,"107","4","Sustainable Development Investment Policy Mechanism","develop investment policy mechanism and mobilise investment resources for sustainable development; raising awareness of all sectors and levels of authority as well as among the community of sustainable development.",""],[1,"107","4","Sustainable Development Awareness-Raising Campaign","raising awareness of all sectors and levels of authority as well as among the community of sustainable development.",""],[1,"107","5","Agenda 21 Development and Implementation Framework","Organize development and implementation of Agenda 21 at all levels and sectors",""],[1,"107","5","Pilot Sustainable Development Models","Develop and maintain pilot models of sustainable development; strive towards the target of at least 2-3 models in each sector and province.",""],[1,"107","6","Sustainable Development Governance and Coordination Strengthening","Consolidate the organization arrangements of administration agencies from the central to local levels to develop and implement the national, sectoral and local Sustainable Development Programs.",""],[1,"107","6","National and Sub-national Sustainable Development Council Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of the National Sustainable Development Council and promote the establishment of Sustainable Development Councils at sub- national levels to guide, operate and implement sustainable development objectives in the whole country.",""],[1,"107","6","Sub-national Sustainable Development Office Capacity Development","Develop resources and physical infrastructure of Sustainable Development Offices at sub-national levels to meet the demand and fulfill the tasks set out in the Vietnam Strategic Orientation of Sustainable Development.",""],[1,"107","7","Sustainable Development Legal and Institutional Reform","Continue to revise, amend and supplement the current legal document system, complete the institutional system of sustainable development, the system of documents guiding implementation and legal documents.",""],[1,"107","7","Sustainable Development Policy Mechanism Development","Develop policy mechanism on sustainable development to ensure a harmonious combination of all three aspects - economic, social and environmental - in the course of industrialization and modernization.",""],[1,"107","7","Environmental Mainstreaming and Sustainable Development Planning","Attention should be paid to institutions needed for mainstreaming environmental issues into socio-economic development strategy; develop and implement sustainable development plans in the entire country and territories.",""],[1,"107","7","Sustainable Development Policy Research and Database System","Study policies and establish database of sustainable development in Vietnam.",""],[1,"107","8","Financial Institutions Participation in Sustainable Development","Encourage financial institutions to participate in the country's sustainable development.",""],[1,"107","9","Education for Sustainable Development Awareness Programme","Organize education to raise the people's awareness of sustainable development.",""],[1,"107","10","International Cooperation for Sustainable Development and Environmental Protection","Strengthen international cooperation in sustainable development and environmental protection.",""],[1,"107","10","Mobilization of International Assistance for Poverty Reduction","Make full use of international assistance in technical, technological and financial aspects in poverty reduction towards sustainable development.",""]],"42":[[1,"9","3","Primary Health Care and Hospital Service Strengthening","Strengthen and improve public health care at grassroots level, preventive healthcare, general hospitals in provinces and districts, regional health centers, intensive healthcare units on the basis of facilitating social participation.",""],[1,"9","3","Epidemic and Disease Surveillance and Control Capacity Enhancement","Improve the capacity to monitor, detect and control epidemics and diseases, especially HIV/AIDS and other emerging diseases.",""],[1,"14","9","Health Care Network Strengthening and Upgrading","Health care receives more attention, medical network is strengthened and upgraded.",""],[1,"14","9","Preventive Medical Activities Enhancement","Preventive medical activities are enhanced;",""],[1,"93","12","Health System Development Planning and Epidemic Control Capacity Strengthening","Improve and complete people's healthcare system: Establish and well perform the planning for medical system development to 2010 and subsequent years.",""],[1,"94","1","Disease Prevention and Early Warning Measures","Timely foresee and take measures to prevent diseases in order to minimize their negative effects on people's health due to the change of lifestyle, environment and working conditions in the process of industrialization and modernization.",""],[1,"95","4","Preventive and Specialized Health System Development","The State focuses on the development of preventive medical system, grassroots health care, hi-tech health care and highly specialized healthcare centers in the Central, regional and provincial hospitals and other centers which are not likely to sell services and attract investment from private investors.",""],[1,"95","4","Provincial Epidemic Control and Prevention Centers","Primary priorities should be given to provincial preventive medicine centers to intensify the control, supervision and prevention of epidemics like malaria, goiter, tuberculosis, leprosy and other emerging dangerous diseases; support the vaccine and biopharmaceutical industries.",""],[1,"95","4","Pharmacy and Vaccine Testing Capacity Improvement","Improve the capacity of pharmacy and vaccine testing.",""]],"43":[[1,"9","4","Social Problem Prevention and Control Measures","Prevent and move forwards to stop social problems: drug addiction, prostitution, and children and women trafficking ...",""],[1,"57","5","Sound Commune and Ward Social Problem Prevention Initiative","The movement of building sound communes and wards free from social problems has been widely replicated.",""],[1,"57","5","Drug Trafficking and Addiction Prevention Measures","Many localities have devised effective solutions to prevent drug trafficking and addiction, sex work and stop any unsound cultural activities.",""],[1,"57","5","Drug Addiction Treatment and Post-Treatment Management","Many effective modes of treatments for drug addicts have been multiplied, together with diversified modes and management of addicts after treatment.",""],[1,"57","5","Drug Treatment Infrastructure Strengthening","Materials and facilities of drug treatment have initially intensified, leading to decreased rate of resumed addiction in localities.",""],[1,"57","5","Professional Security Operations Against Drug Crime","Professional security force against drug criminals have timely eliminated a number of drug-use places and stopped several big drug trafficking cases, contributing to the restriction of drug addiction and other social problems.",""],[1,"103","1","Crime-Free and Strong Commune and Ward Building Movement","Continue to speed up the work of building crime-free and strong communes and wards without social problems; in association with the movement of \"All the people strive together for building up cultural life in their neighborhood\".",""],[1,"103","2","Drug Crime and Trafficking Control Measures","Take strong measures to strictly control and then reduce drug related crimes, sex work, women and children trafficking.",""],[1,"103","2","Measures to Reduce Social Disease Transmission","at the same time take measures to reduce the adverse impacts of social disease transmission.",""],[1,"103","2","Study and Replicate Local and International Lessons","Study, and learn from the lessons/experience of localities domestically and internationally and then widely apply them to our situations.",""],[1,"103","3","Grassroots Crime Prevention Coordination","Intensity the roles of grassroots authorities, public security and judicial branches, Youth League, Women Union and other social organizations in the prevention of drug-related crimes, sex work, and women and children trafficking right at the communes or wards.",""],[1,"103","4","Drug Addict Detoxification Center Expansion","Improve material facilities with all sources to build drug-addict detoxication centers.",""],[1,"103","4","Compulsory and Voluntary Drug Detoxification Placement","Send most of the drug addicts in big cities and key provinces to compulsory and voluntary detoxication centers.",""],[1,"103","4","Post-Detoxification Monitoring and Reintegration Support","Strictly control them after detoxication, attach responsibilities of families and local authorities to the control and creation of jobs for these people.",""]],"44":[[1,"10","1","General Power in External Relations Policy","Create successfully general power in external relation policy to consolidate peace and stability, to enhance socio-economic development, raising competitiveness internally and internationally, timely and effectively deal with emerging international problems.",""],[1,"40","3","ODA Partnership and Harmonization Mechanism","The relations between Vietnam and donors have been established on the basis of partnership, with more emphasis on the ownership of the ODA recipients through the harmonization of ODA processes and procedures.",""],[1,"62","2","External Resource Mobilization Strategy","To use effectively external resources, we must have an appropriate strategy and sound business environment, first and foremost a consistent institutional and policy system and an effective, efficient and transparent administration system.",""]],"45":[[1,"2","18","Law Enforcement Capacity and Effectiveness Improvement","Improve capacity and effectiveness of law enforcement",""],[1,"10","2","Legal System Completion and Legislative Quality Reform","Promptly complete and ensure the consistency of legal system to satisfy the needs of building a Socialist Legitimate State.",""],[1,"10","2","Regulatory Clarity and Transparency Improvement","Continue reform and enhancing quality of legislation, ensure that legal regulations are specific, clear and transparent in order to reduce gradually promulgation of directive or sub-legal documents.",""],[1,"10","2","Legal Compliance Inspection and Monitoring Mechanism","Organize on the effective and frequent basis the implementation of checking, inspection and monitoring in promulgating detail and directive document to realize laws, ordinances and resolutions; respect laws in all social and economic activities.",""],[1,"10","4","Justice Reform and Judicial Institutions Strengthening","Continue the strategy of justice reform, complete organization and operations of inspectorates, procuracies, courts, judgment execution organizations, and justice support organizations; effectively fight against all kinds of crimes, especially organizational crimes, creating sound and safe conditions for social and economic development.",""],[1,"10","5","Judicial Jurisdiction Expansion and Court Reorganization","Organize properly the implementation of raising jurisdiction for district level courts and organize regional levels courts as indicated in the Strategy for Justice Reform.",""],[1,"140","5","Legal and Justice Sector Reform and Institutional Strengthening","Continue the strategy of legal reform, complete organization and operation of inspectorates and procuracies, courts, executors, legal support organizations, ... to fight effectively against crimes, especially organizational crimes, to create a sound environment for economic growth.",""],[1,"140","6","District Court Power Improvement","Rationally organize the power improvement for district level courts in accordance with organization of regional level courts as said in the legal reform strategy.",""]],"46":[[1,"7","1","Fundamental Renewal of Public Service Management and Delivery","Fundamental renewal of the management mechanism and methods of public service provision is an important breakthrough to enhance the socialization of cultural and social sectors.",""],[1,"10","3","Administrative Reform and Civil Service Discipline Programme","Push up administration reform; realize democracy in all sectors.",""],[1,"18","9","Public Administrative Reform","renovation of the apparatus and operational practices of the political system with focus on the public administrative reform.",""],[1,"60","8","Clarification of State Administrative Agency Mandates and Functions","The mandates and functions of State administrative agencies from Government, Ministries, Central branches to local authorities continue to be clarified so as to eliminate or avoid overlaps and parallels in terms of functions and duties among institutions.",""],[1,"61","2","Administrative Procedure Simplification and One-Stop Shop Reform","The institutional reform has helped simplify and streamline administrative procedures by applying the \"one-stop shop\", \"one stamp\", \"on-site stop shop\" and removing cumbersome formalities which have seriously bothered people so far.",""],[1,"61","2","Public Administration Reform Capacity Improvement","Positive improvement has been made in the quality and capacity of State officials and public servants.",""],[1,"62","7","Civil Service Recruitment and Personnel Accountability Reform","It is necessary to recruit righteous staff, civil servants to serve public work; clear assignment to leaders, organizations and units with responsibility and power, including in term of organization and personnel; at the same time, responsibility of leaders and staff should be raised when duties and tasks are not met, fails, delay, etc.",""],[1,"66","6","Administrative Reform and Anti-Corruption Drive","enhance democracy, use the national solidarity as the driving force and the decisive factor in improving the efficiency of a socialist State ruled by law, creating a comprehensive and significant change in administrative reform, pushing back bureaucracy, corruption, waste.",""],[1,"141","1","Administrative System Modernization","Build the administrative system to be professional and modern.",""],[1,"141","2","Civil Service Management Reform","Renew the management of cadres and civil servants to meet the changing demand of socio- economic development process.",""],[1,"141","3","Salary Reform for Civil Service Human Resources","Continue salary reform, regarding salary as the direct investment in human resources, contributing to improvement of quality of cadres and civil servants and civil service.",""],[1,"141","4","Cadre and Civil Servant Training Reform","Enhance training for cadres and civil servants, develop and implement plans of training cadres and civil servants in the state administration system in different fields: cadres and civil servants engaged in advisory work for policy formulation; administrative and operational cadres and civil servants and local cadres and staff.",""],[1,"141","5","Civil Service Ethics and Responsibility Strengthening","strengthen education of cadres and civil servants on responsibility and devotion to the work.",""],[1,"141","5","Professional Ethical Standards for Civil Servants","Develop professional ethical standards for cadres and civil servants.",""],[1,"141","5","Civil Service Regulations and Open Administration Reform","Issue and strictly implement civil service regulations linked with implementation of democracy regulation in the state administration organizations.",""]],"47":[[1,"10","6","Anti-Corruption Law Implementation and Enforcement Measures","Organize the implementation of the Law on Economical Practices and Prevention of Wasteful Spending and the Law on Corruption Prevention.",""],[1,"10","9","Legislative Oversight of Resolution Implementation","The Standing Committee of the National Assembly, Council for Ethnics, Committees of National Assembly, Delegations of National Assembly Deputies, National Assembly Deputies, People Councils and People Council's Members of all levels should heighten their responsibility to monitor the implementation of this Resolution.",""],[1,"144","2","Economical Practices and Anti-Corruption Implementation","Intensify economical practices, prevent wasteful spending, and strengthen the fight against bureaucracy and corruption in the State apparatus.",""],[1,"144","3","Public Sector Anti-Corruption and Integrity Reform","Generate significant changes in the combat against corruption, trouble-making, negligence and irresponsibility of State officials and public servants.",""]],"48":[[1,"10","8","Action Plan for Five-Year Socio-Economic Development Plan Implementation","The Government is to prepare an action plan, which is submitted to the National Assembly for approval, on detail annual plans; guiding sectors, levels to proactively implement and to achieve goals, targets and measures of the Five-year Socio-Economic Development Plan 2006-2010.",""],[1,"11","1","Civic Monitoring and Mobilization for Socio-Economic Plan Implementation","National Fatherland Front and its member organizations are to monitor and mobilize all people in promoting democracy, proactive implementation of the socio-economic development plan.",""],[1,"11","2","National Mobilization for Comprehensive Reform and Five-Year Plan Implementation","The National Assembly calls upon entire Vietnamese people, civil servants, and soldiers throughout the country and Vietnamese people who live abroad to heighten patriotic loves, promote proactiveness, and creativeness, to overcome every difficulties and challenges, to make contributions to the task of reforming comprehensively, achieving goals, targets of the Five-year Socio-economic Development Plan 2006-2010.",""],[1,"73","9","Grassroots Democracy and Rural Social Development Initiative","Promote the Democracy at grass roots level, in which democracy should go together with building modern culture, fighting against social problems in rural areas; maintain and develop sound and good traditional culture of different ethnic groups.",""],[1,"141","1","Civil Society Participation in State and Social Management","Bring into play the diverse forms and modes of operation of the mass organizations and non-governmental organizations engaged in State and social management; prevent the trend of being too administrative in public organizations.",""],[1,"144","4","Civil Society Participation in Economic Management and Monitoring","Encourage social organizations, mass organizations and civil societies to engage in managing and monitoring some public fields: attract and encourage the engagement of social organizations, mass organizations and non-governmental organizations in economic development and management.",""],[1,"144","4","Diversification of Participation in Economic Management","At the same time, diversify the modes of participation in economic management of various economic subjects such as enterprises, cooperatives, associations of producers, consumers' societies, etc.",""],[1,"147","14","Transparent, Responsible, and Participatory Government Reform","Improve people's access to a transparent, responsible and participatory government;",""]],"49":[[1,"79","3","High-Quality Tourism Services Development","strongly developing high quality tourism services and creating many more jobs.",""],[1,"80","4","Tourism Product Quality and Infrastructure Improvement","Continue attracting investment in improving tourism product quality and tourism infrastructure, especially in key regions.",""],[1,"80","4","Cross-Sector Tourism Coordination and Product Diversification","Take advantage of and coordinate with investment programs of other sectors to increase the quality and efficiency of tourism, exploit the potentials of ecological tourism and the advantages of coastal holiday resorts, historical and cultural tourist attractions.",""],[1,"80","4","Tourism Capacity Building Initiative","Invest in capacity building in order to create highly competitive tourism products.",""],[1,"80","5","Tourism Information Dissemination and Overseas Promotion Campaign","Boost information dissemination and advertisement about tourism, especially promotion of Vietnamese tourism overseas.",""]],"50":[[1,"82","5","Securities Market Legal and Regulatory Framework Reform","Rapidly complete the legal framework and policies for operating and developing the stock market.",""],[1,"82","6","Foreign Investment and Stock Market Development Measures","Expand the right of foreign investors in capital contribution or buying stocks.",""],[1,"82","7","Stock Market Information, Training, and Awareness Programme","Push up activities of Stock Association, especially in the fields of information supply, training and awareness improvement of investors and society in terms of stocks and stock markets.",""],[1,"82","7","Dedicated Stock Market Television Channel or Programme","Study and build a separate television channel or program for stock markets.",""],[1,"139","6","Financial Market Development and Securities Market Expansion","Develop the financial market along the line of complete structure, wide and safe operating scale and scope, close management and supervision, protection of legitimate interests of all investors, and active integration into the international financial market.",""],[1,"139","6","Securities Market Development for Capital Mobilization","Vigorously develop the securities market, progressively making it really a main capital mobilization channel for development investment.",""],[1,"139","6","Enterprise Equity Listing and Capital Raising Reform","Enterprises of all economic sectors should gradually post up a notice of shares and mobilize capital through the securities market.",""],[1,"139","7","Monetary and Financial Market Linkage Strengthening","Intensify the accomplishment of monetary markets; make healthy short-term capital transactions and dealings of valuable documents in the market; promote linkages between monetary and financial markets in policy planning, operation mechanism, management control, governance and operation supervision.",""]],"51":[[1,"83","1","Export Business Development and Export Structure Upgrade","Develop the export business with high and stable growth rate as a momentum for GDP growth.",""],[1,"84","2","Export Diversification for Processed and Manufactured Goods","it is necessary to expand the export of new items such as shipbuilding, mechanical and electric products, potential goods like arts and handicraft products, processed food, wooden products, cosmetics and common chemicals, plastic products, etc.",""],[1,"85","7","Competitiveness and Export Efficiency Improvement Measures","Improve the competitiveness, efficiency and quality of goods and services; step by step increase the export efficiency.",""],[1,"85","7","Trademark Solutions for Goods Competitiveness","Find solutions for the matter of trademarks to enhance the competitiveness of goods.",""],[1,"85","8","Trade Promotion and Export Market Diversification","Develop the market based on rapidly developed trade promotion, materializing international economic integration commitments: actively expand the markets, multi- lateralize and diversify relations with partners; make use of all conditions to increase export into all available markets, and at the same time boost the export into markets with low shares but high purchasing power; and penetrate into new markets.",""],[1,"85","9","Trademark Registration Support for Enterprises","Guide and support enterprises to make and register trademarks.",""],[1,"85","9","Export Market Promotion and Intelligence Support","Focus on advertising and promoting markets.",""],[1,"85","9","Market Information and Export Forecasting System","Pay attention to gathering information, forecasting and analyzing the market, and the price tendency of main exports.",""],[1,"85","9","Global Distribution Network Customer Base Development","Build a stable network of customers, especially big customers as a base for penetrating into the global distribution network.",""],[1,"85","10","Investment Environment Improvement for Exported Goods Production and Processing","Focus on improving the investment environment to attract investment, especially in the field of producing and processing exported goods.",""],[1,"85","10","State-Association-Business Coordination Strengthening","Strengthen the relationship between State administration agencies - goods associations - enterprises.",""],[1,"85","11","Import and Export Policy Reform","Complete mechanism and policies on import and export, gradually improve export efficiency through the completion of the tax and fee system in the orientation of encouraging export and exported goods production, restricting import, encouraging the use of home-made materials, raw materials and manufactured products for production in general and exported goods production in particular.",""],[1,"85","11","New Import Control Tools","Continue implementing some new import controlling tools consistent with WTO regulations.",""],[1,"86","5","Export Promotion and Import Management Measures","Take strong measures to boost export and take initiative in import, limit excessive import.",""],[1,"86","5","Export Structure Diversification and Market Expansion","Facilitate the shift of export structure; create stable markets for exports by strengthening market shares in traditional markets and exploiting potential ones.",""],[1,"86","5","Enterprise Consultation and Integration Support","Take consultative measures and help enterprises solve problems arising from integration but gradually phase out irrational protectionism.",""]],"52":[[1,"94","4","Pharmaceutical Industry Development and Domestic Production Expansion","Strongly develop pharmaceutical industry, and improve domestic production capacity.",""],[1,"94","4","Vaccine and Biopharmaceutical Research and Production Programme","Promote research and production of vaccines and biopharmaceutical products.",""],[1,"94","4","Medicinal Raw-Material Supply Area Development Plan","Plan and develop raw-material-supply areas for medicine production.",""],[1,"94","4","Pharmaceutical Transport, Distribution, and Supply Network Reinforcement","Reinforce the network for transportation, distribution and supply of pharmacies in order to stabilize the pharmaceutical market.",""]],"53":[[1,"98","7","Continuation of Program 135 for Extremely Disadvantaged Communes","Continue the implementation of the Program on Socio-economic Development of extremely disadvantaged communes (Program 135) in the 2006-2010 period, basically ensure that all communes have essential public works.",""],[1,"98","7","Rural Infrastructure and Settlement Planning for Disadvantaged Communes","Improve infrastructures, communal cluster's centers, plan and re-locate residential areas, promote the development of agriculture and forestry.",""],[1,"98","8","Land and Forest Allocation for Ethnic and Mountainous Areas","Well perform the allocation of land and forest to individuals, households and organizations in ethnic and mountainous areas, especially to households of ethnic minorities.",""],[1,"98","8","Support Policy for Cultivation Land, Housing, and Clean Water","Effectively carry out the assistance policy on cultivation land, residential land, housing, and clean water for poor ethnic minority people.",""],[1,"99","1","Sedentary Cultivation and Settlement Project","Well complete the project of sedentary cultivation and settlement, reduce spontaneous migration, stabilize production, improve the living standards of ethnic minority people in conformity to their traditional practices on the basis of population planning which establishes concentrated residential clusters, communal clusters, townships, together with the provision of infrastructure to those establishments such as roads, water and electricity supply, information, markets.",""],[1,"111","8","Clean Water Supply Investment","Invest to ensure clean water supply for people's life and production.",""],[1,"111","8","Irrigation Works Construction Programme","Build new irrigation works in Ha Giang, Tuyen Quang, Cao Bang, Lang Son, Lao Cai, Son La, etc.",""],[1,"111","8","Power Transmission Grid Upgrading","Ensure the quality of the power transmission grids; develop modern and effective post and telecommunication network to meet the requirements of socio-economic development.",""],[1,"111","8","Modern Postal and Telecommunications Network Development","Ensure the quality of the power transmission grids; develop modern and effective post and telecommunication network to meet the requirements of socio-economic development.",""],[1,"111","9","Urban Systems and Rural Settlement Modernization","Develop urban systems and master plans of living areas towards modernizing rural areas.",""],[1,"111","9","Regional Town Development and Urbanization Programme","Develop towns in association with the development of the region's industrial and economic centers, especially in cities like Viet Tri, Thai Nguyen, Yen Bai, Lang Son, Dien Bien Phu; build up Lao Cai city and urbanize towns and townships in the region.",""],[1,"111","9","New Tam Duong Town Construction","Prioritize the construction of new Tam Duong town.",""],[1,"111","9","Resettlement and Town Cluster Development for Hydropower Projects","Develop town clusters together with the relocation of people when building Son La and Tuyen Quang Hydropower plants.",""],[1,"111","9","Border Commune Living Stabilization Programme","Complete the living stabilization in communes along Vietnam-China and Vietnam-Laos borders, ensuring production and life stability for people therein.",""],[1,"112","2","Commune Postal-Cultural and Village Community Cultural Center Development","Continue to invest in building commune postal-cultural centers, village community cultural centers, building radio broadcasting stations, and television repeaters for communes outside the coverage of Vietnam central radio and television stations, increase broadcasting time in ethnic minority languages.",""],[1,"112","3","Primary Healthcare Quality Improvement","Improve the quality of primary healthcare for people, especially ethnic minorities.",""],[1,"112","3","Commune Doctor Availability Expansion","Strive for the availability of doctors in 60-70% of communes by 2010.",""],[1,"112","3","Hospital Modernization and Regional Healthcare Center Development","Modernize clinical facilities for provincial and district hospitals and establish regional healthcare centers in Thai Nguyen for the Northeast and in Son La for the Northwest.",""],[1,"112","3","Detoxification and Social Reintegration Centers","Assist the investment in building social centers of detoxification, caring and training drug addicts and sex workers back to normal life.",""],[1,"112","4","Residential Land, Production Land, and Clean Water Support for Poor Ethnic Minority People","Properly implement policies of allocating residential land, production land and providing clean water to poor ethnic minority people with an aim to stabilizing their life.",""],[1,"112","5","University Upgrading and Expansion Programme","Invest and upgrade the following universities: Tay Bac University, Thai Nguyen University, Hung Vuong University (in Phu Tho);",""],[1,"112","5","Vocational Training School Expansion for Rural and Ethnic Minority Youth","strengthen and open more vocational training schools, especially for providing vocational training for ethnic minority youths and rural laborers to create local jobs.",""]],"54":[[1,"100","3","Implementation of the National Strategy for the Advancement of Vietnamese Women","Organize the good implementation of the National Strategy for the Advancement of Vietnamese Women to 2010.",""],[1,"100","5","Gender Mainstreaming in Policies and Development Programs","Effectively mainstream gender issues into policies, national action programs, and programs on socio-economic development of all levels and sectors.",""],[1,"100","5","Gender Equality Awareness and Institutional Responsibility Strengthening","Intensify the roles and responsibilities of Ministries, sectors and local authorities in raising people's awareness of gender equality.",""],[1,"100","5","Coordination for Gender Equality Model Implementation","Coordinate Ministries, sectors and local authorities in the introduction and implementation of good models of gender equality.",""],[1,"100","7","Gender Equality Awareness and Anti-Discrimination Campaign","Promote propagandizing on mass media and by other means of communication to improve people's awareness of gender equality, targeted especially to women and children in rural, remote and hinterlands, and ethnic minority areas to help them protect their own rights.",""],[1,"100","7","Implementation of International Conventions on Women's Rights","Well implement international conventions, eliminate all forms of discrimination against women, fight against discrimination and maltreatment to women and children.",""],[1,"100","8","Women’s Advancement Efficiency and Funding Initiative","Improve efficiency, invest labors and fund in activities for the advancement of women nationwide; intensify the inspection and supervision of the implementation of action plans for the advancement of women; intensify international cooperation for the advancement of women.",""],[1,"101","4","Women's Participation and Gender Equality in Local Planning and Governance","Facilitate women's participation in meetings and planning, implementing and supervising programs and projects in villages, communes and at all levels.",""],[1,"101","4","Equal Pay and Incentives Policy for Female Staff","Check all policies on female staff to ensure that they are equal to men in terms of remuneration and incentives.",""],[1,"101","4","Gender Mainstreaming in Political and Administrative Training","Integrate gender issues into programs on political and administrative training at all levels.",""],[1,"101","5","Women's Rights Legal Framework Completion","completing laws and legal documents for the implementation and protection of women's rights and interests.",""],[1,"101","5","Women's Legal Awareness and Access Programme","Improve women's awareness and access to the use of legal instruments.",""],[1,"101","5","Institutional Capacity Building for Women's Advancement","Improve the capacity of the administrative system and social organizations in order to successfully implement policies and strategies for the advancement of women and effectively protect their rights and interests.",""],[1,"101","5","Women's Land Rights and Local Decision-Making Inclusion","Improve women's rights in land use rights certificates and increase their roles in local decision-making.",""],[1,"101","6","Gender Equality Support Policy for Ethnic Minority People and Single Women","Implement support policy to ensure gender equality among ethnic minority people and single women.",""],[1,"145","9","Increase Female Representation in Elective Agencies","Increase the number of female delegates in elective agencies at all levels;",""],[1,"145","10","Increase Women Staff Representation in Public Agencies and Enterprises","Increase by 3-5% of women staff in agencies and sectors (including ministries, central offices, enterprises) at all levels over the next 10 years;",""],[1,"145","11","Joint Spousal Land-Use Right Registration","Execute the regulation on entering names of both husband and wife in the land-use right certificate;",""],[1,"145","12","Domestic Violence Vulnerability Reduction","Reduce women's vulnerability to domestic violence.",""],[1,"147","8","Income Improvement Support for Poor Households Headed by Women","Improve the income situation of the poor, especially poor households headed by women;",""]],"55":[[1,"103","8","Hydro-Meteorological Data Collection and Forecasting System","Survey, collect and process hydro-meteorological data of the country and each region to assess the change patterns and provide long and short-term and seasonal hydro- meteorological forecasts to serve economic sectors, especially agriculture production.",""],[1,"103","8","Natural Disaster Forecasting Service","Provide timely forecasts of natural disasters such as earthquake, typhoons and floods.",""],[1,"105","1","Hydro-Meteorological Monitoring Modernization","modernize the system of hydro-meteorological monitoring, analyzing and forecasting to catch up with the advanced countries in the region to serve the people's life and socio-economic development.",""],[1,"120","9","Anti-Flood Border Defense Infrastructure Investment","Focus on anti-flood investment for border posts, district- level military headquarters, defense system, patrol routes and the border.",""],[1,"120","9","Rapid Reaction Force Development for Emergencies","Develop military forces and quick reaction forces to deal with emergency situations (flood, forest fire, etc).",""],[1,"126","2","Research Center Investment and Baseline Survey Programme","Increase investments in research centers to conduct baseline surveys of natural resources and natural conditions; invest in the improvement of the quality of hydrometeorology and natural disaster warning systems and develop plans for natural disaster control and relief.",""]],"56":[[1,"127","7","One-Stop Shop Business Facilitation Reform","Continue improving supportive environment to provide favorable conditions for enterprises of different types to develop; focus on the development and implementation of \"one-stop shop\" procedures, review and reduce licensing procedures, time and cost for all domestic and foreign investors to participate in Vietnam market; remove limitations of investment and labor scales; remove discrimination in terms of access to opportunities, resources and market information.",""],[1,"127","7","Local Resource Mobilization Mechanism","Provide appropriate mechanisms to attract local resources, making full use of their advantages.",""],[1,"128","8","Implementation Guidelines for Construction and Investment Laws","Complete legal documents and guidelines for the implementation of Construction Law and Law on Investment passed by the National Assembly.",""],[1,"128","8","Investment Resource Management Regulations","the government will issue legal documents and guidelines to implement regulations on the management of investment resources in the direction of providing favorable conditions to mobilize the most possible investment resources in the society.",""],[1,"128","8","Investment Management Reform","Also, tackle with shortcomings and problems in the existing investment management to effectively utilize the investments for essential purposes as planned to avoid loss and waste.",""],[1,"128","8","Planning Legal Framework Establishment","Quickly establish a legal framework for planning work to ensure that planning is one step ahead, serving as the basis for implementation of investment projects.",""],[1,"128","9","Community Planning Supervision and Inspection Strengthening","Enhance the community supervision in regard to planning work, ensure publicity of plans, strengthen inspection and examination of construction management and land use plans in selected provinces.",""],[1,"128","10","Investment Management Decentralization Reform","The investment management regulations submitted to the Government for approval will continue to decentralize investment management responsibilities to conform to",""],[1,"129","1","Administrative Reform for Investment Procedure Simplification","requirements of administrative reforms, to increase the efficiency of State management, and to simplify investment procedures.",""],[1,"129","1","Decentralization of Investment Management","Besides the decentralization of investment management, it is necessary to identify responsibilities of institutions and individuals to increase their liability involved in investment activities.",""],[1,"129","2","Consultancy Standards and Investment Procedure Reform","Provide standards for consultant companies, entrepreneurs to ensure independence and objectiveness of consultancy services, remove the existing \"closed\" procedures in investment and construction.",""],[1,"129","3","Investment Process Governance and Compliance Framework","The Government is to have comprehensive control by providing legal frameworks, setting standards and criteria for investment as well as guidelines for the implementation, evaluation and monitoring of the whole investment process.",""],[1,"129","4","Management Staff Education and Professional Training","Strengthen education and provide professional training for management staff, especially knowledge related to investment and construction management.",""],[1,"129","4","Ethics Education for Construction Investment Staff and Workers","Improve professional awareness and ethics; strengthen education of ethics for staff and workers in construction investment.",""],[1,"129","4","Party Organization Role in Investment Management","Improve the role of party's organizations in operational arrangements and investment management from the planning to the implementation in investment.",""],[1,"142","3","Enterprise Cost Reduction and Administrative Simplification Measures","Amend mechanisms and policies on charges to minimize input costs for enterprises, especially the costs which enterprises are unable to adjust on their own (electricity, water, telecommunications, aviation transport, marine shipping, etc.) Eliminate illegitimate charges in the fields of transport, customs, etc., while encouraging the diversification of supporting services.",""],[1,"142","3","Unified Enterprise Accounting Standards System","Issue the complete common accounting standard system for all types of enterprises.",""],[1,"142","3","Single Business Registration, Taxation, and Customs Code","Use a single code for the three purposes of business registration, taxation and customs for all types of enterprises.",""],[1,"142","3","Online Business Registration Expansion","Widely develop the application of e-business registration through the web.",""]],"57":[[1,"137","7","Institutional Development and Improvement","Develop and improve institutions",""],[1,"137","8","Market Economy and State Administration Institutional Reform","Focus on improvement of institutions in some types of market, such as commodity and service markets, real estate, labor, finance and technologies; conduct institutional reforms in organizations and operations of the administration system; institutions between the government and the people.",""],[1,"137","8","Business-State Management Authority Reform","Continue the institutional reform of state management authority in relation with the business.",""],[1,"137","9","Renewal of Legal Normative Document Preparation and Promulgation Process","Renew the process of preparation and promulgation of legal normative documents",""],[1,"137","10","Legal System Completion and Legislative Reform Programme","Quickly complete and ensure the consistency of the legal system to meet the requirements of building a law-based socialist government.",""],[1,"137","11","Strict Law Enforcement by State Agencies","Ensure strict enforcement of laws by state agencies, cadres and civil servants",""],[1,"138","2","Legal Economic System Reform","Continue building and perfecting the laws on ownership with a view to institutionalizing the market economy development policies with different kinds of ownership forms and economic sectors.",""],[1,"138","4","Planning Law Completion","Complete the law on planning in the socialist-oriented market economy.",""],[1,"138","7","Harmonious Legal System for Economic-Technical Sectors","Build a harmonious legal system on economic-technical sectors (construction, electricity, posts and telecommunications, food security, veterinary, fishery, etc), which represents the rules, conditions and economic-technical standards related to sectoral development and management.",""]],"58":[[1,"78","10","Public Service Delivery Mechanism Reform","Basically renovate management mechanism and distribution methods of public services.",""],[1,"79","6","Public Service Management Mechanism Reform","Fundamental renewal of the management mechanism and methods of public service8 provision is an important breakthrough to enhance the socialization of cultural and social sectors.",""],[1,"79","8","Public Service Supplier Operating Mechanism Reform","It is important to renew the operation mechanism of public service suppliers to ensure greater autonomy and self-accountability in task implementation, personnel management and in independent accounting and cost recovery without reliance on the state subsidy.",""],[1,"79","9","Public Service Delivery Reform","changes in methods of supplying these services need to be performed actively and consistently with a synchronous plan and an appropriate roadmap.",""]],"59":[[1,"86","6","Education and Training Reform and Modernization","Continue the systematic and comprehensive reform, standardization and modernization of education and training, broaden international cooperation, improve the quality of human resource training to meet the demands of the industrialization and modernization process, and approach to the advanced education level of the region and the world.",""],[1,"86","7","Nursery School Expansion in Residential Areas","Boost the development of nursery schools in all residential areas, especially in rural and disadvantaged areas;",""],[1,"86","7","Primary Education Universalization Strengthening","strengthen and improve the results of primary educational universalization, implement the universalization for children of the right ages and ensure the comprehensive quality;",""],[1,"86","7","Lower and Upper Secondary Universalization Programme","fulfill the lower secondary universalization program by 2010 and move on to upper secondary universalization where possible.",""],[1,"145","4","Primary Education Quality Improvement and Extended Learning Hours","Complete the improvement of primary education quality and increase the number of all-day learning hours at primary level by 2010;",""]],"60":[[1,"100","4","Women’s Access to Health Care Services","Implement gender equality in health care; ensure that women can access to healthcare services.",""],[1,"101","2","Women's Health and Family Planning Services Improvement","Improve women's health through improved awareness and behavioral changes in providing medical and family planning services.",""],[1,"101","2","Grassroots Reproductive Health Counseling and Contraceptive Promotion","Strengthen the medical systems at the grassroots, including the provision of counseling about reproductive health and family planning, take positive measures to encourage the use of various contraceptive methods.",""],[1,"101","2","Poor Women's Access to Healthcare Services","Facilitate poor women's access to healthcare services.",""],[1,"101","2","Maternal Care Quality Improvement","Improve the quality of prepartum, partum and postpartum services.",""],[1,"101","2","HIV/AIDS and Reproductive Tract Infection Prevention Measures","Take measures to reduce the transmission of HIV/AIDS and other reproductive tract infection diseases.",""],[1,"101","2","Occupational Disease Record and Database System","Establish the record system and database of occupational diseases.",""],[1,"101","2","Health Worker Skills and Service Quality Improvement","Improve professional skills and knowledge of the medical staff and service quality at women and children's health care facilities.",""],[1,"146","3","Postpartum Maternal Health Improvement","Improve mother's postpartum health.",""]],"61":[[1,"120","8","River Waste Control Measures","Strictly control waste from people living on rivers.",""],[1,"125","1","Urban and Rural Water Supply System Upgrading","Develop and modernize infrastructure systems in urban areas, improve the water supply systems and provide sufficient clean water for cities and industrial parks.",""],[1,"125","1","Rural Clean Water Supply Expansion","Continue to upgrade and build the clean water supply systems in rural areas, especially in the Mekong Delta and mountainous areas.",""],[1,"125","1","Drainage, Sewage, and Solid Waste Treatment Improvement","Basically improve the drainage system, sewage treatment and solid waste treatment in special urban areas, level-1 and level-2 cities, industrial zones and a number of urban centers, trade villages and residential areas which are being heavily polluted.",""],[1,"127","3","Provincial Drainage and Environmental Sanitation Projects","Focus on the construction of provincial-level projects for drainage systems and environment sanitation.",""],[1,"127","3","Modern Sewage and Solid Waste Treatment Upgrade","In big cities and industrial parks, gradually apply modern technology to sewage and solid waste treatment (including hazardous medical and industrial waste), and support rural people to construct hygienic latrines and sanitation works.",""],[1,"127","3","Rural Hygienic Latrine and Sanitation Support","In big cities and industrial parks, gradually apply modern technology to sewage and solid waste treatment (including hazardous medical and industrial waste), and support rural people to construct hygienic latrines and sanitation works.",""],[1,"127","4","Urban and Industrial Waste Treatment Investment","Invest in the development of treatment of solid waste and waste water in cities, industrial parks, tourist centers and hospitals.",""],[1,"127","4","Integrated Solid Waste Collection and Hazardous Waste Treatment System","Increase solid waste treatment in which recycle and reuse prevail, reduce landfills, construct inter-provincial treatment facilities for hazardous waste, invest more in the provision of facilities for waste collection, transportation and treatment of solid waste.",""],[1,"146","9","Urban Wastewater and Drainage System Upgrade","Basically complete the improvement and upgrade of waste water and rain-water drainage systems in urban areas, industrial zones and export processing zones;",""]],"62":[[1,"12","15","Job Creation and Labor Supplementation Initiative","Job creation and supplementation for about 7.5 million laborers, as planned.",""],[1,"67","6","Job Creation Programme","In 5 years, create jobs for over 8 million laborers, i.e. an average of over 1.6 million per annum, 50% of whom are women",""],[1,"90","7","State Investment and Social Mobilization for Job Creation","State investment and social mobilization are prioritized to job creation.",""],[1,"90","7","Labor Force Quality and Efficiency Improvement","Improve the quality and efficiency of labor force.",""],[1,"90","7","Labor Structural Shift Policy","Continue labor structural shift with reduction of agriculture, forestry and fishery labor to 50% in 2010, increase of industry and construction labor to at least 23 - 24% and increase service-commerce labor to at least 26 - 27 %.",""],[1,"139","4","Comprehensive Labor Market Development","Develop a comprehensive labor market; create a thorough environment to improve the labor supply-demand balance; diversify labor transaction forms; ensure laborers' rights to freedom of choice of working places and residence.",""],[1,"139","4","Labor Contract Promotion and Employment Protection","Promote the use of labor contracts; ensure interests of both employees and employers are met; establish unemployment insurance; complete the policy of recruiting and using employees in the State economic sector and public administrative authority; develop business administrative manpower markets.",""],[1,"139","4","Labor Market Information and Statistics System","Consolidate the system of information and statistics on labor markets.",""],[1,"146","14","Job Creation and Female Employment Expansion","Generate jobs for about 1.6 million employees per annum, reaching a total of 8 million jobs in the five years 2006-2010.",""],[1,"147","11","Job Creation and Workplace Safety Support for Vulnerable Groups","Increase the quantity and quality of jobs and ensure job safety for the poor and people with extreme difficulties;",""]],"63":[[1,"41","6","Flood Monitoring and Irrigation Development Projects","In irrigation, focus has been put on flood monitoring programs, especially irrigation projects in the Mekong River delta, and Central provinces, on the 2nd phase of irrigation development in the Red River delta, on reservoirs in Central Highlands provinces.",""],[1,"72","5","Production Infrastructure Development and Irrigation Investment","Priority is to be given to infrastructure development to service production; increase investment in irrigation and underground water exploitation works so as to quickly solve drought problems, ensure irrigation and drainage requirements of agriculture, water supply to industry, people's life and aquaculture.",""],[1,"72","5","Natural Disaster Warning and Forecast System Strengthening","Intensify natural disaster warning and forecast systems; synchronously develop the system for disease prevention and combat among cattle, poultry rearing and aquaculture.",""],[1,"72","5","Drought-Resilient Livestock and Crop Variety Transition Study","Study to shift to livestock and plant varieties with lower water requirements in drought-stricken areas.",""],[1,"73","4","Agricultural Insurance Policy Development","Develop insurance policies for agricultural production and farmers such as social insurance, natural disaster insurance, insurance against risks due to market and price fluctuation.",""]],"64":[[1,"71","2","New Rural Infrastructure and Urbanization Linkage Development","Build new rural systems with modern infrastructure in association with urbanization.",""],[1,"71","2","New Countryside Development and Farmers' Living Standards Improvement","Develop new countryside with modernized infrastructure linked with urbanization and improved farmers' living standards.",""],[1,"72","7","Rural Economic and Social Infrastructure Construction","Support the construction of both economic and social infrastructure in rural areas;",""],[1,"73","9","New-Model Village Development and Rural Urbanization Programme","Organize the building up new-model villages, where modern life and clean environment is facilitated together with urbanization of rural living areas.",""]],"65":[[1,"7","8","Information Forecasting and Market Management Strengthening","Enhance quality and effectiveness of information forecasts and analysis; strengthen price control and market management, proactively deal with negative impacts of world's price fluctuation, price changes of essential materials or consumption goods, ensuring smooth integration in one hand and controlling inflation in the other hand, creating stable condition for production and people's living improvement.",""],[1,"73","2","Agricultural Market Information and Forecasting System","Provide proper market forecasts and information to farmers and enterprises.",""]],"66":[[1,"7","9","Wage and Salary Reform","Continue wage and salary reform.",""],[1,"7","9","Single Minimum Salary Policy","Study and implement the policy of a single minimum salary level for domestic and foreign business sectors.",""],[1,"7","9","Public Sector Salary and Welfare Adjustment","Deal with inappropriate practices in salary and earnings of cadres, civil servants and public employees in state agencies, political and socio-political organizations; income of retired people and other ones that benefit from State's social welfare policies.",""],[1,"78","3","Labor Protection Policy Measures","Implement policies to ensure laborers' interests, particularly their working and living conditions.",""]],"67":[[1,"8","1","Development of Key Economic Zones","Promulgate policies to develop key economic zones so that they will become driving force for the country's economic development process.",""],[1,"8","1","Direct Support for Disadvantaged and Minority Regions","Pay more attentions to development in disadvantaged regions, mountainous, border-line and ethnic minority density areas through direct supports of the Government in order to narrow the gaps of development, income and living standards among regions and ethnic groups.",""],[1,"41","2","State Budget Investment in Social Development and Priority Regions","the capital from the State budget has been focused on the development of education and training, science, technology and environment, social welfare and health care, national programs, hunger eradication and poverty reduction, and priorities have been given to the socio-economic development in provinces in the central highland region, the northern mountainous region, and the Mekong River delta, in difficulties-driven provinces and regions frequented by natural disasters.",""]],"68":[[1,"6","15","Development Investment Management Reform","Complete mechanism and policies on development investment management, abolish the \"ask-and-give\" mechanism, surmount the spreading out situation in investment, avoid losses, mis-spending and debts, strengthen quality control of infrastructure investment.",""],[1,"8","2","Effective Implementation of National Key Investment Projects and Targeted Programs","Organize effective and on-scheduled implementation of national key investment projects, of which investment orientation has been approved by the National Assembly, of on going projects and national targeted programs.",""],[1,"40","1","Strengthened Investment and Construction Governance","the decentralization of decision-making power has been strengthened which facilitates the activeness and autonomy of ministries, sectors, localities and investors.",""],[1,"40","1","Strengthened Project Monitoring Across the Investment Cycle","monitoring of all projects during the entire investment process has been strengthened.",""],[1,"69","8","Infrastructure Development Investment Prioritization","The State budget spending structure is expected to shift towards ensuring more spending for investment in infrastructure development with priority given to social infrastructure;",""]],"69":[[1,"71","3","Food Production and Diversification Programme","Increase production at reasonable rate to ensure national food security, food reserve, animal feeds and export of 3 - 4 million tons per annum.",""],[1,"71","3","High-Quality Rice Export Upgrade","Emphasize quality, increase high- quality rice for export without increasing rice-cultivating areas;",""],[1,"71","3","Low-Productivity Rice Land Conversion","low-productivity rice- cultivating areas are to shift to other crop cultivation with higher efficiency.",""],[1,"71","3","Food and Foodstuff Hygiene and Safety Improvement","intensify food and foodstuff hygiene and safety, and increase organic products.",""],[1,"71","3","Native Crop Variety and Biodiversity Conservation","Preserve and develop native crop varieties and biodiversity in various areas.",""]],"70":[[1,"71","4","Industrial Crops Productivity and Value-Addition Development","Industrial Crops: improve their productivity, quality; process high-value products and develop product trademarks.",""],[1,"71","4","Large-Scale Crop Specialization and Agro-Industrial Linkages","Develop large-scale specialization areas closely linked with processing industry, gradually industrialize and modernize agriculture and rural areas.",""],[1,"71","4","Agricultural Technology and Improved Variety Support","Invest and apply scientific and technological advances, new high-yield and high quality varieties, and devise solutions for ensuring the provision of varieties at reasonable prices for remote and mountainous areas.",""],[1,"71","4","Tea Crop Market-Oriented Development","Develop tea crops in response to the market.",""],[1,"71","4","Cashew Area Expansion and Production Increase","Quickly increase cashew cultivation areas and production.",""],[1,"71","4","Coffee Area Rationalization and Productivity Adjustment","Reduce coffee plantation in areas with difficult irrigation, unsuitable soil and low productivity.",""]],"71":[[1,"71","5","Centralized Livestock Development and Disease Control","Develop livestock in the orientation of centralized farm in association with processing industry and disease prevention and treatment.",""],[1,"71","5","Integrated Fisheries Development and Processing","Systematically develop fishery products, including all stages of exploitation, aquaculture and processing, ensuring sustainable development in line with the strategy for developing sea and island economy.",""],[1,"71","5","Coastal Fisheries Stabilization and Seafood Farming Expansion","Stabilize coastal exploitation linked with development of seafood farming development.",""],[1,"71","5","Offshore Fisheries Expansion Programme","Rapidly develop off-shore exploitation.",""],[1,"72","1","Aquaculture Product Development and Control Plan","design plans for the development of key products in the coming five years, ensuring control in aquaculture, exploitation, processing as well as in product sales.",""]],"72":[[1,"71","2","Rural Economic Diversification and Craft Development","Diversify economies and crafts, particularly those with high added and export value.",""],[1,"71","2","Rural Industrial and Services Development","Development rate of industry and services in rural areas should not be lower than the country's average.",""],[1,"72","6","Rural Non-Agricultural Economic Development Programme","Develop non-agricultural economies in rural areas for employment and income generation and rural economic structural transformation in the orientation of development of industries and services in rural areas.",""],[1,"72","6","Rural Small and Medium Enterprise Development","Develop various types of rural business, especially small and medium size businesses and industrial villages.",""],[1,"73","7","Rural Industrial and Trade Village Support Deployment","Dispatch more officials to rural areas to support the development of rural industries and trade villages, education and vocational training for farmers.",""]],"73":[[1,"49","1","Population and Family Planning Strengthening","Population and family planning activities have been continuously strengthened.",""]],"74":[[1,"8","7","Population Health Improvement Initiative","Improve the physical, intellectual and spiritual health of the population;",""],[1,"57","1","Nationwide Anti-Malnutrition Program for Under-Five Children","Anti-malnutrition program for under-5-year-old children has been carried out nation-wide",""],[1,"57","1","National Extended Vaccination Program for Children","National Extended Vaccination Program for children is maintained",""]],"75":[[1,"9","5","Women's Training and Participation Support Programme","Provide training to women so that they can more and more participate in social activities, leadership and management organizations of all levels; create favorable conditions for efficiently ensuring basic rights and bringing into play the role of women in political, economic, cultural and social fields.",""],[1,"9","5","Anti-Discrimination and Domestic Violence Elimination Measures","Eliminate all forms of discrimination against women, domestic violence.",""],[1,"9","5","Child Rights Protection and Care Measures","Respect and ensure rights and responsibilities of children for the family and society according to the international convention for children and laws on protecting, taking care of and training children of Vietnam.",""],[1,"57","2","Educational Fee Exemption and Reduction for Orphaned and Disabled Children","Educational support for orphaned, handicapped children is continued with 100% of them enjoying exemption or reduction of school fees and other payments.",""],[1,"57","2","Community Child Health Care and Rehabilitation Services","Health care and rehabilitation for children in the community have gained some achievements, along with well-organized programs to support children suffering from innate defects, such as eyes, heart, harelips, cleft palate, Agent Orange intoxication, etc.",""],[1,"57","3","Vocational Training and Job Placement for Children","Vocational training and job generation for children have got further attention.",""],[1,"66","5","Social Progress, Equity, and Gender Equality Promotion Measures","Sixth, realize social progress, equity and gender equality, create jobs, encourage people to get rich in legitimate ways, alleviate hunger and reduce poverty, develop social security system and prevent social problems.",""]],"76":[[1,"3","20","Freedom of Religion and Belief Protection Policy","Implementation of the policy of respecting and ensuring people's freedom of religion and belief.",""],[1,"9","6","Youth Development Law and National Strategy Implementation","Develop and well implement the Law on Youth and National Strategy for Youth Development, creating conditions for young people to be in an important position, and fulfilling given tasks.",""],[1,"9","6","Freedom of Religion and Belief Enforcement","Implement laws and policies of respecting and ensuring people's freedom of religion and belief.",""],[1,"9","6","Religious Organizations Social Participation Enablement","Create conditions for organizations of religion and belief to participate in social activities, to make contribution to country's construction and development.",""]],"77":[[1,"6","17","Industrial Competitiveness and Selective Industry Development","Maintain rapid economic growth together with improving product quality, industry's effectiveness, raising competitiveness of industry to keep and to expand domestic and international markets.",""],[1,"6","17","High-Tech and Potential Industries Development","Concentrate on selective development of potential industries, hi-tech products.",""],[1,"6","17","Labor-Intensive Industry Development","Pay attention to the development of labor-intensive industries, facilitating economic infrastructure development for the industrialization and modernization process.",""],[1,"74","1","Industrial Competitiveness and Product Quality Improvement","Continue to maintain high growth rate together with industrial product quality improvement and production efficiency, increasing competitiveness of the industrial sector in order to sustain and expand domestic and international market shares.",""],[1,"74","1","Targeted Development of High-Potential High-Tech Industries","Focus on development of selected industries that have potentials, and products that contain high technology value.",""],[1,"74","6","Selective Industrial Development and Export Quality Improvement","Concentrate on selective development of potential industries, hi-tech products, critical industries that manufacture production materials and industries for national defense; Pay attention to the development of labor-intensive industries, facilitating economic infrastructure development for the industrialization and modernization process.",""],[1,"74","7","National Industrial Production Network Development","Synchronously develop industrial production network throughout the country on the basis of rational planning of economies and appropriate distribution of resources, advantages and market opportunities among regions and localities.",""],[1,"74","7","Industrial Diversification and Local Content Enhancement","Diversify scale and ownership, increase scientific, technological and local content in industrial products.",""],[1,"74","7","Balanced Industrial Development with Services, Urban Development, and Environmental Protection","Develop industry parallel to services, urban development and environmental protection.",""],[1,"77","4","Industrial Development Planning Adjustment","Adjust industrial development planning to facilitate the participation of all economic sectors in investing into supporting industries, producing essential products such as steel, iron, cement, electricity, etc.",""],[1,"77","6","Industrial Sector Promotion and Investment Attraction Policy","Have policies to promote and to create better conditions for all economic sectors participating in industries.",""],[1,"77","6","Support for Key Industrial Industries and Products","Government provides supports to development of key industries and products, in which non-state economic sector can not or do not want to invest, and at the same time it has policies to invite foreign investors in important industrial projects, such as ore mining, steel, bauxite and aluminum production, oil refinery, manufacturing, basic chemicals production, medical chemistry, fertilizers, cement, paper-pulp production and afforestation, and other potential industries like electronics, telecommunication, IT, etc so that the industrial structure would shift to producing more added value and intellectual products.",""],[1,"77","6","Supplementary Industries Promotion Policy","Have appropriate policies to promote supplementary industries.",""],[1,"78","1","Production Innovation and Quality Management Upgrade","Apply technical, technological and management innovations to reduce production costs, improve productivity, quality and competitiveness.",""],[1,"78","1","Quality Assurance and Environmental Management System Adoption","Intensify the application of advanced quality assurance, environmental management systems (ISO 9000, ISO 14000, etc.)",""],[1,"78","1","Product Standardization and Market Penetration Support","Also, pay attention to product standards, packages and tastes as well as traditional customs and practices in each region for market penetration and expansion.",""],[1,"78","2","Promotion of Locally Made Industrial Products","Issue policies to encourage the use of locally-made industrial products, facilitating enterprises' market expansion.",""],[1,"78","4","Industrial Development and Regional Planning Review","Review and adjust industrial development planning as well as regional and territorial planning.",""],[1,"78","4","Prioritized and Key Industries Support Policy","Clearly define lists of prioritized industries, key industries with consistent supporting policies.",""],[1,"78","4","Anti-Monopoly Program for Production and Circulation","Carry out the program of reducing and eliminating monopoly in production and good circulation.",""]],"78":[[1,"74","8","Industrial Zone and Cluster Development Programme","Develop industrial zones, clusters and concentrations throughout the country as planned.",""],[1,"74","8","Focal Industrial Zone Establishment","Establish focal industrial zones while paying attention to investment in developing other zones in a suitable structure, avoiding discrepancy among regions and localities.",""]],"79":[[1,"7","3","Export Expansion and Technology Attraction Initiative","Rapidly increase exports and attract capital and technologies, especially high technologies in order to lower production costs and improve the competitiveness of enterprises.",""],[1,"62","4","Market Opening for Export and Investment Mobilization","It is necessary to open up markets for boosting up export, including international and domestic markets, service markets in order to mobilize more investment, technologies and advanced management technics, raising effectiveness and competitiveness of the economy.",""],[1,"71","5","Domestic and Export Market Development Strategy","Implement the strategy for domestic and export market establishment within the context of international economic integration.",""],[1,"74","9","Regional Industrial Cooperation and Export Promotion","Intensify industrial cooperation and production division in the region and the world.",""],[1,"74","9","Industrial Trade Promotion and Export Upgrading","Intensify trade promotion and export of industrial products, increase processed and high- tech products.",""],[1,"77","5","Industrial Development Resource Mobilization","Mobilize more resources for faster development of industries that have competitive advances, such as agro-forestry-aqua processing industries, textile and garments, footwear, ship-building, machinery, assembling, transportation meals, wood industry ...",""],[1,"77","7","Enterprise Branding and Market Promotion Support","Maintain and improve the prestige of products, establish, protect and promote each enterprise's own trademarks in the market.",""],[1,"77","7","Marketing, Advertising, and Sales Modernization","Renovate marketing, advertising and sale modes.",""],[1,"77","7","Enterprise Distribution Network Development","Each sector, each enterprise needs to develop its own appropriate distribution network and participate in distribution channels of transnational groups.",""],[1,"77","7","E-commerce Development Initiative","Develop e- commerce, using the Internet to search for market information, advertisement and business opportunities.",""],[1,"78","2","Customs and Trade Procedure Streamlining","Streamline customs, export and import procedures.",""],[1,"78","3","Market Information and Trade Promotion Support for Export Expansion","Well organize market information activities, trade promotion, execution of international laws and Vietnam's commitments with other countries and regions to support enterprises in export market penetration and expansion.",""],[1,"79","2","Trade and Services Competitiveness Enhancement","Continue developing trade and services, fully using their potentials; enhance capacity and quality, increase the competitiveness of goods and services with the participation of many economic sectors.",""],[1,"79","3","Import, Export, and Foreign Trade Promotion","Push up import, export and foreign trade activities.",""]],"80":[[1,"75","2","Rural Electrification and Renewable Power Supply Expansion","By 2010, 90 - 95% of households, 100% of communes in the rural areas, in particular, are to be provided with high quality, stable electricity at regulated prices.",""],[1,"75","2","Off-Grid Power Supply for Remote Areas and Islands","Remote areas, islands will receive power from new sources such as micro hydropower stations, wind and solar power, etc.",""],[1,"75","2","Electricity Cost Reduction Measures","Try to reduce production and investment costs.",""]],"81":[[1,"75","3","Rational Coal Production Organization","The principle is rational organization of coal production to ensure satisfaction of current supply-demand balance and long-term supplies for later development stages, giving priority to coal provision to huge consumers such as power generation, cement, fertilizers, construction material producers as well as cooking fuel users in rural and mountainous areas.",""],[1,"75","3","Coal Production Expansion and Export Supply Plan","The sector's average growth rate is to reach 9.3% per annum in the next five years; 42-45 million tons of clean coal is expected to be produced in 2010, mostly for domestic consumption and 8-9 million tons for export in the initial years and for later years to be gradually reduced80.",""],[1,"75","4","Foreign Investment Attraction for Oil and Gas Exploration","Intensify foreign investment attraction in exploration and search to increase identified reserves.",""],[1,"75","4","Dung Quat Oil Refinery Project Completion","Complete investment in Dung Quat oil refinery project in 2009;",""],[1,"75","4","Nghi Son Petrochemical and Oil Refinery Project","implement Nghi Son petrochemical and oil refinery project, oil refinery project in the South, and invest in oil and gas extraction overseas.",""],[1,"75","4","Overseas Oil and Gas Extraction Investment","implement Nghi Son petrochemical and oil refinery project, oil refinery project in the South, and invest in oil and gas extraction overseas.",""],[1,"75","4","Gas Supply Assurance for Power, Fertilizer, and Industry","Ensure gas supply to power generation, fertilizer production and industries.",""],[1,"75","4","Overseas Oil and Gas Operations","Implement oil and gas operations overseas.",""]],"82":[[1,"75","5","Foreign Investment Promotion for Steel Production Capacity","Facilitate the attraction of foreign investment to increase steel production capacity.",""],[1,"75","5","Ore Exploitation and Steel Production Projects","Develop the projects for ore exploitation and steel production in Lao Cai, Ha Tinh, Thai Nguyen and Cao Bang.",""],[1,"75","6","Sin Quyen Copper Complex Completion","Concentrate on completing Sin Quyen Copper Complex in 2006;",""],[1,"75","6","Lam Dong Bauxite-Aluminum Complex Investment","invest in Lam Dong bauxite - aluminum complex with the capacity of 600,000 tons per annum to export aluminum, and later stage of aluminum electrolysis.",""],[1,"75","6","Dak Nong Aluminum Production Project for Export","Continue the aluminum production project for export in Dak Nong with the capacity of 1 - 2 million tons per annum.",""],[1,"76","1","Cement Production Expansion and Plant Renovation","In order to achieve this objective, investment should be accelerated for projects started in 2004 - 2005 and provided for newly planned projects.",""],[1,"76","1","Cement Factory Technology Upgrade","Renovate, replace blast furnace with reverted furnace in a number of cement factories so as to increase production and quality, using existing facilities to increase production and stabilize the quality.",""],[1,"76","2","Paper and Pulp Investment Programme","Focus investment on paper and pulp projects so as to gradually replace pulp importation.",""],[1,"76","2","Domestic Paper Production Expansion","Try to increase production to satisfy domestic demands of medium and low- grade paper.",""]],"83":[[1,"76","3","Machinery Industry Development and Diversification","Concentrate on products with market advantages and competitiveness, particularly those serving agriculture and rural areas such as small motors, water pumps, tractors, farming machines, agricultural and aqua-product processing equipment.",""],[1,"76","3","Auxiliary Industries Development for Automotive and Motorbike Sectors","Develop auxiliary industries for automobile and motorbike industries.",""],[1,"76","3","Mechanical Industry Development for Construction and Heavy Equipment","Develop mechanical industry for construction, total machinery, shipbuilding, tool machine engineering, automobile and motorbike industry.",""],[1,"76","3","Industrial Equipment and Spare Parts Manufacturing","Research, design and manufacture total machinery and spare components for cement, paper, electricity, fertilizer and chemical industries.",""],[1,"76","4","Electronic Industry and ICT Manufacturing and Modernization Programme","Focus on manufacturing electronic accessories, industrial electronic devices, information technology and software production for management, education and training, e-commerce development, and financial and banking management.",""],[1,"77","5","Information Technology and Bio-Industry Development","Put more attentions to development of IT, bio-industries, supplementary industries, export processing industries, and industries that serve transportation, construction, services.",""]],"84":[[1,"76","5","Nitrogenous Fertilizer Plant Construction and Expansion Programme","To achieve this objective, Ninh Binh Project of constructing a plant in Ninh Binh that produces nitrogenous fertilizers from fine coal with the capacity of 560,000 tons/year should be accelerated and put into operation in 2008; nitrogenous fertilizer plant with the capacity of 800,000 tons/year from gas, DAP fertilizer plant with the capacity of 330,000 tons/year, and other plants are also to be constructed.",""],[1,"76","6","Selective Chemical Industry Development","Study the market and efficiency of investment in soda-chlorine plants near input (salt) supply sources and convenient for other related industries like PVC and paper mills.",""],[1,"76","7","Study for Domestic Pharmaceutical Production Investment","Conduct comprehensive study of the advantages, demands and capital potentials to invest in the production of a number of medicines for domestic demands and gradual decrease of imports.",""]],"85":[[1,"76","8","Textiles and Garments Production Expansion and Upgrading","In order to achieve this objective, there needs to be a fundamental shift in product structure, gradually increase high-value products, fashionable items and increase domesticalized content in exported goods.",""],[1,"76","8","Domestic Market Expansion and Global Distribution Integration","Expand domestic markets parallel to export intensification, gradually participating in global distribution networks of transnational groups.",""],[1,"76","8","Textile Input Self-Supply and Production Investment","Ensure self-supply of local inputs.",""],[1,"76","8","Modern Equipment and Design Upgrading for Silk Production","Invest in production expansion, especially silk production, with modern equipment and technology; special attention should be paid to improved designs and quality.",""],[1,"77","1","Footwear and Leather Production Modernization Programme","Focus on modernizing parts of footwear and leather production, developing leather sources of all types and increasingly using local materials to improve the value added of export products.",""],[1,"77","1","Footwear Quality and Production Improvement Investment","The next five years will see more investment in improving quality and production with the introduction of application software into design, sewing, etc., diversifying products, designs, transforming from partial to complete production lines.",""],[1,"77","2","Fruit Beverage and Mineral Water Plant Investment Priority","Give investment priority to plants producing beverages from fruits and mineral water.",""],[1,"77","2","Beer Brewery Capacity Expansion","Expand existing beer breweries to increase capacity to 2.5 billion liters in 2010, satisfying domestic demands and promoting exports.",""]],"86":[[1,"78","6","Construction Sector Upgrading and Advanced Facilities Investment","Develop the construction sector to reach an advanced level in the region, in the fields of project construction, construction materials, architecture and construction planning, urban and housing development; Invest in advanced facilities in the construction sector, rapidly access to and own modern construction works in the construction and installation of complicated and big works as hydropower works, thermal power works, multistoried buildings, works with high aperture, bridges, tunnels, underground works, oil and gas works, etc.",""],[1,"78","7","Urban Development and Construction Planning Programme","Continue to implement the urban development orientations until 2020, in order to formulate an appropriate urban system over the country for the sake of industrialization and modernization.",""],[1,"78","7","Regional and Urban Construction Planning Framework","Focus on the promotion of regional construction planning, general planning for urban construction, detailed planning for urban construction, planning for rural construction in order to manage construction as planned.",""],[1,"78","7","Urban Infrastructure Modernization Initiative","Push up urban development, construction of civilized and modern infrastructure.",""],[1,"78","8","Construction Sector Governance and Decentralization Reform","Strengthen the State management effectiveness on construction while expanding the decentralization, clearly defining the rights and responsibilities of subjects participating in construction in order to ensure the schedule, volume, quality and efficiency, creating a legal framework and driving forces for pushing up construction investment activities and form construction market along the socialist orientation.",""]],"87":[[1,"30","6","Central Highlands Hydroelectricity and Agro-Industrial Development","The Central Highlands region is developing hydroelectricity; constructing clusters of processing industries, developing handicrafts industry, farming; restructuring crops, developing animal husbandry.",""]],"88":[[1,"80","6","International Tourism Cooperation and Market Access Measures","Strengthen international cooperation in tourism.",""],[1,"80","7","Tourism Human Resource Training and Development","Strengthen the training and development of human resources for tourism.",""],[1,"80","8","Tourism Advertising Capital Mobilization Mechanism","Build mechanism to raise capital for tourism advertisement in international markets.",""],[1,"80","8","Foreign Investment Promotion in Tourism Areas","Encourage foreign investors to invest in some tourism areas.",""]],"89":[[1,"80","12","Air Transport Liberalization Regulatory Roadmap","Support the air transportation regulatory roadmap to reach liberalization of air transportation in ASEAN; invest to increase Vietnam-owned aircraft fleet.",""]],"90":[[1,"81","4","Telecommunication Market Liberalization Policy","Issue policies to open the telecommunication market in line with commitments prescribed in the Vietnam-US Bilateral Trade Agreement and those on international economic integration to boost the mobilization of domestic and external resources.",""],[1,"81","4","Labor Productivity and Competitiveness Improvement Measures","Take measures to increase labor productivity, reduce production cost, improve service quality to strengthen competitiveness.",""],[1,"81","4","Human Resource Training and International Cooperation Expansion","Pay attention to the training of human resources and expansion of international cooperation in this field.",""],[1,"81","5","Charge Management Mechanism Reform","Renovate the charge management mechanism in which the State directly controls the charges of services still affected by monopoly, applying the principle of 'cost-based charges' and making them compatible to those in the region.",""],[1,"81","5","Competitive Service Pricing Framework","Charges for the services for which truly competitive markets have been established are decided by the service providers themselves, while the services with newly-born competition are controlled according to the charge framework.",""],[1,"81","5","National Infrastructure Network Sharing and Separation Reform","The management policy is to maximize efficiency by sharing the national infrastructure network, separate infrastructure network management from service management.",""],[1,"81","6","Private Sector and FDI Infrastructure Attraction Mechanism","Issue policies and mechanisms to attract private economic sectors, including FDI in constructing infrastructure and urban structures.",""]],"91":[[1,"82","8","Expansion of Insurance Services Across Economic and Social Activities","Insurance service is targeted to be present in all economic and social activities.",""],[1,"82","9","Insurance Capital Increase and Product Diversification Measures","Implement solutions to increase charter capital applicable to insurance companies to improve their financial competence and payment.",""],[1,"82","9","Insurance Product Development for Agricultural, Forestry, and Fishery Sectors","Diversify products, encourage companies to study new products, especially for agricultural, forestry and fishery programs.",""],[1,"82","9","Insurance Information Technology Modernization","Modernize information technology in financial operation management, develop safety/security technology (for treasuries and deposits), risk assessment technology to prevent and minimize losses.",""],[1,"82","9","Vietnam Insurance Federation Mediation Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the competency of Vietnam Insurance Federation to function as an \"umpire\" among member enterprises.",""],[1,"82","9","Insurance Regulatory Supervision and Client Protection","Improve the responsibilities of the State management agencies in insurance business to closely control and supervise the compliance with regulations in the Insurance Business Law of insurance companies, ensure the full rights of clients.",""]],"92":[[1,"83","7","Aquatic Product Processing Upgrading for Exports","Raise the processing proportion in exported aquatic products to increase the value added.",""],[1,"83","9","Coffee Quality Improvement and Modern Trade Methods Initiative","Focus on increasing the quality and processing proportion in exported coffee, and at the same time actively apply modern coffee transaction and trade methods in the world to minimize price risks.",""],[1,"83","10","Tea Quality Improvement and Export Promotion Programme","Focus on producing clean tea, improve the quality of exported tea, boost processed products from tea, actively increase the share in the world's big tea markets including the UK, Russia, the Middle East, China, etc, to raise the price of our exported tea.",""],[1,"83","11","Domestic Rubber Processing and Value-Added Export Investment","focus on the domestic production and processing investment to export products made from rubber and gain higher value added.",""],[1,"84","1","Cashew and Pepper Production and Export Development Measures","Try to maintain and develop the production and export of cashew nuts and pepper, focus on measures to improve export prices.",""]],"93":[[1,"84","3","Garment Sector Competitiveness Enhancement Measures","To strengthen the competitiveness of the garment sector, it is essential to implement uniform measures, including decreasing production costs, diversifying designs and models, carrying out internal cooperation within the sector, building trademarks, focusing on market segments in which we are strong, establishing trading centers and hubs which provide garment materials and accessories.",""],[1,"84","4","Footwear Export Upgrading and Market Diversification","Focus should be given on making high-grade items serving big markets such as the USA, Japan and EU.",""],[1,"84","4","Footwear Input, Design, and Pattern Self-Sufficiency","Besides, increase autonomy and self-supply of materials, designs as well as patterns.",""],[1,"84","5","Wooden Products Export Development Programme","Wooden products are the items that require encouragement and development for export in the following years.",""]],"94":[[1,"84","7","Services Export Expansion Strategy","Strive to increase the total export turnover of services to USD 8 billion by 2010, making the total of USD 34-35 billion for the whole period of 2006-2010, with emphasis on the services with high potential of generating foreign currency income such as tourism, ship repair, export of labor and expertise.",""]],"95":[[1,"86","9","Curriculum and Teaching Methods Reform","Renovate the curricula and teaching methods at university, professional and nursery education level.",""],[1,"86","9","Nursery and Secondary Education Quality Upgrade","Upgrade the quality, renovate the curricula and teaching methods of nursery schools and secondary education.",""],[1,"86","9","Upper Secondary Specialization Adjustment for Career Guidance","Adjust the specialization on science, liberal arts, etc., at upper secondary schools in order to provide better career guidance and orientation for students in Vietnam's specific context.",""],[1,"86","9","Gender and Reproductive Health Curriculum Integration","Introduce gender and reproductive health issues into the curricula at all school levels.",""],[1,"87","1","National Standardized Education Quality System Development","it is necessary to build and complete the national standardized systems covering the content, skills required by each education and training level; fundamental demands on morality, manners and responsibility of learners; and conditions guaranteed for education quality",""],[1,"87","3","Marxist-Leninist and Ho Chi Minh Thought Education Improvement","Improve the efficiency of Marxist-Leninist theory and Ho Chi Minh thoughts education, pay attention to teaching humanities (together with teaching knowledge and vocation) in order to create modern Vietnamese generations.",""],[1,"87","4","Education Method Modernization and School ICT Integration","Focus on renovating teaching and learning methods, apply information technology to the teaching, learning and school management.",""],[1,"88","5","Education Quality Assurance and Accreditation Reform","Implement the educational quality assurance and accreditation schemes, gradually applying standards and criteria used by developed countries to the educational quality assessment of a number of specific fields; prepare to join the international educational quality accreditation system.",""],[1,"88","6","Education Inspection and Oversight Strengthening","Intensify inspection, supervision and oversight of the law execution in educational and training activities.",""]],"96":[[1,"87","5","Social Equity and Gender Equality Promotion","Further perform social equity and gender equality, give priority to the education development in ethnic-minority inhabited and disadvantaged areas and education for disadvantaged children and illiterate women.",""],[1,"87","6","Education Socialization and Resource Mobilization Mechanism","Implement mechanism and policies to encourage investment and mobilize social resources for education and training development.",""],[1,"87","6","Education Governance and Stakeholder Responsibility Framework","Issue concrete mechanism and policies defining the responsibility of sectors, localities, socio-economic organizations and individuals and encouraging them to contribute to the construction of schools, give financial support to learners, use trained human resource and supervise education activities.",""],[1,"87","7","Education and Training Institutional Financial Mechanism Reform","Renovate financial mechanism and policies in education and training institutions to make them more pro-active and responsible for finance, staff and organization.",""],[1,"87","8","Tuition Regime Reform","Fundamentally renovate the tuition regimes: apart from the State support depending on the budget, the tuition has to cover necessary costs for teaching, learning and partly become investment for school construction; in the first stage, the tuition compensates adequately for regular costs.",""],[1,"87","9","Education Fee Subsidy and Scholarship Support","The State is to issue policies of subsidizing fees or granting scholarship to students of the educational universalization program, beneficiaries of social welfare, learners in disadvantaged areas, poor students and excellent ones in both public and private schools.",""],[1,"88","4","International Educational Cooperation and ODA-Funded Education Modernization","Intensify proactiveness in international educational cooperation.",""],[1,"88","8","Increase Education and Training Investment","Increase investment in education and training to reach 20% of total State budget expenditure 2 - 3 years before 2010.",""]],"97":[[1,"89","5","Biotechnology Application for Agriculture and Fisheries","Pay attention to the wide research and application of bio-technological achievements to serve agricultural and fishery production.",""],[1,"89","5","High-Yield Breed Improvement and Intensive Farming Support","Accelerate the research, selection and import of high-yield, high-quality plant and animal breeds, apply technological advances to intensive farming, in order to increase productivity, generate jobs and produce goods for consumption, production and export.",""],[1,"99","3","Scientific Work Training and Agricultural Extension Programme","Train people how to work scientifically, actively conduct agricultural and forestry extension activities, transfer technology and provide people with information to develop commodity economy.",""]],"98":[[1,"89","6","Fundamental Medical Research and Disease Prevention Focus","Concentrate on fundamental medical research, environmental impacts on health, critical infectious diseases as well as HIV/AIDS prevention.",""],[1,"94","5","Scientific Research and Modern Technology Application Promotion","Promote scientific studies, access to and apply modern science and technology achievements, especially biology and computer technologies; gradually heighten the country's health care to the regional progressive standards.",""]],"99":[[1,"89","7","Scientific and Technological Solutions for Resource Efficiency and Environmental Protection","Study and apply scientific and technological solutions to the rational, efficient extraction and utilization of natural resources and protection of the ecological environment.",""],[1,"89","7","New Technologies for Environmental Pollution Control and Treatment","Apply new technologies in environmental pollution control and treatment.",""],[1,"89","7","Local Science and Technology Research and Application Support","Foster research and application of science and technology in localities, with special attention paid to the rural, mountainous, remote and disadvantaged areas.",""]],"100":[[1,"91","2","Labor Export Program","Effectively implement the program on labor export, raising percentage of trained workers.",""],[1,"91","5","Labor Export Expansion Program","Develop labor export into a big, harmonious program with expanded participation of all economic sectors; improve productivity of export labor so as to penetrate into high-value labor markets, creating important resources for the country's socio-economic development and the people's improved living standards.",""],[1,"91","5","Labor Export Market Expansion Measures","Issue strong and specific measures and policies to expand labor export markets and create opportunities for laborers to participate in labor export markets.",""],[1,"91","6","Training Reform for Exported Laborers","Strongly renovate the training modes of exported laborers so that they acquire industrial production practices, law compliance awareness, good cultural behaviors, good understanding of the recipient countries' culture, customs and traditions as well as fluency in their foreign languages.",""]],"101":[[1,"92","7","Social Support Policies for Meritorious Persons and Vulnerable Groups","Well implement policies towards people with meritorious contribution to the nation, and families of martyrs and disabled soldiers, elderly, disable people and others that benefit from social support policies of the State, including housing, health care, rehabilitation, education, loans for job creation policies, and subsidy to those engaged in the revolutionary wars.",""],[1,"92","8","Community Resource Mobilization for Living Standards Improvement","Continue strengthening the socialization of these activities through such movements as 'Paying tribute\" or \"Returning Favor\", \"When you drink, remember the source\", etc, in order to mobilize resources for improving the living standards of these people equal to or higher than the average living standards of local people.",""],[1,"92","9","Martyrs Remains Recovery and Cemetery Construction","Quickly resolve the wars' aftermaths, such as finding the remains of martyrs (those missing in action), building cemeteries for martyrs to bury the remains found in neighboring countries.",""],[1,"92","10","Social Security Network Development","(3) Develop the social security network",""],[1,"92","11","State Support for Vulnerable and Disadvantaged Groups","Supplement policies to provide the State support to vulnerable groups, people in extreme difficulties, and the disadvantaged so that they can have opportunities to create jobs for themselves or get employed, earning sufficient income to support themselves, participate in community and social activities and benefit from the economic reform.",""],[1,"92","13","Social Security Network Strengthening and Humanitarian Assistance","Intensify social security network through the development and consolidation of social and mass organizations' funds.",""],[1,"93","1","Safety Net for the Poor","Build up a safety network for the poor.",""],[1,"93","2","Social Support Policies and Solutions for Vulnerable Groups","Develop the system of policies and solutions to support PLWD (people living with disability), the elderly (particularly the solitary elderly without any family support), people infected with toxic chemical, HIV/AIDS, etc.",""],[1,"93","3","Community-Based Social Protection in Poor and High-Risk Areas","Develop community-based social protection work in poor and risk-frequented areas to support those deprived of opportunity and capacity to earn their own living.",""],[1,"93","3","Decentralized Budget Allocation for Social Policy Delivery","Adjust budget allocation methods to implement these social policies; give more autonomy to localities, particularly communes and districts to foster community funds in villages and communes.",""],[1,"93","6","Emergency Aid Fund Operations Renovation","Renovate the operation of Funds for Emergency Aids to the poor.",""],[1,"93","7","Social Security Network Participation Expansion","Expand the participation and heighten the role of social, non-governmental organizations in the development of social security networks.",""],[1,"93","7","Charity Mobilization for Poverty Support","The Fatherland Front at all levels takes the lead and cooperates with the authorities, associations, mass organizations in developing a variety of modes for advocacy, involving all agencies, enterprises and people in charity work to help the poor.",""],[1,"93","7","Housing Support Program for Poor and Ethnic Minority Households","Continue the support program on housing for the poor and ethnic groups in remote and disadvantaged areas.",""],[1,"93","8","Humanitarian Support for Social Security Networks","Encourage humanitarian activities of all non-governmental organizations, social associations and unions to develop the social security networks and provide effective assistance to the vulnerable.",""]],"102":[[1,"92","12","Voluntary Security Network Diversification","Diversify voluntary security networks.",""],[1,"92","12","Agricultural Insurance Pilot Scheme","Pilot test some forms of insurance for crops and livestock or market insurance for farmers.",""],[1,"92","12","Community-Based Insurance Programme for Informal Sectors","Develop community-based insurance programs for non-official economic sectors, following the principle of group insurance (family at least).",""],[1,"92","12","Household Insurance Scheme Reform","Develop Household insurance scheme to gradually replace school health insurance system.",""],[1,"93","8","Medical Insurance Scheme for the Poor","Continue the medical insurance scheme for the poor.",""],[1,"93","8","Pro-Poor Social Insurance Schemes","Establish pro-poor social insurance schemes in various forms (crop insurance, domestic animal insurance, loan insurance).",""]],"103":[[1,"93","4","Emergency Social Assistance System","Develop the system of emergency social aids, providing effective support to the poor, the vulnerable in case of natural disasters, accidents and adverse social impacts.",""],[1,"93","4","Storm and Flood-Resilient Housing Support","Provide partial funding for improving houses so that they can endure storms and floods.",""],[1,"93","5","Disaster-Resilient Settlement and Infrastructure Replanning","Re-plan residential areas, social and production infrastructure to make it convenient and facilitative to disaster prevention and rescue work.",""],[1,"93","5","Disaster Logistics and Emergency Preparedness System","Organize, prepare ready logistics and facilities to respond to natural catastrophes and mitigate their adverse impacts; train and guide the poor to provide mutual help among themselves in the event of disasters.",""]],"104":[[1,"94","1","Food Hygiene and Safety Control Measures","Take strong measures to control food hygiene and safety and prevent accident injuries.",""],[1,"94","1","Sanitation, Disease Prevention, Sports, and Physical Training Programs","Launch sanitation, disease prevention, sport and physical training programs.",""],[1,"94","1","Occupational Disease Prevention","Intensify the prevention of occupational diseases.",""],[1,"94","1","School Health Care Improvement","Strengthen and improve school medical care.",""],[1,"94","1","Maternal, Child, Elderly, and Rehabilitation Health Services","Attach special importance to healthcare for mothers and children, and the elderly, as well as rehabilitation activities.",""],[1,"95","7","Home Health Care and New Care Model Expansion","Expand the forms of home health care, and gradually develop new health care models.",""],[1,"95","7","Health Care and Improvement Project Expansion","Expand and implement projects under health care and improvement programs, focusing on the cure of the 6 main infectious diseases; non- infectious diseases; projects of people health improvement and of military and civil medicine combination.",""],[1,"95","7","HIV/AIDS Prevention Partnership Expansion","Encourage domestic and foreign organizations and individuals to take part in preventing HIV/AIDS.",""]],"105":[[1,"94","3","Upgrade Traditional Medicine Hospital and Ward Facilities","Upgrade hospitals for traditional medicine and Oriental medical wards in General Hospitals.",""],[1,"94","3","Medicinal Herb Cultivation and Use Promotion","Propagandize, encourage and guide people to cultivate and use medicinal herbs and animals.",""],[1,"94","3","Traditional Medicine Research and Preservation Programme","Speed up research, inherit, preserve and develop traditional medicines and pharmacies.",""],[1,"94","3","Military-Civil Health Service Cooperation","Promote the cooperation of military and civil medical services in taking care and protecting the health of ordinary people and servicemen, especially those in remote, hinterlands, border and island areas.",""]],"106":[[1,"95","3","Health Sector Legislative and Regulatory Reform","Continue to complete the system of medical legislation; develop, amend, supplement and issue legislative documents such as Pharmaceutical Law, Medical Insurance Law, Law on people health care and protection, etc .; Issue standards for medical specialized practices.",""],[1,"95","3","Routine Monitoring and Evaluation of Health Programs","Carry out regular monitoring and evaluation of medical programs and major targets of the health sector in order to timely adjust policies.",""]],"107":[[1,"95","7","Socialization of Medical Services and Health Insurance","Speed up the socialization of medical activities: Create a healthy competitive environment for businesses involved in the supply of diversifying medical services and insurances to meet people's demand.",""],[1,"95","7","Non-Public Health Care Participation Expansion","Promote the participation of non-public medical systems in the implementation of people's health care and protection targets.",""],[1,"95","7","Private Sector Health Investment Promotion","Encourage the private sector to invest in healthcare.",""]],"108":[[1,"96","3","Socialization of Cultural and Information Activities","Promote the socialization of informational and cultural activities to successfully encourage and mobilize resources from individuals and socio-economic organizations in cultural development.",""],[1,"96","3","Strengthening State Administration in Culture","Strengthen effectiveness and efficiency of State administration in culture, in particular press and publication.",""],[1,"97","3","Equal Financial Mechanisms for Public Service Providers","Apply the same financial mechanisms to all public service providers (theaters, cinemas, museums, libraries, fine arts galleries, etc) as those for utility providers or enterprises.",""],[1,"97","5","Cultural Activities Master Planning and Regulatory Framework","Develop master plans and regulations providing proper management and conditions to cultural activities that are so sensitive that can be abused for unsound purposes.",""]],"109":[[1,"96","5","National Cultural Values Preservation and Unity Promotion","Promote the preservation, inheritance, and improvement of the national cultural values, constantly enrich them, and at the same time maintain, strengthen and improve the unity in cultural diversification, prevent the national united solidarity from any challenges or threats, particularly those by abusing culture.",""],[1,"96","6","Cultural Development Policy and Talent Promotion","Foster cultural and artistic talents, promulgate proper mechanisms and policies to facilitate the country's steady cultural development in the right orientation as the era requires.",""],[1,"96","7","Cultural Talent Development and Creative Works Promotion","Cultivate cultural geniuses, encourage the creation of typical cultural and artistic works, which are valuable in terms of thoughts and arts, in line with the national revolution and renovation achievements.",""],[1,"97","1","Grassroots Cultural Life Promotion Movement","Build up cultural life at grassroots, continue the movement of \"The entire people unite to build up cultural life\", build up cultural families, villages, communes, organizations, and offices.",""],[1,"97","1","Anti-Discrimination and Anti-Maltreatment Measures for Women","Fight discrimination and maltreatment against women.",""]],"110":[[1,"96","8","Science and Technology Application in Cinematographic Production","Promote the application of science and technology achievements to cinematographic production, improve the number of movies with quality to catch up with other regional countries; heighten Vietnamese arts to regional level.",""],[1,"97","2","Enterprise Equitization in the Cultural Sector","Equitize enterprises working in the field of culture with conditions.",""],[1,"97","2","Private Film Studio Authorization","Authorize private film studios to be established, and allow private cinemas and theaters to carry out diverse activities.",""]],"111":[[1,"98","4","Sports Unit Commercialization and Equitization Reform","Change most sports and physical training units to those which can generate their own revenue or become equitized businesses.",""],[1,"98","4","Sports Facilities and Competitions Investment Promotion","Encourage the establishment of businesses for investment and trading in sports facilities and competitions.",""],[1,"98","4","Sports Governance Responsibility Clarification","Clarify responsibilities of State administrative agencies and sports leagues and associations.",""],[1,"98","4","Sports Management Mechanism Reform","Strongly transform sports management mechanism according to international integration requirements.",""],[1,"98","4","Delegation of Sports Event Organization to Non-public Institutions","Hand over the organization of sports and physical training activities and competitions to social and non-public institutions.",""],[1,"98","4","Selective State Financing for Sports Activities","The State only finances those activities assigned to certain organizations or agencies, or partly or wholly cover the expenses of major international sport events.",""],[1,"98","5","Sports Facility Financial Mechanism Reform","Classify and design proper roadmaps so that by 2010, 100% of public sports and physical training facilities which can potentially provide services (including hotels, stadiums, swimming pools, clubs) can apply the same financial mechanism as public services providers.",""],[1,"98","5","Block Grants for Sports Social Organizations","Provide block grants to social organizations specialized in sports and exercises in accordance to their tasks assigned by the State.",""]],"112":[[1,"98","6","International Sports Cooperation and Event Preparation","Expand international cooperation in order to make use of resources, learn experience and acquire advanced technology to urge the development of the country's sports and physical training.",""],[1,"98","6","Asian Indoor Games Hosting Preparation","Make the best efforts in preparation for hosting the 2009 Asian Indoor Games.",""]],"113":[[1,"99","2","Appropriate-Scale Agricultural and Forestry Farm Development","Establish farms for agriculture and forestry cultivation of appropriate scale to the management capacity and production potentials of each area.",""],[1,"99","2","Mountain Area Agro-Processing and Market Linkage Development","Combining the development of processing industries with the development of demand for output in mountainous areas.",""],[1,"99","2","Mountain Area Land, Labor, and Rural Enterprise Development","Effectively utilize land and labor resources, promote the development of forestry, industrial crops, fruit trees, and local traditional handicrafts in these areas.",""],[1,"99","3","Ethnic Minority Economic Development Support Policies","Work out policies to assist economic development of ethnic minority people and help them really benefit from economic growth.",""],[1,"99","4","Ethnic Minority Training and Local Employment Policy","Prioritize the training and employment of ethnic minority people right in their localities.",""]],"114":[[1,"99","4","Ethnic Minority Community Leadership Engagement Policy","Well treat and make use of village leaders, the elderly and women of ethnic minorities.",""],[1,"99","4","Great Unity Policy for Ethnic and Mountainous Areas","Well implement the policy of Great Unity among peoples in ethnic and mountainous areas.",""],[1,"99","5","Ethnic Minority Education and Cultural Support Programme","Attach importance to the consolidation and expansion of educational, medical, cultural and informative activities for ethnic groups.",""],[1,"99","6","Information Dissemination for Hunger Eradication and Poverty Reduction Programs","Strengthen the dissemination of information about programs on hunger eradication and poverty reduction through appropriate methods, forms, organizations and venues that are accessible to minority people.",""],[1,"99","6","Ethnic Minority Self-Help and Poverty Reduction Support","Encourage the self-help and pro-activeness of ethnic minority people to get rid of poverty.",""]],"115":[[1,"99","7","Religious Organizations Engagement and Religious Compliance Policy Development","Develop to the highest degree the social roles of religious organizations in the implementation of the country's renovation process for \"a wealthy people, a strong country, and a fair, democratic and civilized society\".",""],[1,"99","8","Religious Policy Awareness and Guidance Initiative","Raise awareness of religious policies among the people.",""],[1,"99","9","Religions and Beliefs Law Development and Promulgation","Continue the completion of legal documents on religion in preparation for the development and promulgation of the Law on Religions and Beliefs.",""],[1,"99","9","Adaptive Foreign Policy on Religion","Perform foreign policies on religions which are responsive to new conditions.",""],[1,"99","10","Religious Affairs Governance Strengthening","Strengthen and consolidate the State management system in religions; implement specific policies on training and retraining officials in charge of religious work to meet the",""],[1,"100","1","Fatherland Front Activities and Progressive Religious Practice Support","Well perform activities of the Fatherland Front, support the development of religious followers as the core to guide progressive religious practices and maintain their traditional patriotism and attachment to the Party and the socialist regime.",""],[1,"100","2","Incentive Policy Support for Religious Organizations","Install incentive policies to support religious organizations in terms of education and training of dignitaries, organizing their periodical congresses and performing foreign affairs in accordance with the policy that associates religion with the country's interests, i.e. religious groups, organizations and followers accompany and share work with the State and people.",""]],"116":[[1,"100","4","Gender Equality in Education, Employment, Health Care, and Leadership","With the target of gender equality in education and training, employment, health care and participation in leadership and managerial work, by 2010 Vietnam strives for illiteracy eradication among women under 40, increased number of women in the total newly employed, and increased number of trained women in the workforce.",""],[1,"100","5","Women Staff Planning and Training Programme","Implement the planning and training of women staff in order to generate sources of potential staffs for replacement and promotion in response to new requirements.",""],[1,"100","6","Women’s Employment Equality and Labor Support Measures","Ensure the conditions for women to enjoy equality in employment and labor through the provision of sufficient cultivating lands and fundamental resources; define clear targets of women recruitment in new jobs.",""],[1,"100","6","Women Workers Policy Enforcement and Regulatory Oversight","Complete regulations and intensify the supervision of the implementation of policies on women laborers to ensure efficiency and fairness in policies on vocational training, social insurance and retirement.",""],[1,"100","6","Sex-Disaggregated Labor Market and Training Database Development","Build up databases of the labor market and vocational training with information and data disaggregated on the basis of sex.",""],[1,"100","6","Women’s Vocational Training and Job Center Development","Develop vocational training and job centers for women.",""],[1,"100","6","Preferential Incentives for Women-Employing Enterprises","Implement preferential policies for agencies and enterprises with 70% women employees.",""],[1,"100","6","Women’s Access to Credit and Poverty Reduction Funds","Intensify women's access to credit sources and funds from hunger eradication and poverty reduction programs, facilitate women to be trained how to directly use such funds.",""]],"117":[[1,"101","1","Women’s Equal Access to Education and Training Measures","Take measures to ensure women' equal access to education, science, technology and training for professional improvement.",""],[1,"101","1","Scientific and Technological Training for Production","Deliver training to improve scientific and technological knowledge to be applied to production.",""],[1,"101","1","Incentive Policies for Girls’ School Enrollment","Issue incentive policies to encourage girls in remote, hinterlands and ethnic minority areas to enroll in boarding schools, high schools, colleges and universities.",""],[1,"101","1","Support for Poor Women and Girls’ Schooling","Implement policies to support poor women and girls to go to school.",""],[1,"101","1","Gender Mainstreaming in Vocational Training","Take measures to adjust gender discrepancies and segregation in terms of fields of study, and mainstream gender issues in vocational training programs.",""],[1,"101","1","Women’s Advancement in Educational Management","Increase the number of women in managerial positions at all educational levels and grades.",""],[1,"101","1","Female Study Encouragement Funds","Establish study encouragement funds for females and identify the number of women in training and retraining courses at all levels and sectors.",""]],"118":[[1,"101","3","Household Chore Reduction through Small-Scale Domestic Technology","Gradually reduce household chore burdens on women through investing in small-scaled technology for domestic purposes, in clean water and power supply projects in rural areas.",""],[1,"101","3","Pre-School and Nursery System Reorganization","Develop and reorganize pre-school and nursery systems.",""],[1,"101","3","Family Responsibility Sharing Campaign","Launch propaganda campaigns on responsibility sharing among all family members.",""]],"119":[[1,"102","6","Implementation of the Law on Youth and National Youth Development Strategy","Develop and well implement the Law on Youth and the National Strategy for Youth Development, in which young people are placed in an important position in national construction and protection, and are the driving force for the development of the country.",""],[1,"102","7","Issue Issue-Specific Policies for Youth Development Strategy Implementation","Issue specific policies to well perform the National Strategy for Youth Development.",""],[1,"102","8","Youth Facilitative Policy for Vanguard Service in Disadvantaged Areas","Promulgate facilitative policies for youth to perform their vanguard roles and voluntarily complete important tasks in the socio-economic development in disadvantaged areas, remote and hinterlands areas and important areas of the county so that they can be the pioneer forces in all fronts from socio-economic development to security maintenance and readiness to defend the country.",""],[1,"102","9","Youth Volunteer Mobilization and Social Problem Prevention Measures","Promulgate policies to mobilize and encourage young people to participate in voluntary movements against social problems and solving social controversial issues.",""],[1,"102","9","Youth Delinquency Prevention and Moral Education Measures","Take practical measures to prevent, constrain and reduce the number of young people involved in illegal activities and to educate them to become good people.",""],[1,"102","10","Vocational Training and Youth Employment Support","Expand vocational training for young people, support them in job finding through numerous methods.",""],[1,"102","10","Youth Entrepreneurship Associations and Business Clubs","Develop Young Entrepreneurs' associations, and Young Businesses' clubs to attract the participation of all youths.",""],[1,"102","11","Basic Social Services Access Support for Rural and Disadvantaged Youth","Help young people in rural, disadvantaged, remote and hinterlands areas in their access to basic social services like education, health care, exchanges and development.",""],[1,"102","12","Youth Science and Technology Development Support","Implement solutions to promote science and technology development among young people.",""],[1,"102","12","Youth Participation in Rural Poverty Reduction","Work out policies on assisting and encouraging youths to actively involve in hunger eradication and poverty reduction in rural, remote and hinterlands areas.",""]],"120":[[1,"108","8","Border Patrol Infrastructure Construction","push up the construction of border patrolling lines, roads and the system of border guard offices and stations.",""],[1,"108","8","National Defense Economic Zone Completion","Basically complete national defense economic zones according to approved planning.",""],[1,"108","8","Vietnam-China Border Delineation and Demarcation","Complete the work of Vietnam - China border delineation and demarcation.",""],[1,"108","8","Border Population Relocation and Settlement Support Policy","Install policies for the promotion of population re-location and settlement along the borders, ensure fundamental conditions for the life and production of ethnic minorities in mountainous, border areas and military bases.",""]],"121":[[1,"108","10","Search and Rescue Services Planning and Core Disaster Response Units","Organize the planning of the search and rescue services for the period of 2006-2010, attach importance to the establishment of some core units for the prevention and relief of natural disasters and catastrophes, as well as the formation of search and rescue teams in the armed forces, aviation, navy, and petroleum and gas sector.",""]],"122":[[1,"109","1","Social Security and Order Maintenance","Ensure social security and order, prevention against drug-related crimes, criminals and other social problems.",""],[1,"109","1","Road Accident Reduction Effort","Maintain the strong reduction of road accidents and this should become the task of everyone and the whole society; attach importance to the provision of material facilities to those who directly implement the tasks.",""]],"123":[[1,"109","3","Regional Economic Center and Industrial Zone Development","Concentrate on the development of large and critical economic centers, improve the effectiveness of the existing industrial and export processing zones, and at the same time develop new industrial, export processing zones and industrial clusters to motivate the strong and sustainable development of all economic regions.",""],[1,"109","3","Regional Coordination Strengthening Initiative","Strengthen the coordination among regions, and in each region itself to overcome the drawback of administrative territorial division.",""],[1,"109","3","River Basin Resource Cooperation","Expand cooperation with countries in the region to manage natural resources along the river basins.",""],[1,"109","4","Development of Key Economic Zones","For three key economic zones (Northern, Central and Southern): gradually execute socio- economic development tasks according to Resolutions of the Politburo and Decisions of the Prime Minister84 on the main orientation of socio-economic development of key economic regions- North, Central and South- to motivate the development of powerful economic corporations, which then creates good environment for active large-scale international cooperation at high levels.",""],[1,"109","4","Industrial and Export Processing Zone Development","Concentrate on the development of industrial and export processing zones, and high-tech industrial zones on the basis of combining as much as possible the existing capacities and build more new facilities to create a driving force for development processes.",""],[1,"109","4","National Highway and Interregional Road Infrastructure Expansion","Build up comprehensive infrastructure systems, especially the system of highways and interregional roads to encourage interregional development and international cooperation.",""],[1,"109","4","Economic Corridor Development Along National Highways","Speed up the development of some important economic corridors along with national highway routes.",""],[1,"109","4","Urban System and Townlet Development","Develop modern urban systems; establish medium and small urban centers (townlets and townships) in rural areas with potential for economic development.",""],[1,"109","4","Scientific and Technological Capacity Development","Develop scientific and technological potentials, especially advanced technology, and produce new materials; develop high-quality services such as postal and communications, banking.",""],[1,"109","4","Vocational Training Network Expansion","Invest in developing vocational training networks as planned; build up 25 vocational training secondary schools and colleges satisfying standards, among which at least 5 schools meeting international standards in order to train high-skilled laborers for the whole region.",""],[1,"109","4","Expanded Mekong River Sub-region Economic Corridor Development","Establish and efficiently develop economic corridors in the expanded Mekong river sub- region.",""]],"124":[[1,"110","7","Agricultural Structural Shift and Diversification Programme","Continue economic structural shift in order to best develop economic efficiency and potentials of the region.",""],[1,"110","7","Crop and Livestock Development Expansion","Develop areas of industrial crops, medicinal plants, aromatic plants, fruit trees, flowers, vegetables for domestic market and export; develop livestock raising and agricultural products, animal husbandry in areas where natural",""],[1,"111","1","Advanced Livestock Raising Support","conditions and climate allow, especially raising buffalos, cows according to advanced technical methods.",""],[1,"111","1","Land and Forest Allocation for Sedentary Communities","Complete the allocation of land and forest to people associated with sedentation; solve the problem of long-term residential and cultivation lands.",""],[1,"111","3","Agro-Food Industry Development and Industrial Zone Upgrading","Develop tea, milk and other agro-food industries, etc., continue to expand and improve the quality and efficiency of the local industrial zones and clusters.",""],[1,"111","3","Small-Scale Industry and Traditional Trade Village Development","Attach importance to the development of small-scaled industry and traditional trade villages.",""],[1,"111","6","Rural and Agricultural Market Development","Develop the system of rural markets and agricultural product markets.",""],[1,"111","6","Farmer Contracting for Agricultural and Forestry Product Sales","Encourage various economic sectors to underwrite contracts with farmers for the sale of agricultural and forestry products, and for export.",""]],"125":[[1,"111","2","Hydropower Plant Construction and Expansion Programme","speed up the construction of Son La Hydropower Plant and other hydropower plants in the watershed of Da and Lo rivers, develop small- and medium-scale hydropower plants, and coal-fired thermal power plants.",""],[1,"111","2","Mineral Mining and Processing Expansion","Effectively mine and process minerals of mineral mines in the region.",""],[1,"111","2","Construction Materials and Chemicals Manufacturing Development","Build factories that produce construction materials and chemicals on the basis of the local natural resources.",""],[1,"111","2","Paper and Pulp Plant Development","Build paper and pulp plants adaptable to the development of the raw material supply areas.",""]],"126":[[1,"111","4","Tourism Site Investment and Development Programme","give priority to investment in and exploitation of tourist points: Dien Bien Phu, historical monuments in Pac Bo, Tan Trao, Dinh Hoa, Hung Temple, Sa pa, Ba Be Lake, Nui Coc Lake, Da Reservoir, etc., with various tourist models, especially ecological tourism, health and spa tourism, cultural and historical tourism",""],[1,"111","5","Border-Gate Economic Zone Development Programme","Develop border-gate economic zones, expand cross-border cultural exchanges, concentrate on the construction of infrastructures for border-gate economic zones; establish and develop services of finance and banking, import and export, post and telecommunications, transportation as well as information technology, etc.",""],[1,"111","7","Economic Infrastructure Upgrading and Construction Programme","Develop economic infrastructure structures: complete the upgrading of national highways 2, 3, 6, 32, especially roads to border crossings, border belt roads, and border patrolling roads; invest in building highway stretches Hanoi-Thai Nguyen, Ho Chi Minh road, main road stretch of Ha Noi - Lao Cai, Ha Noi - Lang Son corridors and other highway lines; upgrade railway routes Ha Noi - Lao Cai, Ha Noi - Thai Nguyen, Kep - Luu Xa, Dien Bien Phu, Na San airports and main riverway routes; repair and upgrade irrigation works in provinces of the area.",""],[1,"112","1","Border Economic Zone and Trade Center Development","Attach importance to the development of economic zones along the borders.",""]],"127":[[1,"112","7","Red River Delta Regional Development Initiative","Build up the Red River Delta as a strongly developed region in terms of cultural, economic and social development, asserting itself as a focal point for regional and international exchanges and cooperation, helping other regions, particularly Northern mountainous and midland regions to develop.",""],[1,"113","2","High-Tech Industry Development and Industrial Upgrading","focus on the strong development of hi-tech industries like software and computer accessories, automatic industries so that they can truly become key industries.",""],[1,"113","2","Industrial Materials and Steel Production Upgrading","Produce new materials, cement; interior furniture and roofing materials; strongly shift to the production of high quality steel, steel sheets, steel plates, engineered steel and electronic products.",""],[1,"113","2","Machinery, Shipbuilding, and Heavy Equipment Industry Establishment","Establish machinery manufacturing and engineering, shipbuilding, construction machines, electricity, coal, garments and textiles.",""],[1,"113","2","High-Quality Consumer Goods Production Initiative","Produce high quality consumer goods.",""],[1,"113","2","High-Tech Industry Establishment Initiative","Establish high-tech industries.",""],[1,"113","3","Industrial Zone Development in City Outskirts and Economic Corridors","Plan and develop industrial zones in the outskirts of big cities, associated with economic corridors along National Highways No18, 5, 1, 10.",""],[1,"113","3","Van Don Economic Complex Establishment","Establish Van Don economic complex (Quang Ninh).",""],[1,"113","3","Nam Dinh Urban Industrial and Training Center Development","Build up Nam Dinh city into an industrial, service and training center, which serves as the development core of the sub-region in the South of the Red River delta.",""]],"128":[[1,"113","4","Agricultural Industrialization and Modernization Programme","Implement the industrialization and modernization of agriculture and rural areas.",""],[1,"113","4","Organic and High-Tech Agricultural Transformation","Transform economic structures in agriculture and rural areas adaptive to the development of organic farming along with high technology and biotechnology.",""],[1,"113","4","High-Quality Commodity Production Centers","Establish high quality commodity centers, areas for rice, vegetables, pigs, dairy cows, cattle, poultry, flowers and bonsais cultivation in appropriate volumes to serve export and organic food supply for local people, and strongly develop marine economy.",""],[1,"113","4","Vocational Training and Rural Employment Linkage","Speed up vocational training in close link with creating jobs, developing small- and medium-scaled handicraft industry and rural industry.",""],[1,"113","7","Agricultural Extension Service Improvement","Repair and upgrade the systems of river and sea dykes, and improve agricultural extension services.",""]],"129":[[1,"113","5","Modern Trading Center Development","Establish modern trading centers of regional and international standards.",""],[1,"113","5","Regional Tourism Development Programme","Strongly develop tourism in the region, making tourism become a key economic activity.",""],[1,"113","5","Hanoi Tourism Investment Initiative","Take advantage of the capital to develop tourism in Hanoi and vicinities; invest in the construction of the national holiday resort in Ha Long - Cat Ba, Hoa Lu - Trang An - Ninh Binh.",""],[1,"113","5","Inter-Regional Tourist Route Development","The development of provincial tourist attractions should be combined with other tourist spots inside and outside the regions to establish clear intra-regional and inter- regional tourist routes.",""],[1,"113","5","High-Quality Services Development Priority","Give priority to the development of high quality services like financial and banking, information and communication, training, science and technology.",""]],"130":[[1,"113","6","Road Infrastructure Upgrade Programme","Build and upgrade roads;",""],[1,"113","6","Airport, Seaport, and Railway Modernization Programme","expand and upgrade some airports, seaports and railways.",""],[1,"113","6","Hanoi Urban Infrastructure Modernization Programme","Comprehensively develop and gradually modernize urban infrastructures of Hanoi.",""],[1,"113","6","Regional Urban Connectivity Initiative","Link Hanoi with the development of other cities and towns in the region like Hai Duong, Hai Phong, Ha Dong, Bac Ninh, Vinh Yen, Ninh Binh, Nam Dinh, etc.",""],[1,"113","6","Gie Bridge - Ninh Binh - Thanh Hoa Highway Project","Build Gie Bridge - Ninh Binh - Thanh Hoa highway route at the soonest time.",""],[1,"113","6","Red River Waterway Transport and Tourism Improvement","Improve the transport system on the Red River to make it become waterway transport and tourism route of the region.",""],[1,"113","7","Postal and Telecommunications Development","Develop postal and telecommunications, information technology to become critical and effective technological economy.",""],[1,"113","7","Urban Electricity and Water Network Upgrading","Continue to improve and upgrade electricity and water supply networks in cities, towns and townships; strive for the reduction of loss, leakages and waste in distribution and consumption.",""],[1,"113","7","River and Sea Dyke Rehabilitation","Repair and upgrade the systems of river and sea dykes, and improve agricultural extension services.",""]],"131":[[1,"113","8","Establishment of Focal Universities","Establish a number of focal universities, especially those specialized in technology.",""],[1,"113","8","Modern Scientific and Technological Research Network","Build up the modern scientific and technological research network of some important fields, especially centers for breed research and technological innovation.",""],[1,"113","8","Hoa Lac High-Tech Zone Construction","Speed up the construction of Hoa Lac hi- tech zone, which links with Lang - Hoa Lac - Xuan Mai urban network.",""],[1,"113","9","Healthcare Service Development and Hospital Upgrading Programme","Develop healthcare services, improve people's physical and mental health; invest in comprehensive hospital system in provinces and cities, upgrade district hospitals to meet people's demands of health check and treatment, reduce overloads for hospitals in Hanoi",""],[1,"114","1","Completion of Hanoi Specialized Medical Center Investment","Complete the investment in Hanoi specialized medical center.",""]],"132":[[1,"114","2","Urban and Rural Environmental Improvement Programme","Ensure the environment in big cities, industrial zones, trade villages, and eco-environment in rural areas.",""],[1,"114","2","Polluted River Restoration Initiative","Improve the environment of polluted rivers as Day, Nhue, Cau, Tich, and Chau Rivers.",""]],"133":[[1,"114","3","Regional Socio-Economic Development Acceleration for Key Areas","Speed up the socio-economic development of the Northern Central area, Central costal area and key economic regions to soon catch up with development of other regions in the country and become one of the whole country's focal points for international exchanges and cooperation;",""],[1,"114","4","Development and Operation of Approved Economic Zones","Develop economic zones: concentrate efforts on development and effective operation of economic zones that have received the approval of the Prime Minister to establish, including Vung Ang, Chan May-Lang Co, Chu Lai, Dzung Quat, Nhon Hoi and Van Phong economic zones.",""],[1,"114","7","Dung Quat Oil Refining and Petrochemical Plant Construction","Build Dung Quat oil refining and petrochemical plant as scheduled",""],[1,"114","7","Nghi Son Oil Refinery Investment Mobilization","attract capital resources for investment in Nghi Son oil refinery",""],[1,"114","7","Thach Khe Iron Mine and Vung Ang Metallurgy Complex Development","prepare for the implementation of Thach Khe iron mine development project together with the construction of a metallurgy complex in Vung Ang (Ha Tinh)",""],[1,"114","7","Shipbuilding and Ship Repair Factory Development","Establish shipbuilding and ship repair factories",""],[1,"114","7","Cement Plant Construction in Planned Resource Areas","Build cement plants in planned areas with available raw materials",""]],"134":[[1,"114","8","Agricultural and Industrial Processing Development","Develop agriculture, forestry and fishery product processing, textile, leather and garment industries.",""],[1,"114","8","Regional Paper Pulp Plant Construction","Build new Thanh Hoa, Nghe An and Binh Dinh paper pulp plants adaptive to raw material supply capacities of the region.",""],[1,"114","8","Industrial Salt Production Expansion","Push up the salt production, especially industrial salt production.",""],[1,"114","10","Agriculture and Aquaculture Development Programme","Agriculture and aquaculture development: Develop agriculture by improving commodity production, improving land use efficiency, adaptive to severe weathers.",""],[1,"114","10","Raw Materials Production and Agro-Processing Linkage Programme","Plan intensive production of raw materials for production associated with processing industry, with emphasis on short-term crops (sugar canes, peanuts, tobacco, and cotton trees) and perennial industrial crops (cashew, coffee, pineapple, tea, rubber, pepper trees), fruit trees, and effectively develop Western part of the region.",""],[1,"114","10","Livestock Development at Reasonable Scale","Develop livestock raising at reasonable scales.",""]],"135":[[1,"114","9","Hydropower and Irrigation Construction Acceleration","Speed up the construction of hydropower plants combined with irrigation.",""],[1,"114","9","National Power Grid Expansion to All Communes","Fundamentally complete the expansion of the national power grid to all communes in the region.",""]],"136":[[1,"114","10","Protective Forest and Watershed Conservation Programme","Focus on nurturing and preserve protective forests and watersheds to reduce flood, retain water and ensure safety for irrigation and hydropower works in the region.",""],[1,"115","7","Upstream Irrigation Works Upgrade and Flood Prevention Restoration","Upgrade big irrigation works upstream to prevent floods, generate electricity and water in dry seasons as well as to protect the environment.",""],[1,"115","7","Central Area Irrigation Development Programme","develop irrigation in Central areas; combine irrigation works with flood prevention.",""],[1,"115","8","University Quality Improvement and Regional Research Center Development","Invest in educational quality improvement in the universities of Vinh, Hue, Da Nang, make them become interdisciplinary training centers and scientific research centers of the region.",""],[1,"115","9","High-Tech Medical Center Construction and Provincial Hospital Upgrading","Speed up the construction of hi-tech intensive medical centers in Hue and Da Nang, invest in the new construction and upgrades of provincial hospitals in the region, construct regional medical centers in Vinh and Nha Trang.",""],[1,"115","10","Eco-Environment Maintenance and Protective Forest Development","ensure the maintenance of the eco-environment, protect and develop coastal protective forests and upstream forests to contribute to the reduction of natural disasters' consequences.",""]],"137":[[1,"116","1","Integrated Central Highlands Regional Development","To make full use of its land, geological position and natural conditions, its strategic position, helping the Central Highlands to develop comprehensively and in sustainable manner in terms of economy, politics, culture, society, national defense and security; and gradually become the driving force region.",""],[1,"116","1","Forest and Industrial Crop Processing Development","Regard the development of forest and industrial crops in combination with effective and comprehensive processing industry as an important breakthrough in developing the region and strengthening the construction of national defense economic zones.",""],[1,"116","1","Economic Restructuring and Job Creation","Attach much importance to economic structural shift and job creation.",""],[1,"116","1","Environmental Management and Livelihood Improvement for Ethnic Minority Areas","Gradually improve and protect the environment through efficiently managing natural resources, improving living standards of local people, especially people of ethnic minorities in remote, extremely difficult areas, areas of ethnic minority people in order to stimulate rapid growth rates help hunger eradication and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"116","4","Commercial Agriculture Development and Crop Diversification","commercial agriculture will continue to be steadily developed by diversifying agricultural production and making full use of the region's strengths of forestry and industrial crops.",""],[1,"116","4","Industrial Crop Intensification and Export Promotion","Intensive cultivation of industrial crops which are adaptable to the region's natural conditions with good yield and export market such as coffee, tea, rubber, cashew, peppers, cotton, medical herbs, fruit trees, etc., will be promoted in order to rapidly increase the efficiency of agricultural production and export.",""],[1,"116","4","Crop and Livestock Improvement Programme","Renovate crops and animal breeds, pay attention to developing cattle husbandry.",""],[1,"116","4","Integrated Forestry Development Programme","Develop the forestry effectively and comprehensively, including afforestation, exploitation, processing and forestry services in order to make it become the key region of forestry development of the whole country.",""],[1,"116","4","Land Reallocation and Ethnic Minority Livelihood Support","Transfer land fund of some agricultural farms and afforestation yards to settle the problem of housing and production land, in combination with rearranging production to create jobs and ensure the lives of ethnic minority people.",""],[1,"116","5","Industrial Development in Priority Sectors","Pay attention to suitable and advantaged industrial fields; develop the mining and processing industry of bauxite in Lam Dong, Daknong; processing industry of agricultural and forest products as coffee, rubber, tea, fine tapioca, cassava, fruits, vegetables, medical herbs; milk, livestock meat processing industry, etc .; mechanical industries, construction material industry, etc.",""],[1,"116","5","Hydropower Development and Irrigation Integration","Develop hydroelectric industry on different scales by diversifying the forms of electricity trade and investment; combine hydro power projects with small and medium irrigation works to serve local agricultural production as well as daily life electricity needs and contribute to the national power grid.",""],[1,"116","5","Acceleration of Key Regional Projects","Speed up the implementation of key projects in the region.",""],[1,"116","6","Industrial Zone Investment Attraction and Cluster Expansion","Attract investors in existing industrial zones, building more industrial clusters in the region.",""],[1,"116","6","Small-Scale Industry and Handicraft Development","Develop small-scaled industries and handicrafts.",""],[1,"116","7","Trade Services Network Development","Develop a diverse trade services network suitable to the local terrain.",""],[1,"116","7","Urban Market Hub and Commercial Center Construction","New market hubs and commercial centers will be gradually built in cities and towns",""],[1,"117","1","Trade and Service Supply Cooperative Development","Speed up the development of models of trade and service supply cooperatives; production based on consumption contracts, good organization of input and output supply services for production, timely transportation of subsidized commodities for ethnic minority people.",""],[1,"117","1","Rural Market and Trade Village Network Development","Develop the network of rural markets and trade villages in areas of local minority people.",""],[1,"117","1","Border-Gate Economic Zone Development","Develop and effectively operate border-gate economies in border- gate economic zones Bo Y, Duc Co, borderline markets linked with Southern Laos and Cambodia.",""],[1,"117","1","Establishment of Dak Per and BuPang Border-Gate Economic Zones","Study to further establish Dak Per and BuPang border-gate economic zones in Daknong.",""],[1,"117","1","Central Highlands Tourism Development","Strongly develop tourist trade in the Central Highland; develop potential tourist centers and ecological tourism in the region.",""],[1,"117","2","Ho Chi Minh Highway and Regional Road Network Development","Take Ho Chi Minh Highway as the artery to develop side roads, feeder roads, border roads, border patrol routes, upgrade road links to Laos and Cambodia, upgrade critical national roads; focus investment in rural transport systems, particularly in remote, mountainous areas.",""],[1,"117","2","Agricultural Irrigation System Development","Develop irrigation systems in combination with service provision to agriculture and people's life;",""],[1,"117","2","Regional Airport Utilization and Investment","invest in and make use of existing airports in the region; complete water supply systems in cities and towns in the region.",""]],"138":[[1,"117","3","School, Clinic, Hospital, and Cultural Center Construction and Improvement","Investment will continue to be made for new construction and improvement of schools, clinics, hospitals, cultural centers, especially in remote areas and ethnic communities.",""],[1,"117","3","Tay Nguyen University Completion","Complete the construction of Tay Nguyen University.",""],[1,"117","3","Central Highlands Medical Center Development","Develop medical centers in the Central Highlands based on developing Dak Lak General Hospital.",""],[1,"117","3","Commune Medical Station Staffing Upgrade","Concretize all commune medical stations with enough professional health care staffs.",""],[1,"117","3","Ethnic Language Broadcasting Expansion","Increase on-air time for broadcasts in ethnic languages, promote community activities to preserve their original cultural identities.",""],[1,"117","3","Ethnic Minority Cultural Preservation Programme","Preserve and develop cultures of ethnic minorities in Central Highland.",""],[1,"117","3","Cultural-Information Activities Implementation of Decision No. 25/2004/QD-TTg","Rapidly complete procedures in order to execute the Decision No 25/2004/QD-TTg dated on February 27th, 2004 by the Prime Minister on \"Development of cultural-information activities of the Central Highland until 2010\".",""],[1,"117","3","Buon Ma Thuot Sports and Physical Training Center Construction","Build the sport and physical training center in Buon Ma Thuot; build sport and physical training units for villages.",""],[1,"117","3","Village Sports and Physical Training Units","Build the sport and physical training center in Buon Ma Thuot; build sport and physical training units for villages.",""],[1,"117","3","Ecological Environment Protection","Ensure the ecological environment.",""]],"139":[[1,"118","2","Oil and Gas Mine Development and Power Infrastructure Expansion","Continue to explore and put into operation new oil and gas mines; develop power sources and power transmission lines.",""],[1,"118","3","Investment Promotion in Industrial and Processing Zones and Hi-Tech Zone","Encourage investment in industrial and processing zones, hi-tech zone in Ho Chi Minh City.",""],[1,"118","4","Commercial Agriculture Development and Diversification","Commercial agriculture will continue to be steadily developed by diversifying agricultural commodities with high efficiency to aim at high quality and clean agriculture which will be able to sufficiently supply for processing industries, for household consumption in cities and industrial parks and for export.",""],[1,"118","4","Intensive Shrimp and Freshwater Fish Farming Development","Develop intensive shrimp farming and freshwater fish raising in irrigation works.",""],[1,"118","4","Aquatic Variety Centers, Trade Centers, and Hi-tech Fishery Processing Plants","Construct centers providing aquatic varieties, trade centers and hi-tech fishery processing plants.",""]],"140":[[1,"118","4","Coastal Protection Forest Expansion","Increase coast protection forests.",""],[1,"118","4","Mangrove Forest Conservation in Coastal Areas","Maintain the areas of mangrove forests in Can Gio district (Ho Chi Minh City) and of the coastal forests in Ba Ria-Vung Tau.",""]],"141":[[1,"118","5","Commercial Center and Tourism Development Network","Establish a network of commercial centers with equal scale and quality to those in other countries in the region.",""],[1,"118","5","Ho Chi Minh City Tourism and Trade Hub Development","While Ho Chi Minh will be built as a great center of tourism and trade, more effort will be made to develop services in Vung Tau Bien Hoa and Con Dao, and ecotourism in Cat Tien forests.",""],[1,"118","5","Border Trade and Border Gate Economy Strengthening","Border trading and border gates economy in border provinces will be strengthened.",""],[1,"118","5","Services Sector Development in Shipping, Telecommunications, Finance, Banking, and Oil","Develop shipping, telecommunication, finance and banking, and oil services, etc.",""],[1,"118","6","Tourism Infrastructure and Heritage Tourism Development","Focus on investment to upgrade tourism infrastructure, improve hotel system to conform to international standards, develop a network of leisure centers; maintain and restore historical and cultural sites as well as organize traditional festivals for tourism.",""],[1,"118","6","Regional Coastal and Ecotourism Development","In addition to big tourism and service centers in Ho Chi Minh city, coastal services and tourism will be developed in Vung Tau, Con Dao, Binh Chau, Ba Den, Section D military Base, Soc Bom Bo, ecotourism in Cat Tien forests (Dong Nai).",""]],"142":[[1,"118","7","Ho Chi Minh City Multi-Center Urban and Transport Infrastructure Development","Develop Ho Chi Minh City as a multi-center city, linked with other provinces in the region through modernized routes.",""],[1,"118","7","New Towns and National Highway Network Expansion","Establish new towns and highways and complete a network of national highways; improve waterways; modernize international airports; effectively utilize existing seaports and gradually build up a cluster of seaports and peripheral road systems.",""],[1,"118","7","Cargo Port Construction and Fish Port Modernization","Gradually invest in the construction of cargo ports; modernize fish ports in the region.",""]],"143":[[1,"118","8","Expansion of Higher Education and Vocational Training Network","Focus on capacity building and expansion of education programs at universities in Ho Chi Minh City and peripheral cities; build up a network of universities, colleges and vocational institutions according to the construction plan approved by the Prime Minister.",""],[1,"118","8","Technical Worker Training Center in Ho Chi Minh City","Establish technical worker training center in Ho Chi Minh City to provide skilled workers for the region, especially high-tech skilled workers for prioritized sectors.",""],[1,"118","8","Migrant Social Welfare and Basic Services Access","Ensure social welfares and access to basic social services for migrants to urban areas and their families equal to local residents.",""],[1,"118","9","Health Service Quality Improvement and Hospital Upgrading","Improve the quality of health services to meet the demands of local people, foreigners working in the region and tourists.",""],[1,"118","9","Leading and Provincial Hospital Upgrade Investment","Investment will be made to upgrade leading hospitals and provincial general hospitals.",""],[1,"118","9","Specialized Health Center Investment in Ho Chi Minh City","Accelerate investment in specialized health centers in Ho Chi Minh City.",""]],"144":[[1,"119","1","Urban Environmental and Water Quality Control","Strictly control environmental conditions in cities, towns, industrial parks and highly populated areas.",""],[1,"119","1","Sai Gon and Dong Nai River Water Quality Management","Control the environmental condition and water quality in Sai Gon, Dong Nai Rivers and canals in the City.",""],[1,"119","1","Urban Flood Mitigation Programme","Completely settle the problem of flooding in big cities, particularly Ho Chi Minh City.",""]],"145":[[1,"119","2","Mekong Delta Focal Economic Zone Development","develop Mekong Delta as a national focal economic zone with high, effective and sustainable growth rates",""],[1,"119","2","Agricultural Industrialization and Rural Modernization Programme","promote industrialization and modernization in agriculture and rural areas to establish a large-scale and specialized commodity-producing region",""],[1,"119","2","Socio-Cultural Conditions Improvement for Local Communities","improve the socio-cultural conditions to be in line with the national average standards, improve the spiritual and material life of local people, especially Khmer people and people in flood-prone areas",""],[1,"119","2","Integrated Socio-Economic and Environmental Protection Approach","socio-economic development is to be closely related to environmental protection, political stabilization, ensured social security and defense",""],[1,"120","5","Can Tho Urban and Regional Center Development","Develop Can Tho city as an industrial, commercial, service, tourism, educational cultural, economic, technical and scientific center; Can Tho also serves as a medical center and a critical transport hub of the whole region which links Can Tho with the Southeastern, with other regions in the country as well as Cambodia and other countries.",""],[1,"120","5","Flood-Prone Area Residential Safety Upgrading","complete residential areas to ensure safety for people in flood-prone areas.",""],[1,"120","6","Education and Training Development Programme","Develop education and training: increase the intellectual standard of local people, strengthen vocational training and higher education.",""]],"146":[[1,"119","5","Ecological Tropical Agriculture Diversification Programme","Develop an ecological tropical agriculture by diversifying crops based on the strategic advantages of sub-regions, establish intensively cultivated areas with crops of high value, good quality, especially rice, fruit trees and industrial crops.",""],[1,"119","5","Rice Area Maintenance and High-Value Export Rice Development","Maintain rice- growing areas of 1.8 million hectares, out of which 1 million hectares is for rice of high value for export.",""],[1,"119","5","Fruit Tree and Industrial Crop Supply Development","Develop fruit trees and industrial crops to provide raw materials for industry and animal feeds plants.",""],[1,"119","5","Aquaculture, Fishery and Seafood Processing Export Development","Develop aquaculture, fishery and seafood processing industry as the focal export sectors in Mekong Delta.",""],[1,"119","7","Agricultural and Fishery Product Processing Industry Development","Strongly develop agricultural and fishery product processing industry.",""],[1,"119","7","Artistic Ceramics Export Quality Improvement","Improve the quality and quantity of artistic ceramics production for export.",""]],"147":[[1,"119","5","Coastal Mangrove and Wetland Forest Conservation and Expansion","Preserve and develop coastal mangrove forests, Phu Quoc primitive forest; expand cajuput forests in the wetland and alum-contaminated areas in Dong Thap Muoi, Long Xuyen Tetragon, western side of Hau River and Ca Mau peninsula.",""],[1,"119","6","Irrigation System Completion and Decentralized Management","Complete the irrigation systems with decentralized management from central to local levels, ensuring irrigation for agricultural production in the region.",""],[1,"120","3","Flood-Resilient Transport Infrastructure Development","Develop traffic system to conform to flood control measures.",""],[1,"120","3","Multi-purpose Irrigation System Completion","Complete multi-purpose irrigation systems to serve cultivation, husbandry, aquaculture, processing industry, services and people's life.",""]],"148":[[1,"119","7","Southwestern Sea Gas-Electricity-Fertilizer Industry Development","Exploit gas reserves in Southwestern Sea to develop gas-electricity-fertilizer industry.",""],[1,"119","7","Ca Mau Gas-Electricity-Fertilizer Complex Construction","accelerate the construction of gas- electricity-fertilizer producing complex in Ca Mau.",""],[1,"119","7","Cement and Construction Materials Productivity Improvement","Continue to improve productivity and quality of plants for cement, concrete, bricks and tiles, building components.",""],[1,"119","7","Agro- and Fishery-Machinery Engineering Development","Develop agro- and fishery-machinery engineering industries.",""]],"149":[[1,"119","8","Can Tho Trade and Tourism Center Development","Establish trade and tourism centers in Can Tho as a focal point for trading in the region and with other regions.",""],[1,"119","8","Tourism Diversification in Can Tho","Take advantage of its geographical location and biodiversity to rapidly develop various types of tourism: garden tour, eco-tour, river tour, marine and island tour in close links with Ho Chi Minh City, southern focal economic",""],[1,"120","2","Phu Quoc Economic Zone Stepwise Investment Program","Make stepwise investment in Phu Quoc economic zone, building it into a large, modern center for tourism, recreation and international trade like others in the region and in the world.",""]],"150":[[1,"120","3","Rural, Remote, and Border Area Transport Upgrading","Focus on traffic system in rural, remote and border areas, provide favorable conditions for former wartime bases, islands and difficult areas.",""],[1,"120","3","Mekong Delta Transport Corridor Development","Establish traffic route connecting the Mekong Delta with the Southeastern and other parts of the country (National Road 1A, National Road 60 along the coast, Roads N1, N2 along the border, the motorway from Ho Chi Minh City to Can Tho.",""],[1,"120","3","Provincial and National Highway Upgrading","Upgrade all provincial and national highways.",""],[1,"120","3","Road, Waterway, Port, Railway, and Airport Upgrading","Upgrade all national roads, provincial roads and waterways bypassing cities and towns along the National Road No1, river ports and seaports system in the Mekong Delta; initiate preparations to restore the railway route Ho Chi Minh City-My Tho; upgrade and expand airports.",""],[1,"120","3","Water, Electricity, and Telecommunications Service Expansion","Develop systems for water supply, electricity supply and telecommunication services.",""]],"151":[[1,"123","10","Comprehensive Veterinary Services Investment","Invest in comprehensive veterinary services to deal with poultry, cattle and aquaculture-related diseases.",""]],"152":[[1,"121","1","Coastal and Marine Development Planning","Intensify developmental planning for coastal, marine areas and islands; ensure sustainable development for them; provide optimal conditions for the development of marine tourism.",""],[1,"121","1","Marine Enterprise Consolidation and Sector Development","Consolidate existing marine enterprises and develop new marine economic sectors with focus on the quality of marine enterprises.",""],[1,"121","1","Marine Economic Sector Development","Develop sectors which have been considered as focal marine economic sectors such as seaports and shipping enterprises, oil extraction and refinery, fishery and aquaculture, and sea-based tourism.",""],[1,"121","1","Coastal and Island Urban and Industrial Development","Develop and improve coastal and island towns, industrial zones, and coastal processing factories.",""],[1,"121","1","Offshore and Coastal Infrastructure Development","Establish consistent off-shore and coastal infrastructure to gradually establish marine developed centers, and to prepare for breakthrough in marine economy after 2010.",""],[1,"121","2","Marine Economy Focal Sector Development","Establish basic components to develop focal development sectors under marine economy.",""],[1,"121","6","Development of Major Maritime Trade Centers","Focus on the development of big trade centers in some maritime areas.",""],[1,"121","8","Coastal Industry Development and Shipbuilding Upgrade","Develop coastal industries with priority for oil and gas industry; improve capacity for production and maintenance of oil-rig devices.",""],[1,"121","9","Coastal Mineral Exploration and Extraction Programme","Promote research, exploration and extraction of minerals in coastal areas with short-term focus on coal and iron ore extraction.",""],[1,"122","3","Focal Investment in Coastal Industrial Parks","Continue focal investment in coastal industrial parks as initial conditions to build development centers toward open sea.",""],[1,"122","4","Marine and Coastal Development Planning","Effectively implement developmental planning for marine and coastal areas.",""],[1,"122","4","Marine Economic Development Strategy Action Plans","Develop detailed action plans to elaborate the Marine Economic Development Strategy; allow sectors and provinces to hire international consultants to design such planning for marine economic development centers.",""],[1,"122","4","Marine Research and Human Resource Development","Improve marine scientific and technological research institutions and train human resources for marine economy.",""]],"153":[[1,"121","7","Island and Coastal Tourism Development","Emphasize the development of island and coastal tourism",""],[1,"121","7","Tourist Center Cluster Development","Develop clusters of tourist centers",""],[1,"121","7","Hotel-School Tourism Training Centers","develop some training centers in the form of \"hotel + school\" in big coastal cities and regional tourist centers",""],[1,"122","6","Tourism Facilities and Heritage Preservation Investment","Make investments in tourism facilities in connection with preservation of historical and cultural sites; invest in ecological environment protection, natural disaster relief and urban infrastructure development.",""]],"154":[[1,"121","10","Fishery and Aquaculture Development Programme","Continue to develop fishery and aquaculture; by 2010 total seafood turnover is to amount to 4 million tons, including 2 million tons from fishery and 2 million tons from aquaculture.",""],[1,"121","10","Offshore Fishing Development Initiative","Develop fishery with focus on off-shore fishing; improve the quality of processed products to ensure the competitiveness and popularity of seafood products.",""],[1,"121","11","Salt Production Intensification and Expansion Programme","Promote salt production with focus on intensive methods and technological improvement; increase the productivity of existing salt fields and expand areas for salt production to 30,000-35,000 hectares by 2010.",""]],"155":[[1,"122","2","Coastal and Island Transport Infrastructure Upgrade","Upgrade some coastal airports and prepare for the construction of new airports. Upgrade coastal roads and roads around islands. Improve the provincial-level road system on islands for both economic and defense purposes.",""],[1,"122","2","Coastal and Offshore Basic Services Expansion","More efforts will be made to supply fresh water and electricity for coastal and off-shore areas.",""],[1,"122","2","Marine Communications, Fisheries Logistics, and Resource Survey Support","Improve the quality of communication facilities and fishing-related facilities, logistics and baseline surveys of marine resources.",""],[1,"122","6","Socio-Economic Infrastructure Investment Programme","Give priority to investments to improve the infrastructure of socio-economic sectors with emphasis on transportation, telecommunication, the development of energy resources, of central irrigation system, and of rural infrastructure, the expansion of agriculture production consistent with processing industry.",""],[1,"122","9","Private Investment in Socio-Economic Infrastructure","Encourage all economic sectors to invest in socio-economic infrastructure in order to make significant changes in infrastructure improvement as initial conditions for the country's economic development.",""],[1,"122","10","Timely Implementation of Approved National Projects and Programs","Effectively implement in a timely manner important projects of the country that are already approved by the National Assembly in term of investment direction, and other approved projects, national programs.",""],[1,"128","6","ODA Mobilization Strategy for Technical Infrastructure Investment","Develop strategies to attract and utilize investments from ODA, with focus on the construction of technical infrastructure in economic centers and economically disadvantaged areas to provide favorable conditions for investors to implement and expand their investment opportunities.",""]],"156":[[1,"122","5","Industrial Modernization and Production Structure Transformation Investment","Continue to make investments in strong transformation of production structure in economic sectors in the direction of reinforced advantages and improved effectiveness of each sector, each region and each product; more investments in modern technical facilities, modernize manufacture industry with emphasis on sectors or products with competitive advantages.",""],[1,"123","1","Industrial Investment Mobilization and Processing Industry Expansion","The targets of industrial investments are to quickly transform the industrial production structure in the direction of increased share of processing industries and diversifying products.",""],[1,"123","2","Industrial Investment and Technological Innovation Programme","Make intensive investments in power industry, construction material industry, high-tech and energy-efficient industries, electronics, information technology, supporting industry, manufacture industry for export, and industrial sectors serving agriculture and rural development.",""],[1,"123","2","Information Technology Innovation and Knowledge-Intensive Product Upgrade","Focus investment in technological innovation and increase knowledge content in IT products.",""],[1,"123","5","Industrial Machinery and Equipment Development Investment","Invest in the development of machinery for agriculture production and rural development, construction machinery, total machinery, ship building industry, automobile and motorbike industry, cement industry, paper industry, power industry, fertilizer and chemical industry.",""],[1,"123","7","Industrial Infrastructure Investment and Factory Relocation","Make intensive and comprehensive investment in industrial infrastructure, relocate textile and dying factories as planned, invest in the expansion of material-supplying areas.",""],[1,"123","7","Footwear Industry Upgrading and Input Supply Development","Accelerate investments to improve the production and quality of footwear industry, develop material supplies for this industry.",""],[1,"123","7","Beverage and Mineral Water Plant Expansion","Expand existing beer breweries; give priority in fruit-based beverage and mineral-water plants.",""],[1,"123","7","Agricultural Processing Plant Investment","Make intensive investments in agriculture- based processing plants.",""],[1,"123","8","Specialized Agricultural Production Zones and Processing Plant Development","Invest in the establishment of specialized zones of agricultural production, intensive cultivation for higher productivity in connection with processing industry development; build up processing plants in material-supplying areas.",""],[1,"129","8","Technology and Facility Modernization for Production Efficiency","Gradually renovate technologies and facilities, applying new scientific and technological advances to the production process to improve business and production efficiency.",""],[1,"129","8","Environment and Workplace Improvement in Production","Closely link production with environment protection and improved working conditions for employees.",""],[1,"129","8","Market Research and Product Quality Improvement","Carry out market research and improve the design, model and quality of goods with a view to meeting the needs of domestic and foreign markets.",""]],"157":[[1,"123","4","Mining Industry Modernization and Coal Mine Capacity Expansion","Invest in the modernization of mining industry, expand and improve the capacity of existing coal mines.",""],[1,"123","6","Cement Industry Investment and Technology Upgrade","Rapidly invest in cement factories under approved plans.",""],[1,"123","6","Cement Factory Furnace Replacement and Productivity Improvement","Repair or replace blast furnace technology by reverted furnace ones in some existing cement factories to improve their productivity and quality, making use of the facilities available.",""]],"158":[[1,"123","9","Investment in Science and Research Centers for Breeding","Make in-depth investments in science and research centers for animal and crop breeding of high productivity and good quality.",""],[1,"123","9","Facilities Development for Production Structure Transformation","Give priority to investments in facilities development for the transformation of production structure;",""],[1,"123","9","Irrigation System Improvement for Agriculture and Aquaculture","more investments will be made to improve irrigation system to ensure water circulation for agriculture and aquaculture.",""],[1,"123","10","Natural Disaster Warning Systems Strengthening","Strengthen warning systems for natural disasters.",""],[1,"123","10","Climate-Resilient Crop and Livestock Adaptation","Invest in changes to animals and crops with less water requirements.",""]],"159":[[1,"124","1","Urban Traffic System Development in Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City","Strongly develop traffic system in Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh Cities to gradually resolve traffic jams.",""],[1,"124","3","Urban Ring Road and Bypass Development","Initially develop rings and bypasses in big cities and towns.",""],[1,"124","3","Urban Transport and Residential Infrastructure Investment","Make comprehensive investments in developing new residential buildings; traffic system inside big cities;",""],[1,"124","3","Sedentary Traffic Facilities Development","Build up establishments for sedentary traffic.",""],[1,"124","3","Railway Network Expansion","Gradually build up railway network.",""],[1,"124","4","Railway Upgrade and Expansion Programme","Upgrade existing railways.",""],[1,"124","4","Rail Links to Seaports and Industrial Parks","Build up new routes for economic purposes to connect seaports and industrial parks.",""],[1,"124","4","Urban Railway Development in Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City","Initially develop railway system inside Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh City; build up elevated railway route Yen Vien-Giap Bat.",""],[1,"125","1","Urban Traffic System Improvement","Improve traffic systems in Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh and central cities.",""],[1,"125","2","Urban Transport Modernization and Congestion Reduction","Develop transport in urban areas in the direction of modernization, appropriateness and basically reduce traffic congestions in cities.",""]],"160":[[1,"124","7","Domestic Waterways Master Plan and Waterway Route Upgrading","Develop master plan for domestic waterways, river ports to be implemented in the period 2006-2010.",""],[1,"124","7","Investment in Key Waterway Route Upgrades","Continue investments to upgrade important waterway routes in the Mekong Delta and the Red River Delta.",""]],"161":[[1,"125","2","Urban Residential Quarter Development and Slum Upgrading","Develop new residential quarters, particularly in suburban areas to increase accommodation, combining urban development and maintenance of existing residential areas.",""],[1,"125","2","Urban Slum Elimination and Unsafe Housing Removal","Eliminate urban slums and repair or remove all unsafe houses in urban areas.",""],[1,"125","4","Housing Construction Continuation Programme","Continue housing construction to meet the accommodation demands of people in urban and rural areas.",""],[1,"125","5","Urban Housing Development and Rental Housing Support Policy","Develop new cities in the direction of modernization.",""]],"162":[[1,"125","3","Office and Institution Modernization Program","Implement Stage I of the Government's plan for office and institution modernization.",""],[1,"127","5","Judicial System Modernization Investment","Invest in the judicial system such as courts, prosecution institution to gradually modernize Government, National Assembly and Party offices.",""]],"163":[[1,"128","1","Land Use Planning and Resource Information Transparency","Provide favorable conditions for business investors by making land use planning and land resource information publicly accessible and transparent;",""],[1,"128","1","Industrial Park Development and Investor Land Access Support","build or support to build industrial parks with internal and external facilities: ensure basic rights of investors to land use.",""],[1,"128","1","Land and Water Surface Reclamation for Reallocation","Reclaim land and water surface of no or limited use from institutions, organizations or State-owned enterprises and provide it to other investors.",""],[1,"128","1","Integrated Water Resources Management","Ensure economical use and integrated management of water resources.",""],[1,"132","2","Foreign Investor Collateralization Mechanism","Institutionalize the mechanism that allows foreign investors to use as collateral their property, including land and values of their land use rights in accessing loans from credit institutions who are permitted to operation in Vietnam.",""],[1,"132","3","Unified Pricing System for Investors","Apply a unified pricing system for goods and services, land rent, compensations for site clearance to both domestic and foreign investors.",""]],"164":[[1,"128","2","Foreign Direct Investment Facilitation and Investment Law Reform","Fully mobilize foreign direct investments (FDI): Ensure the MFN (most favored nations) principles, national treatment principles and fully implement measures to ensure investment safety by issuing united Law on Enterprises and common Law on Investment.",""],[1,"128","3","Foreign Investment Attraction Measures","Develop and implement appropriate measures to attract investments from other countries, primarily the United States, China, Japan, the EU and Russia.",""],[1,"128","3","Policies to Attract Investment from International Corporations","Develop suitable policies and methods to attract investments from leading international corporations, making significant changes in quality, quantity and efficiency of foreign investments.",""],[1,"128","4","Foreign Investment Climate Reform","Improve investment environment to create more comparative advantages than other nations in the region and in the world to attract direct and indirect foreign investments.",""],[1,"128","5","Services Sector Liberalization for Foreign Investment","Gradually open the services sector to foreign investors as stipulated in Vietnam-US Bilateral Trade Agreement and during Vietnam economic integration into ASEAN, APEC and WTO.",""],[1,"128","7","Diaspora Investment Mobilization","Encourage Vietnamese overseas to make financial or intellectual investments in Vietnam.",""],[1,"132","1","Investment and Enterprise Law Implementation and Foreign Investment Liberalization","Implement the Law on Investment and the Law on Enterprises, gradually reduce and ultimately abolish all special regulations on foreign-invested enterprises.",""],[1,"132","5","Domestic and Foreign Investment Attraction Measures","strongly attract domestic and foreign investment sources, both direct and indirect, through the domestic financial market and the issuance of Government bonds on the international financial market.",""],[1,"134","3","Foreign Capital Policy and Capital Account Liberalization Framework","Complete policy and legal framework for foreign capital sources; define a suitable roadmap to liberalize capital flows in the context of integration into the world economy.",""],[1,"134","3","Diversification of Capital Sources and Foreign Investment Promotion","Diversify capital sources; expand the partnership relations on a multilateral scale in order to attract more foreign-invested capital sources and gradually extend investments abroad.",""]],"165":[[1,"128","3","Foreign Loan Administration and Settlement Procedures","Complete administrative procedures for granting and settling foreign loans to ensure national financial security.",""],[1,"128","3","Public and State-Owned Enterprise Foreign Investment Utilization","Effectively utilize foreign investments via the Government or State-owned enterprises.",""],[1,"132","5","National Development Finance Mobilization Measures","Continue strengthening the national financial potentials, mobilizing all financial sources for development investment.",""],[1,"132","5","Real Estate Market Development for Capital Mobilization","Promote capital mobilization by developing the real estate market.",""],[1,"132","5","Social Mobilization for Development Capital","Encourage and widely attract capital sources in the society by speeding up the social mobilization.",""],[1,"134","3","External Borrowing and Debt Repayment Management","Effectively manage external borrowing and repayment to ensure the national financial security.",""],[1,"134","3","Efficient Use of Foreign Loans by Government and State Enterprises","Effectively utilize foreign loans by the Government and State enterprises.",""]],"166":[[1,"131","13","Legal Safeguards for Property Search and Seizure","eliminate unsuitable and unnecessary legal regulations relating to the search of living and working places, confiscation or temporary seizure of citizens' property.",""]],"167":[[1,"132","8","Tax Policy Reform and Administration Modernization","Reform tax policies in the direction of lowering and stabilizing the tax rates, expanding types of taxable items and taxpayers, rationally regulating incomes and separating the social policy from the tax policy.",""],[1,"132","8","Income Source and Taxpayer Management Reform","Implement the tax administrative reform with a focus on managing income sources and taxpayers, paying attention to fostering and developing income sources.",""],[1,"132","8","Uniform Tax Policy and Tax Privilege Rationalization","Adopt uniform tax policies for all economic sectors; minimize the scope and rate of tax privileges; and implement time bound for tax privileges.",""],[1,"133","1","Tariff Relief Program","tariff relief program in conformation with the process of integration into the world economy.",""],[1,"133","1","Tax Collection Technology Renovation","Renovate the tax collection technology and enhance the collection performance.",""],[1,"133","1","Tax Administration Modernization and Tax Consultancy Services","Modernize taxation administration system and develop tax consultancy services.",""],[1,"133","1","New Tax Law Development and Issuance","Study and issue some new tax laws in accordance with the requirements of the market economic development and integration.",""],[1,"133","5","State Budget Revenue Structure Adjustment","Continue adjusting the structure of the State budget income sources along the line of increasing the percentage of income sources from domestic production and business, reducing that of those from import-export taxes, which are subject to impacts of foreign market factors.",""],[1,"133","6","Corporate Income Tax Subsidy Reduction Reform","Continue amending and modifying the Law on Enterprise Income Tax along the direction of reducing the forms of tax-based subsidization such as preferential tax and tax reduction/exemption.",""],[1,"133","6","Value Added Tax Uniform Rate Reform","Continue modifying the Law on Value Added Tax along the direction of applying one uniform tax rate for all domestic consumer goods and services.",""],[1,"133","7","Individual Income Tax Law Reform","Issue the Law on individual income tax to substitute the Ordinance on income tax for high income individuals in the direction of gradually unifying tax rates for Vietnamese and foreigners.",""],[1,"133","7","Tax Rate Reduction and Tax Base Expansion","Reduce tax rates in parallel with the expansion of tax collection scope (types of taxpayers).",""],[1,"133","7","Income Control and Tax Collection Efficiency Improvement","Enhance the income control methods and improve the tax collection efficiency.",""],[1,"133","7","Property Tax Law","Issue the Law on Property Tax imposed on purchases and ownership of real estates in order to guide people in using savings for production and business investment.",""],[1,"133","7","Natural Resource Tax Reform","Amend and supplement taxes on natural resources to encourage the efficient use of natural resources and rationally regulate revenues from natural resources.",""],[1,"138","6","Tax Law Reform for Stabilization and Simplification","Continue reforming the Tax Law along the line of stabilization and simplification, with consideration of international and regional economic regimes and regulations as well as other related international treaties.",""]],"168":[[1,"127","10","Public Service Delivery Reform","Transform administrative institutions into public services providers.",""],[1,"127","10","Expanded Public Participation in Service Activities","Increase public participation in service activities such as education, medical care, vocational training, social insurance, scientific research, etc.",""],[1,"127","10","Selective Public Budget Allocation Reform","In the future, it is likely that the Government will provide budget only to institutions responsible for politics and basic research for technology development.",""],[1,"135","8","Salary and Wage Policy Reform","The objective of the salary and wage policy in the upcoming time is to go against subsidy and privileges, reduce egalitarianism; implement the principles of distribution on the basis of labor and outcome of production activity of each organization and business; have separate salary and wage policies for administrative cadres and civil servants and public",""],[1,"136","1","Public Service Delivery Salary and Incentive Reform","employees working in public service delivery organizations based on financial autonomy; use of staff and payment to public service delivery organizations in order to develop public services; increase low and average salaries and wages, encouraging cadres, civil servants and public employees to improve professional skills; adopt reasonable treatment policy to scientists, talented art workers, scientific staff working in remote and isolated areas; ensure publicity and transparency in income, control and legalize salary-nature earnings so that salary will become the major source of income, sufficient to cover expenses of the public cadre, civil servant and the employee; establish a mechanism to use all financial resources in each organization, unit and budget level to pay salary to motivate cadres, civil servants and employees to improve labor productivity, quality and effectiveness of work.",""],[1,"136","2","Salary Reform and Payroll Resource Mechanism","Salary reform contents consist of the following: minimum salary; the relationship of minimum-average-maximum salary; the system of salary scale and scheme and fringe benefits; mechanism to ensure resources for salary payment; mechanism to manage the personnel, salaries and earnings.",""],[1,"136","3","Single Minimum Salary Policy Reform","Continue to study and implement the policy of a single minimum salary level for domestic and foreign business sectors.",""],[1,"136","3","Public Sector Salary and Earnings Reform","Deal with inappropriate practices in salary and earnings of cadres, civil servants and public employees in state agencies, political and socio-political organizations.",""],[1,"136","4","Salary Scale and Scheme Design Reform","This will serve as the basis to identify the highest- lowest salary levels in each field (elected, administrative, service, armed forces, business) to design salary scales and scheme of such fields.",""],[1,"136","5","Civil Service Salary and Allowance System Reform","The system of salary scales and schemes and fringe benefits are developed on the basis of existing salary scales and schemes with refinement to avoid overlapping and complexity in implementation.",""],[1,"136","5","Civil Servant Skills Development Incentives","Encourage civil servants to develop their qualifications and professional skills, complete the allowance system in each salary scale and scheme in each sector.",""],[1,"136","6","Public Service Salary Reform and Financing Measures","The salary reform proposal has been approved by the Government, on which basis about 50% of the additional budget revenue will be spent on project implementation; 10% of recurrent expenditure estimates of all organizations using the funds from the stage budget will be saved to pay for their own salaries.",""],[1,"136","6","Public Service Personnel and Salary Management Reform","The mechanism of management of personnel, salary and income in the public service delivery sector needs to be reformed to ensure resources for payment of salary; financial autonomy is to be linked with spending accounting in all service delivery organizations to cover part of their salary payments.",""],[1,"136","6","Socialization of Service Delivery Activities","Promote socialization of service delivery activities, reduce the pressure on increased expenditure on infrastructure investment and funding from the state budget.",""],[1,"136","7","Non-Salary Income Management and Legalization Mechanism","Implement measures and mechanisms to manage non-salary incomes by exercising financial autonomy and salary payment for organizations getting funding from the state budget, and legalize legitimate non-salary incomes in these organizations.",""],[1,"136","9","Salary Reform Roadmap","Continue salary reform roadmap up to 2007 as identified by the approved project",""]],"169":[[1,"138","1","Public Administration Legal Information and Compliance Support","Provide cadres and civil servants with adequate information of the state's policies and laws for application in the workplace with right authority and function.",""],[1,"138","1","Grassroots Democracy and Public Information Regulation","Implement the regulation of grassroots democracy and publicity of information for the people on the policies of the state and the local government; adopt regulations of periodical meetings and dialogues with key managers from central and local authorities to address issues raised by the people and the business.",""],[1,"138","1","Inspection, Checking, and Arbitration Strengthening","Bring into play inspection, checking and arbitration to ensure the effectiveness of state administration and social order.",""],[1,"138","1","Expanded Legal Aid and Consultation Services","Legal consultation service should be extended to the people, the poor, the people with meritorious contribution to the country and the ethnic minority people living in remote and isolated areas.",""],[1,"138","1","Legal Advice Support for Lawyers","Create conditions for lawyers to provide effective legal advice under the law.",""]],"170":[[1,"132","1","Trade Barrier and Market Access Reform for Priority Production Projects","Amend or supplement measures to deal with trade barriers and limitations on market access primarily to projects in production, manufacturing or those with high export values or high localization rate in substitution for import, and those to develop domestic material supplies.",""],[1,"138","3","Business Freedom Protection and Fair Competition Mechanism","Accomplish the mechanism for protecting free conduct of business; create a healthy and fair competition environment in accordance with published international commitments and roadmaps.",""],[1,"138","3","Implementation of the Law on Enterprises and the Law on Investment","Properly organize the implementation of the Law on Enterprises and the Law on Investment.",""],[1,"138","5","Trade and Services Law Reform","Perfect the law on trade and services corresponding to international practices and treaties in which Vietnam is a signatory or participant, creating a legal foundation for meeting the needs for trade liberalization, investment, services and protection of intellectual property rights Vietnam has committed to.",""],[1,"138","8","Natural Resources and Environment Law Enforcement and Sanctions Reform","Continue accomplishing the law on natural resources and environment based on principles of sustainable development",""],[1,"138","9","Trade Protection Legal and Institutional Framework","Grant priority to building necessary legal documents and institutions for protecting the economy in the process of integration into the world economy, such as most-favored nation treatment, national treatment, measures of self-protection, anti-dumping, anti-subsidization and antagonistic measures in the world trade.",""],[1,"139","1","Market Legal and Institutional Framework Development","Develop various types of market: complete a legal and institutional framework for the formation and effective operation of diverse types of market to ensure that all transactions and activities follow the market principles; concentrate on markets of goods and services, real estate, labor, finance, science and technology.",""],[1,"139","2","Competition Law Implementation and Monopoly Control","effectively organize the implementation of the Competition Law and monopoly control in close links with the market.",""],[1,"139","2","State Price Control Reform","Improve State control over prices in accordance with the market economy.",""],[1,"139","2","Trade and Investment Liberalization","Implement trade and investment liberalization in conformity with bilateral and multilateral commitments and international practices.",""]],"171":[[1,"139","3","Real Estate Market Reform and Regulation","Carry out policies to easily transform the land use rights into a kind of goods, making land really become development capital.",""],[1,"139","3","Real Estate Intermediary Services Development","Develop intermediary service activities on land (brokers, valuation, information, mortgage, guarantee, etc).",""],[1,"139","3","Real Estate Registration and Information System","Build a real estate registration and information system; issue the Law on real estates business and Law on real estates registration.",""],[1,"147","9","Urban Land Use Right and Housing Ownership Certification","By 2010, ensure families in urban areas to be granted the land use right certificates and ownership of houses built on legitimate land plots;",""]],"172":[[1,"139","3","Investment Facilitation for Housing and Infrastructure Construction","Facilitate domestic and foreign investments into the construction of houses, hotels, offices for lease, roads, bridges, ports, storages, etc.",""]],"173":[[1,"139","5","Skilled Labor Export Promotion","Promote labor exports in the direction of gradually increasing the percentage of technically-skilled exported laborers and experts.",""],[1,"139","5","State Management of Labor Export Activities","Strengthen the State's management towards labor export activities.",""]],"174":[[1,"140","3","State Management Apparatus Innovation","Continue innovation of the organization of State management apparatus:",""],[1,"140","4","Government Function Reorganization and State Management Reform","Clearly define the scope and content of the State's economic management; adjust the functions of the Government so that the Government, ministries and central branches can concentrate on policy-making and exercising their monitoring and supervision of the implementation of State plans, policies and legislation.",""],[1,"140","4","Government Restructuring and Administrative Streamlining","Restructure the Government by reducing the number of focal points; ministries perform their State management tasks by issuing policies, regulating professional standards and norms applied for the whole country; at the same time, check and inspect law implementation in the entire society related to the fields they are responsible for.",""],[1,"140","4","State Enterprise Ownership Function Separation","Eliminate the function of owner representative of ministries, city and provincial peoples' committees in State enterprises as soon as possible.",""],[1,"140","4","Separation of Public Administration and Public Service Management","Clearly separate State administrative management from the management of public services.",""],[1,"140","9","State Administrative Machinery Restructuring","Readjust the structure of agencies in the State administrative machinery at all levels in the direction of rapidly reducing the number of deputies, abolishing intermediate levels, changing services personnel from permanent registered staff into contractual ones, and decentralizing authority to the lowest levels possible together with closer inspection and checking by superiors.",""],[1,"140","10","Administrative Autonomy and Self-Responsibility Reform for Non-Productive Units","Intensify the sense of initiative, self-control and self-responsibility for operation, organization, personnel and finance in non-productive units.",""]],"175":[[1,"142","4","Enterprise Credit Non-Discrimination Reform","Abolish discrimination in the provision of credits by State commercial banks, ensuring self-control and self-responsibility of State commercial banks in their decision to provide loans or guarantees.",""],[1,"142","4","Business Dispute Settlement Simplification","Simplify procedures and minimize charges for enterprises in the settlement of economic and contractual disputes.",""],[1,"142","5","SME and Cooperative Support Policy Package","Create favorable conditions for small and medium-size enterprises, cooperatives, farms and models of enterprises of the private economic sector to fully and effectively develop through the issuance of new policies, enabling enterprises to have easier access to the State's incentive policies and assistance programs, especially the mobilization of investment capital and credits, renting land for business and production, accessing market information, using technical consultation and human resource development training, and access to business development services.",""],[1,"142","5","SME Financing and Credit Guarantee Measures","The State has established more funds for investment assistance and medium- and long-term loans for medium-and small-sized enterprises; established credit guarantee funds, expanded credit forms of financial lease, use of personal trust as a kind of collateral in granting loans, offered preferential taxes, tax reduction and exemption, funded scientific research programs and technological innovation in labor-intensive enterprises.",""],[1,"142","5","Enterprise Capacity and Competitiveness Support Programmes","Special attention should be paid to supporting programs to strengthen the capacity and competitiveness of enterprises.",""]],"176":[[1,"142","6","Open Land Use and Infrastructure Planning","Intensify the openness of land use planning, urban development planning, infrastructure development planning for people's life (housing, water supply, bus/train stations, roads, etc.) at localities so that all enterprises, regardless of the sector to which they belong, can decide their own development/investment options.",""],[1,"143","4","Spatial Planning and Infrastructure Coordination","Pay attention to spatial planning, technical infrastructure, construction, urban and rural residential planning.",""]],"177":[[1,"142","7","Economic Regulation and Planning Reform","Renovate the mode of State's economic regulation on the basis of fundamentally improve the planning work, and socio-economic development towards the direction of taking advantages of market positive impacts and in the context of international economic integration: vigorously innovate; improve the quality of forecasts, planning and plans in order to better satisfy the requirements of socio-economic guidance and management.",""],[1,"143","1","Inter-sectoral and Inter-regional Socio-economic Forecasting","Strengthen inter-sectoral and inter-regional forecasting in socio-economic development and integration.",""],[1,"143","1","Policy Impact Forecasting and Timely Adjustment Mechanism","Give emphasis on forecasting the impact of integration and socio- economic policies on the country's development to make timely adjustments policies to reflect the real situation.",""],[1,"143","1","Statistical and Economic Information Strengthening","Strengthen statistical work and economic information, attaching importance to consensus combined with direct surveys of different residential groups, regions, themes and public opinion on the state's policies to adopt appropriate adjustment measures.",""],[1,"143","1","Central, Sectoral, and Local Coordination for Socio-economic Forecasting","Strengthen coordination between economic, financial and general organizations at the central, sectoral and local level to produce sound assessment and forecasts about socio-economic growth.",""],[1,"143","2","Public and Consultative Master Planning Framework","For master planning: planning should have scientific bases, long-term vision, be widely commented and consulted, and its implementation should be supervised by the whole public.",""],[1,"143","2","Public Disclosure of Planning Documents","Except for some planning related to national defense and security, all other planning should be publicized.",""],[1,"143","3","Master Planning for Sectors, Regions, and Areas","Build master plans for each sector, region and area with quantitative development scenarios.",""],[1,"143","4","Market Forecasting and Socio-Economic Planning Research Improvement","Improve the quality of market forecasts and research in socio-economic planning projects, ensuring active and sustainable development.",""],[1,"143","4","Cross-Sector Development Conflict Prevention","Prevent overlapping development efforts and conflicts between sectors and territories.",""],[1,"143","4","Production and Business Development Planning Support","Plan the development of production and business; planning on core products is merely predictive and supportive to enterprises in building their own business strategies.",""],[1,"143","5","Planning Legal and Institutional Framework Reform","Quickly establish a legal and institutional framework for clear assignment and decentralization, creating standardization in planning processes and planning time frames for all types of plans as well as unity and coordination among plans.",""],[1,"143","5","Planning Governance Coordination and Responsibility Assignment","The Government unifies the State management in planning and clearly stipulates the responsibilities of ministries, branches and peoples' committees at provincial and district levels.",""],[1,"143","5","Planning Capacity-Building and Professional Development","Push up training, fostering and develop a contingent of responsible and well-qualified professionals to do planning tasks at all levels and sectors.",""],[1,"143","6","Planning Process Innovation and Legal Framework Reform","Continue innovating the plan contents (paying attention to sustainable development), plan-making methods, plan adoption and approval methods to make them effective management and guidance instruments, drawing the attention of investors and people.",""],[1,"143","6","Strengthening Five-Year and Annual Plan Specificity","Five-year and annual plans should improve their specificity in concretizing development strategies and master plans.",""],[1,"143","6","Plan Monitoring and Civil Society Participation Mechanism","Intensify measures of checking, supervising and organizing the plan performance, particularly the participation of people, communities and civil society in planning, implementation and monitoring from central to local levels.",""]],"178":[[1,"144","1","Administrative Procedure Reform and One-Stop Shop Modernization","Continue renovating administrative procedures in order to ensure legality, efficiency, transparency and fairness in solving administrative affairs.",""]],"179":[[1,"146","12","Vital Infrastructure Works Expansion Programme","Improve, upgrade, expand and build vital infrastructure works (small irrigational works, schools, communal health stations, roads, electric lighting, water for domestic use, markets, communal cultural post offices, meeting houses, etc), ensuring 100% of poor communes to have access to vital infrastructure works by 2010;",""]],"180":[[1,"147","2","Information and Culture Development and Ethnic Minority Cultural Preservation","Develop information, culture, improve people's spiritual life; preserve the cultures of ethnic minorities.",""],[1,"147","3","Expansion of Radio and Television Broadcasting in Ethnic Minority Languages","Increase the amount and transmission hours of radio, television programs, especially broadcasts in ethnic minority languages;",""],[1,"147","4","Ethnic Minority Cultural Preservation and Literacy Support","Improve people's intellectual life, preserve and bring into play traditional cultural values of ethnic minorities.",""]],"181":[[1,"147","5","Ethnic Minority Employment in State Agencies","Assist more people of ethnic minorities to work in State agencies;",""],[1,"147","6","Land Use Rights Granting for Ethnic Minority and Mountainous Communities","Ensure granting land use rights to communities, individuals in ethnic minority areas and mountainous areas.",""],[1,"147","6","Grassroots Service Expansion for Ethnic Minority Areas","Consolidate and expand health care services, cultural activities, and information provision to grass-roots units to serve ethnic minorities.",""]]}});